2 CONT
2 CONT ==Additional Data==
2 CONT will dated 1717 will proved 1718 Limerick, Ireland. Lived Limerick, Ireland. (whose will? cda)
2 CONT
2 CONT JUNE 10, 1663 PURCHASED LAND LYING AT WARIANOAKE RIVER AT WESTFIELD, MASS FROM THOMAS COWPER. HE WAS A AGENT OR TRADER BECAUSE HE LIVED IN HARTFORD, WINDSOR , WESTFIELD & BOSTON. Chosen fence viewer 12 Mar 1676, 5 Feb 1677, and 5 
2 CONC Mar 1678/9 for Westfield , Mass. 9 DEC 1686 HE & CAPT.THOMAS NOBLE WERE APPOINTED TO APPRAISE ALL THE BUILDINGS IN WINDSOR, CONN. . 25 Jan 1687 conveyed to sons Joseph & Benjamin the house and homestead of 21 acres.
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT George Sexton was born in 1632 in Limerick Ireland.  He married  Katherine Cowing on 10 Jun 1663 in Ireland.  George Sexton,  son of  James SEXTON of Limerick, Ireland (a descendant of Denis) and his wife Katherine and their famil
2 CONC y fled to North America, making them among the first Sextons to arrive in this country. 
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT George Sexton b. 1632 Limerick, Ireland d. 31 Oct 1689 Westfield, MA USA s/o: Christopher Sexton & Sarah Battely married: 1656 Limerick, Ireland to: Katherine Byrd b. 1636 Ireland d. 19 Sept 1689 Westfield,MA
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT George & Katherine, escaping religious percution fled Ireland, went to London, England before sailing in early 1663 to America ...arrived in Windsor, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Our family tradition has always had it that 1632 George was the son of James Sexton of Limerick. However, other information mentions a Christopher who I have always believed was James' older brother. I am very pleased that you ope
2 CONC ned up this heretofore closed door. Do you know what ship the family sailed on in 1663? I assume it departed from London. In a real irony of history, if George had waited another 18 months or so, the persecution you mention would 
2 CONC have ended with the accession of Charles II, and the ancestral lands in Limerick restored.
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Christopher Sexten b. ca 1584 Limerick, Ireland d. aft. 1640 " " s/o: Edward Sexten & Joane Gould m.: Sarah Battely - d/o: William Battely
2 CONT
2 CONT James b. ca 1604 d. Will: 14 Dec 1669 m.: Ellis ______
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard b. 1621 d. 3 May 1662 Windsor, CT. m.: 16 Apr 1646 Windsor, CT.- Sarah Cook ...Richard emigrated to Colonies (America) on 13 Jul 1635 from London, Eng. on ship named: The Blessing, settled in Windsor, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORGE B. CA 1632 D. 31 OCT 1689 M.: 1656 - KATHERINE BYRD
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT James Sexten - s/o: Christopher Sexten 1604-1669 wife: Ellis _____
2 CONT
2 CONT George b. ca 1632 d. 1717 IRELAND m.: Mary ( this George NEVER LEFT IRELAND )
2 CONT
2 CONT Joane b. ? d. 4 May 1636 of smallpox Symon b. 1634 d. ? Patrick b. 1636 d. will dated: 1742 Joseph b. 1638 d. 18 Jul 1715 m.: 15 Jul 1680- Hannah Cheesboro Stephen b. ? d. 29 May 1636 unmarried
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Dennis Sexten  Morris Sexten & Christian Nagle  Edmond Sexten & Katherine Arthur  Stephen Sexten & Alson (White) Comyn  Edmond Sexten & Joane Gould  Christopher Sexten & Sarah Battely
2 CONT ____________________ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmond Sexten: b. 1514 Limerick, Ireland was a Chief of Servants to King Henry VIII at the Royal Household in England and was granted the confiscated Abbey Houses of: St. Mary & St. Francis , in Limerick, Ireland with their hugh l
2 CONC ands.  Edmond also Mayor of Limerick, Ireland in 1535. Also was a Chief Sargent of the County of DUBLIN, IRELAND. He was also associated with St. John's of Dublin, Ireland
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT to Dr. Chris O'Mahony, director of the Limerick regional archives, Edmond's line died out on the male side after four generations. "You may be sure that you are not related to Edmond, mayor, knight, awardee of St. Mary's abbey lan
