2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Encyclopedia of Massachusetts, biographical--genealogical, (Volume 12), Author : American Historical Society
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 The history and genealogies of ancient Windsor, Connecticut: (Volume 2), Author : Stiles, Henry Reed, 1832-1909, Published in 1891
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 New England families, genealogical and memorial : a record of the achievements of her people in the making of commonwealths...,Published in 1913
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Joseph and Philena (Elton) Fellows, their ancestry and descendants : also the ancestry of Reuben Fairchild, John and Dorothy (Waldorf)...,Published in 1940
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the state of Massachusetts, (Volume 3) Author : Cutter, William Richard, 1847-1918, ed, Published in 1910
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Commemorative biographical record of Dutchess County, New York : containing biographical sketches of prominent and representative citizens, and of many..., Published in 1897
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Genealogical and family history of the state of Connecticut, a record of the achievements of her people in the making..., Author : Cutter, William Richard, 1847-1918, ed, Published in 1911
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Additional Data==
2 CONT Alternatively, Hannah died 19 Sep 1680 Westfield, Connecticut; only 10 days after son Charles, on 9 Sep 1680, though if she died at that early date, the mother of Nathaniel Sexton born 5 Dec 1682 in Westfield, CT is left unexplain
2 CONC ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT One family historian, V. O. Gehrke speculates George was born 1656 Limerick, Ireland and died at sea; possibly buried there. He was a sea captain trading with the West India Islands.
