1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note: Ancestors and Descendants of Jonathan Abell, pp 21-22:
2 CONT
2 CONT KITCHEREL FAMILY: Martha Kitcherel, who m.Lieut. Abel Wright, d.Oct. 19, 1709; dau. of Samuel Kitcherel. Samuel Kitcherel's wife m.Anothony Dorchester Jan. 1651, Samuel, probably son of Joseph Kitcherel, who on May 15, 1639, was g
2 CONC iven half acre of land at Winter Harbor, Salem, for fishing and was living at Charlestown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Colonial & Continental Anc, p 127:
2 CONT
2 CONT MARTHA2 KITCHEREL, 
2 CONT *married at Springfield, December 1, 1659, ABEL1 WRIGHT, who was born in or about 1631, and died at Springfield, October 29, 1725 (see WRIGHT). 
2 CONT *Martha was captured and scalped by the Indians July 26, 1708, at or near Springfield, and died October 19, 1708, at Springfield
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Pope: KITCHEREL FAMILY: Martha Kitcherel, who m.Lieut. Abel Wright, d.Oct. 19, 1709; dau. of Samuel Kitcherel. Samuel Kitcherel's wife m.Anothony Dorchester Jan. 1651, Samuel, probably son of Joseph Kitcherel, who on May 15,
2 CONC  1639, was given half acre of land at Winter Harbor, Salem, for fishing and was living at Charlestown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Event: Misc 26 JUL 1708 in Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: were subjected to an Indian attack in which Indians scalped Martha (who later died of her wounds), captured their son Henry's wife (Hannah Bliss, who also died soon after) and killed Henry and Hannah's infant son
2 CONT
