1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Goodell was born 16 August 1601 in Dennington, Suffolk, England and died 27 June 1682 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts. Children with Catherine Kilham:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.    Mary b: 1630 in Dennington, Suffolk, England.  Married John Pease
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mary Goodale
2 CONT * Birth:	Jan 5 1630 -  Dennington, Suffolk, England
2 CONT * Death:	Jan 5 1669 - Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Parents:	Robert Goodale, Catherine Killiam
2 CONT * Husband:	John Pease
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT MARY GOODELL was born about 1630 in England (age 4, 1634) and died 5 Jan 1668/69 in Salem MA (Torrey) (DRS). She married JOHN PEASE in 1653. John, the son of Robert and Marie (---) Pease, was probably born about 1633 in England an
2 CONC d died in 1693 in his 60th year. He married (2) ANN CUMMINS on 8 Dec 1669 Topsfield (Torrey) (Salem IGI, 8 Oct 1669, o.s.). Ann (Cummins) Pease died in 1689 (Torrey). John Pease was of Salem and Enfield MA. See Bowen #2.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of Robert Goodale and the 1st wife to John Pease. She was the mother of five children from John: John, Robert, Mary, Abraham and Jonathan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # Isaac Cummings, of Topsfield, Mass., and Some of His Descendants. Author: Topsfield Historical Society 1899
2 CONT # [http://photos.geni.com/p13/cf/57/d3/d0/5344483bde91b30d/three_mary_peases_original.pdf "Three Mary Peases of Salem, Massachusetts"] by Ian Watson.  TAG: 70 (1995) 205-208 Sources 
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=zsQWAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA164&ots=7DcMvgMWzB&dq=John%20goodale%201679&pg=PA164#v=onepage&q=John%20goodale%201679&f=false Daughters of the American Revolution Magazine,] Volume 20.  Page 164.  113. Good
2 CONC ale-thurston.  "Zachariah was a son of Robert Goodale, who embarked at Ipswich, England, with his wife Katherine in April, 1634, he in his 31st, and she in her 29th year. They brought with them three children, Mary, 4 years: Abram
2 CONC , 2 years, and Isaac, 6 months.—(Hist. Marlborough, Mass.. 1657-1861.) 
2 CONT
