1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/25612255/mary-parsons
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find A Grave contributor:
2 CONT
2 CONT wife of Mr. Christopher Parsons
2 CONT aged 80 years
2 CONT
2 CONT THERE HAVE BEEN SO MANY EDITS SENT FOR THIS ENTRY AND IT IS STILL NOT CORRECT. MORE CHANGES TO COME. HELP APPRECIATED. jf
2 CONT
2 CONT [This Mary Pease married Christopher Parsons who was born Dec 28, 1718 in Enfield and died Nov 20, 1789 in Enfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT [He was the son of Christopher Parsons; b. Jan 28, 1691 in Enfield; d. Dec 30, 1749 in Enfield and Mary Pease; b. Dec 19, 1695 in Enfield; d. Dec 30, 1774 in Enfield.
2 CONT Contributor: Rick Bart (47601455)]
2 CONT
2 CONT [To Help understand the 2 Christopher Parsons married to 2 Mary Peases', from Enfield CT, information from, "List of First Settlers of Enfield," with a few dates added for clarification by me:
2 CONT Benjamin Parsons born 15 September 1685 Springfield, Massachusetts Bay Colony and died 22 December 1728 in Springfield but was making preparations to move to and build in Enfield, Hartford Co., Connecticut Colony where he was on t
2 CONC he Proprietors Committee. He died in Springfield soon after the settlement of Enfield, and he had two sons who settled in Enfield, Benjamin, who died without children and Christopher Dudley Parsons born 1691 and died 10 September 
2 CONC 1749, who married Mary Pease, daughter of Robert Pease and Hannah Warriner. Christopher Dudley Parsons had a son (who was my direct ancestor-Joseph Parsons (1724-1776), who married Rebecca Allen (1724-1793), daughter of Azariah Al
2 CONC len and Martha Burt). Christopher also had a son Christopher (not my direct ancestor) who also married a Mary Pease -yes, two Christopher Parsons" married two Mary Peases' and hence a lot of confusion as to their respective lines.
2 CONC  Christopher Dudley Parsons' son Christopher Parsons was born 1718 and died 1789 in Enfield, Hartford Co., Connecticut Colony who married Mary Pease, the daughter of Samuel Pease (1686-1770) (who is my direct ancestor through thei
2 CONC r son Aaron Pease & wife Ann Geer). Samuel Pease was married to Elizabeth Warner (1683-1783).
2 CONT
2 CONT I Think this will help dispel much confusion I noticed on Find A Grave as to the 2 Christopher Parsons married to two Mary Pease if this information is added. These are my lines and I have researched them thoroughly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Respectfully submitted, Shirl Hering
2 CONT Contributor: Shirl Hering (48777241) ]
