1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Andrew Bartholomew Sr.=
2 CONT * BIRTH 11 Dec 1670 Roxbury, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 1755 (aged 84–85)
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown. Specifically: Lost to time 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 49471410  
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William and Mary (Johnson) Bartholomew, III who married of Hannah (Frisbie) Bartholomew in 1698.  Andrew Bartholomew Sr. managed his father's mills in Branford after his removal to Woodstock and after his father's death own
2 CONC ed and operated them in company with his brother Benjamin.  This partnership continued until 11 Jan., 1711-2 when they divided the properties; Andrew turning his attention principally to farming, purchasing large quantities of rea
2 CONC l estate in Branford, Wallingford and adjoining towns.  He removed to Wallingford between 1729 and continued there the remainder of his life.  He was a prominent man in Brandford and frequently called upon to sustain its trusts.  
2 CONC  They joined the Branford church, she in 1700 and he in 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT William Bartholomew 1640–1697
2 CONT Mary Johnson Bartholomew 1642–1705
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Hannah Frisbie Bartholomew 1681–1741 (m. 1698)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Isaac Bartholomew 1664–1727
2 CONT Abigail Bartholomew Paine 1672–1752
2 CONT Elizabeth Bartholomew Chamberlain 1675–1746
2 CONT Benjamin Bartholomew 1677–1748
2 CONT Joseph Bartholomew 1682–1724
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT William Bartholomew 1699–1734
2 CONT Samuel Bartholomew 1706–1795
2 CONT Daniel Bartholomew 1708–1777
2 CONT Rebecca Bartholomew Hall 1712–1798
