1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://archive.org/stream/newhavengenealog00jaco#page/n3/mode/2up  Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 60, 694, 1137 https://archive.org/stream/historyofnewhave01rock#page/n7/mode/2up  Histo
2 CONC ry of New Haven
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John, son of David Atwater, was born Nov. 1, 1654, and married (first) Sept. 13, 1682, Abigail Mansfield, born Feb. 7, 1664, died Sept. 24, 1717; (second) Nov. 27, 1718, Mary Beach. He settled in Wallington, Conn., upon a farm whi
2 CONC ch belonged to his brother Joshua. He was called "weaver." He died in 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Atwater was born on November 1, 1654, and died in 1748. He married Abigail Glover on September 13, 1682. His second wife was Mary Beach, widow of John Beach. Per Genealogical Register ..., he married Abigail Mansfield on the 
2 CONC above date and settled in Wallingford on a farm which had belonged to his brother Joshua. He had ten children: John (b. Aug. 17, 1683), Abigail, Mercy, Hannah, Joshua, Moses, Phineas, Caleb, Benjamin, and Ebenezer (b. Feb. 6, 1709
2 CONC ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Genealogy of Walter Gilbert"
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Atwater Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Learn about upgrading this memorial... Birth: 	Nov. 1, 1654 New Haven New Haven County Connecticut, USA Death: 	1748 Wallingford New Haven County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of David & Damaris (Sayre) Atwater, he married Abigail Mansfield on September 13, 1682 in New Haven. Among their descendants were Ward Atwater, a prominent sea captian in the West Indies trade, and Jeremiah Atwater, presid
2 CONC ent of Middlebury College, Vermont & later of the Dickinson College of Pennsylvania (Ref. "Gen. & Family History of the State of Conn.: A Record of the Achievements of Her People in the Making of a Commonwealth and the Founding of
2 CONC  a Nation, Vol. IV).
2 CONT
2 CONT He became a freeman of Wallingford in October of 1683. A weaver by trade, he settled on a farm that belonged to his brother, Joshua.
2 CONT
