1 NAME John /McGregory/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN McGregory
2 _MARNM McGregory
1 NAME Johannes MacGregorie/John MacGregorie
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 JAN 1687
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kingston
3 STAE New York
3 POST 12401
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1729
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He is most likely the son of Col./Major Patrick MacGregorie ( Died in 1691 ). Previously, he was listed as being born 1692 in Connecticut, however, I could not locate any sources confirming that date of birth nor t
2 CONC he birth location. In contrary, I did locate the birth/baptism record in the Dutch Church of Kingston for a Johannes MacGregorie son of Col. Patrick MacGregorie. Ultimately his name was John ( the Dutch form of John being Johannes
2 CONC  ). Additionally, I was able to locate a family descendant of John MacGregory here on Geni and verified that their haplogroup was the same/ common haplogroup for MacGregor's or Clan Gregor of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT I know Patrick or Peter MacGregory Jr. , his Mother Margaret, and heirs fought for the rights of land that belonged to Col. Patrick MacGregorie SR. after his death, so it does make me question why John would go to Connecticut. Per
2 CONC haps he wanted to move elsewhere for various reasons, such as work, new life opportunities etc. Maybe he didn't think they would get the land back in their family? These could be reasons amongst many other potential ones for John 
2 CONC to make a move.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lastly, he is listed as being one of the first settlers of  Somers, Tolland County, Connecticut around 1713 with a few other first settlers. I could not locate any other family members of the same surnames MacGregory/MacGregorie/M
2 CONC acGregor  in  the Enfield, Connecticut area either during the time of or prior to John MacGregory settling around that area. ( Leading me to believe he came from somewhere else prior to settling around this area in Connecticut, he
2 CONC nce aligning towards being the son of the Col. Patrick MacGregorie by coming from New York first before arriving in Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I have attached the link here for first settlers of Somers Connecticut down below that names John MacGregory.
2 CONT https://www.somersct.gov/about-somers/#:~:text=Settlement%20here%20in%20%E2%80%9CEast%20Enfield,Lord%20John%20Somers%20of%20England.
