1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=40152501 Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Nov. 11, 1850 Salt Lake City Salt Lake County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Nov. 2, 1910 Roosevelt Duchesne County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelbert Breed Searle, 52, two year resident of Roosevelt, died November 2, 1910 at Roosevelt, Utah. He was a son of Breed and Rebecca Saxton Searle and was born at Salt Lake City, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Jane Cloward in Provo, Utah, October 9, 1870 and moved to Payson where seven of their children were born. From Payson, they moved to Dry Fork, Uintah County, Utah, in 1885, where the balance of their family of thir
2 CONC teen children were born, ten of whom are living.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 15, 1890, Adelbert was made counselor to Bishop C. P. Bingham of Dry Fork and in 1900 his wife was called to be president of the Relief Society, of which organization she has been a member ever since she was a very you
2 CONC ng girl. This position she held for ten years, when the family removed to Cedarview, Utah where they proved up on a homestead. Here the family resided until 1914, when the ranch was sold and a home built for her in Roosevelt.
2 CONT
2 CONT -from obituary of Mary Cloward Searle
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT He married Mary Jane Cloward on Oct 15, 1890 at Manti, Utah and his occupation was a farmer. Interment was made in the Roosevelt Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *Breed Searle (1803 - 1879)
2 CONT *Rebecca Ann Saxton Searle (1809 - 1897)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *Mary Jane Cloward Searle (1853 - 1918)
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT View Utah death certificate
2 CONT
2 CONT BYU Idaho - www.abish.byui.edu/specialCollections/westernStates
2 CONT
