1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cook, Isaac, son of Samuel and Hope, '''b Jan. 10, 1681''';  [Note: The birthdate does not match the Barbour VRs. “p 91 - Isack, s. Sam[ue]ll, b. 10th, seventh, 1673/4 - Vol PR, p 15”]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Davis, Charles Henry Stanley. History of Wallingford, Conn: from its settlement in 1670 to the present time, including Meriden, which was one of its parishes until 1806, and Cheshire, which was incorporated in 1780. (Meriden,
2 CONC  Connecticut: C.H.S. Davis, 1870 (Wallingford, Conn. : Mount Tom Printing House, 1870)), Secondary quality. Vol 1, p 674 - [https://archive.org/details/historyofwalling00daviiala/page/674 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.  ISAAC.  ISAAC COOK, son of Samuel and Hope Cook, married Sarah Curtis, Oct. 11, 1705. He d. Feb. 1, 1712, in Wallingford. His widow married Caleb Lewis, in 1714. Estate £103.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *35 Sarah, b July 20, 1707 ;
2 CONT *36 Amos, d in childhood ;
2 CONT *37 Mindwell, b May, 1709, m Caleb Evarts of Guilford, Conn. ;
2 CONT *38 Isaac, b July 22, 1710.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Book of Gideon: Cook 4-6” pdf numbered page 352, pdf Page 6:
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 1st Marriage to Hope Parker:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Samuel, b March 3, 1667-8, in New Haven ;
2 CONT 2 John, b Dec. 3, 1669, in New Haven;
2 CONT 3 Hannah, b March 3,1671-2, in Wallingford ;
2 CONT 4 Isaac, b March 10, 1673, d April 7, 1673;
2 CONT 5 Mary, b April 23, 1675, m Nathaniel Ives, April 5, 1699;
2 CONT 6 Elizabeth, b August 22, 1677, d young;
2 CONT 7 Judith, b Feb. 29, 1679, m Jeremiah How jr., April 20, 1704, she d March 20, 1708 ;
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 '''Isaac, b Jan. 10, 1681;''' [Note: The birthdate does not match the Barbour VRs. “p 91 - Isack, s. Sam[ue]ll, b. 10th, seventh, 1673/4 - Vol PR, p 15.”
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Joseph, b Feb. 25, 1683 ;
2 CONT 10 Hope, b Sept. 27, 1686, m Joseph Benham, Dec. 18, 1706, she d Jan. 30, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 2nd marriage to Mary (unknown):
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Israel, b May 8, 1692 ;
2 CONT 12 Mabel, b June 30, 1694; [SIC: Mehitabel]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 3rd marriage to Mary Mallory, widow of Eli Roberts:
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Benjamin, b April 8, 1697, d 1717, unmarried, was a tanner and currier;
2 CONT 14 Ephraim, b April 19, 1699;
2 CONT 15 Elizabeth, b Sept. 10, 1701, m Adam Mott, Aug 28, 1717."
2 CONT See also https://sites.google.com/site/webstergriggsfamilies/williams/cook?t...
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd wife Mary Unknown:
2 CONT Ca 1691 when Samuel was 49, he second married Mary3, in Wallingford, CT.3,11 Born ca 1656.3 Mary died in Wallingford, CT, on 4 Sep 1695; she was 39.3,9 4 Dec 1695 per Wallingford records.
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 i. Israel (1692-)
2 CONT 23 ii. Mehitabel (1694-1732)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [cos1776 Note: No record of son Amos Cook in Barbour VRs.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Isaac_Cook_%2820%29
