2 CONT New Jersey Prerogative Cpourt I, Henry C. Kelsey, Register of the Prerogative Cortu of the STate of New Jersy, do hereby certify, that the forgoing is a true copy of the last will and testament of WIlliam Sascton, late of the Coun
2 CONC ty of Monmouthdeeased asthe same is taken from and compard with the original  now remaining on file [and of record crossed out]  in my office.  Witness my hand and seal of the Perogative COurt at Ftrenton, this Third day of April 
2 CONC A.D. 1878 Henry C. Kelsey, Register.
2 CONT
2 CONT To all Christain People, Greeting. Know Yee that I WIlliam Sascton of Upper Freehold in the COunty of Monmouth and Province of New Jersey yeoman being sick andweak of body ut of perfect mind and memory praised be almightGod theref
2 CONC ore   and being mindful to sebbell my temperall affairs do  make this my last will and testament. First and principally I recomend my SOul to allmighty God that gave it and my body to be deaseretly  beurried in the Ca__le at the d
2 CONC escressian ofmy Ecexutrix hearafterfter named and as touching  such  temperall estates as it hath pleased God to bestow upon me. I give bequeath and dispose of as followeth. Imprimis. I giveand bequeath to my loveing wife Anne Sas
2 CONC cton the sum of one hundred piund current money of America so longf asshe remains my widow but if she mary my will is that she shall leave  have an equall  shear with my children that is one twelfth part of my whole estate if ther
2 CONC e all live but if any of them die in the mynority then his  her ortheirpartor parts so dyingshall be equally divided amongest the survivors she to have an equsally shear with them I h_e_e I give and bequeath to my eldest son WIlli
2 CONC am Sascton five pounds currant money of Amarica over and above his eaqual share with the rest of my children and funde_ my will is that after my lands aresol as hereafter the remainder of my whole estate shall be divided eaqually 
2 CONC amongst my children to wit. William Sascton, Daniel Sascton, Peter Sascton, Charles Sascton and Janie  Sascton,  Sarah Sascton, AnneSascton, Charity Sascton, JemimaSascton, Elizabeth Sascton, Rebecah Sascton, and to epaidthem by m
2 CONC y escecutors and executrix at thetime here after appointed that is to say my three eldest daughters Sarah Sascton, AnneSascton, and Charity shall have each of them twenty pounds paid them within two years after my decease in curre
2 CONC nt money as  above and the remainding part of their share shall be paid them when all my lands are sold and the rest of my childre so many of  them as are attained totheage of one and twenty years at  the time when all my lands sh
2 CONC all be sold which is not to esceed term of tenn years from this date my will is that they shall have their partion immediately paid them out of the purchas money by my esceutors and theyoungar children that are not arrived to thei
2 CONC r age at the time of sale of the land  my will is that they shall have their portion paid them as they severally attain to there age of twenty one years. And lastly  I nominate and constitute and appoint my loving wife Anne Sascto
2 CONC n and my brother in law Samuel Shringuy togather with my son William Sascton and my fried John Steward escecutrix and escecutors of this of this my last will and testament and to them of their survivers of them I give full power a
2 CONC nd absolute authoirity to sell and  dispose of _iat farme  or plantation whereon I now live and all therest of my lands  and the same convey and confirm to any parson or parsons whtsoever as if the same had been actually done in m
2 CONC y lifetime by me one lans for they payment of my debts and leagacies above given out if my son William neglect or refuses to joyne with  the rest of my esecutors in the sale of my  then my will is that the survivors or survivor of
2 CONC  my esceutors shall sell all my land leaving the same power and for the _ou_es above said. In witness whereof I nave hereunto set my hand and seal this twelfth day of September one thousand seven hundres and tirty two. William Sas
2 CONC cton (his mark) Signed sealed published and declared to be his last will and testament in the presents of us. Thos. Shaw (M.D.), David Lippincott, Joshua Wright
2 CONT
2 CONT Be it remembered that on the Seventh day on Novemeber A.D. 1732 the last will & testament of William Sascton late of upper Freehold in the County of Monmouth of Province of N. Jersey yeoman dec. was duly proved before Samuel Bus_e
