1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT On 29 April 1680, James Sexton-244 married his firstwife, Hannah Fowler, the daughter of Ambrose and Jane (Alvord) Fowler. She was born on 20 December 1654 at Windsor, Connecticut, and died at Westfield on 20 March 1700 (another r
2 CONC eference states death occurred on 10 March 1701).
2 CONT CHILDREN by HANNAH FOWLER The Early History of Saxton-Sexton Family isthe reference for the birth years of the children. This resource doesnot list the birth of Catherine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Sexton born on 28 January 1680 at Westfield CT. * Hannah Sexton was born 29 October 1683 at Westfield. She married on 22 June 1710, John Harmon. She died 25 Dec 1757. * Phebe Sexton was born on 7 January 1686 at Westfield. 
2 CONC She married on3 November 1711, as his second wife, John Pyncheon. She died 17 Oct 1722. *Elizabeth Sexton was born on 5 February 1688 at Westfield; and died 7 May 1689. * Mary (or Mercy) Sexton was born on 26 December 1695 at West
2 CONC field. Intentions of her marriage to James Burt were published on 6 November 1725. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT <references />* <span id='Welles'></span>Welles, Edwin. ''[[Space:Births, Marriages,and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield, and Entered in the Early Land Records of the Colony of Connecticut|Births, Marriages, a
2 CONC nd Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield]]'' (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., 1898) [https://archive.org/stream/birthsmarriagesd00well_1#page/45/mode/1up Page 45]
2 CONT *"Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7WN-ZSS : 3 December 2014), Ambrous Fowler in entry for Hanna Fowler, 20 Dec 1654; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Saxton, Harold N. Early History of Saxton-Sexton Family. 
2 CONT *Saxton, Howard N., and James Saxton. “Some Descendants of George Sexton of Westfield, Massachusetts.” The Nebraska and Midwest Genealogical Record (Lincoln, NE: January, 1932) Vol. X/1, pgs. 3-5, 31. 
2 CONT *Ballantine, Rev. John. Journal of Rev. John Ballantine. New England Historical and Genealogical Record (Vol. VI) p. 265. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Connecticut Historical Society 
2 CONT *Papers and proceedings of the Connecticut Valley Historical Society, 1876-1903 (Springfield, MA: Connecticut Valley Historical Society, 1881-1914) Vol. 2, pp. 179-80. At Family History Library, Salt Lake City,UT: Call # 974 H2c v
2 CONC . 2. 
2 CONT *New England Historical and Genealogical Register. Vol. 6, p. 268; Vol. 11, p. 249; Vol. 39, p. 283; Vol. 61, pp. 139, 307, 308; Vol. 123/1 (1969) p. 260. At Family History Library, Salt Lake City, UT: The Library has vol. 1/1 (1 
2 CONC Jan. 1847) - vol. 161/643 (July 2007). Various film numberes. 
