1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SAMUEL KITCHEREL, variously recorded as Ketcherwell, Ketchering, Kecherell, Kritchwell, Ketchell, Cretchwell, etc., etc., was at Hartford, Connecticut, in 1644, when he was granted a house lot there. With him was h
2 CONC is wife, MARTHA, who, after Kitcherel's death in 1650, married Anthony Dorchester of Springfield, Massachusetts. This marriage took place January 2, 1651, and Martha and her three children by her first marriage removed to Springfi
2 CONC eld. She sold the Kitcherel. home lot in Hartford to Ozias Goodwin. She died December 17, 1662, and Dorchester died August 28, 1682 or 1683 
2 CONT
