1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I am not happy with the evidence that this Abel Morley is the father of the Thomas Morley.  Many (50 or so?) Internet entries affirm, so I am accepting it until someone puts forth a rebuttal.  I am leaving it in, b
2 CONC ut I do not entirely like it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abel Morley, born at Westfield 18 Jan. 1689, died at Feeding Hills, now in the town of Agawam, 17 Jan. 1771. He married at Glastonbury, Conn., 9 Apr. 1719, Susannah Kilborn, who died at Feeding Hills 16 Feb. 1782, daughter of John
2 CONC  and Susanna. He and his wife joined the Westfield Church, by letter from Glastonbury, 27 Dec. 1741, and they helped form the church at Feeding Hills in 1762.
