1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wright-4013
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca (Wright) Ordway (1692 - abt. 1745)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rebecca Ordway formerly Wright===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 7 Sep 1692 in Springfield, Hampden, Colony Of Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Abel Wright II and Rebecca (Terry) Wright
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Samuel Wright, Abel Wright III, Samuel Wright II, Ebenezer Wright, Mary Wright, Ephraim Wright Sr., Martha (Wright) Holbrook, Jemima (Wright) Hutchinson, Ann (Wright) Buell, Miriam (Wright) Owens, Benjamin Wright and Ben
2 CONC jamin Wright Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Jacob Ordway — married about 1711 in Lebanon, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Isaac Lyman — married about 1729 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Mary (Ordway) Gillett, Rebecca (Ordway) Hunt, Jemima (Ordway) Smalley, Rachel (Ordway) McCall, Daniel Ordway, Sarah Ordway and John Ordway
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1745 at about age 52 in Lebanon, New London, Colony Of Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 30 Jan 2022 | Created 23 Aug 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Wright-4013, the daughter of Abel Wright and Rebecca Terry, was born in Springfield, Hampden, MA 7 Sept 1692. She married first Jacob Ordway about 1711 and their first four children are recorded in Lebanon, CT. Three more 
2 CONC children were recorded in Windham, CT. As Rebecca Ordway, Rebecca Wright-4013 married Isaac Lyman about 1729 and had two more children recorded at Lebanon. Rebecca Wright-4013 Lyman died before 6 Aug 1745 when Isaac Lyman married 
2 CONC his fifth wife, Sarah Walcott, widow of Jonathan French.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Wright-4013 lost her first husband between 1725 and 1729. As Rebecca Ordway she married Isaac Lyman before the birth of her first Lyman child 10 Nov 1730. Therefore Rebecca Wright-4013 could not have married Benjamin Small
2 CONC ey and and died in 1726. Rebecca Wright Smalley had children in Lebanon during the same time Rebecca Wright-4013 Ordway had children in Windham. Rebecca Wright-4013 Ordway continued to have children after Rebecca Smalley died.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rebecca Ordway who was Rebecca Wright-4013 Ordway’s daughter could not be Isaac Lyman’s wife because she married Gideon Hunt 7 June 1732 Lebanon, CT in between the births of the two sons of Isaac and Rebecca Wright Ordway Lyma
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT SMALLEYS (Lebanon Vital Records)
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 240 Rebecca Wright m. Benjamin Smalley [no date] Original Lebanon VR, Vol. 1, p. 287
2 CONT p. 185 Rebecca Smalley d/o Benjamin and Rebecca b. 26 Jun 1726
2 CONT p. 185 Benjamin Smalley s/o Benjamin and Rebecca b. 25 Oct 1724
2 CONT p. 287 Rebecca Smalley w/o Benjamin d. 3 July 1726
2 CONT ORDWAYS (Lebanon Vital Records)
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 240 Rebecca Wright m. Jacob Ordway [no date] Original Lebanon VR, Vol. 1, p. 233
2 CONT p. 158 Mary d/o Jacob and Rebecca b. 16 Aug 1712 m. Ebenezer Gillett 23 Sep 1730
2 CONT p. 158 Rebecca d/o Jacob and Rebecca b. 16 Jan 1713/14 m. Gideon Hunt 7 Jun 1732
2 CONT p. 158 Jemima d/o Jacob and Rebecca b. 11 Dec 1715 m. Joseph Smalley 31 Oct 1734
2 CONT p. 158 Rachel d/o Jacob and Rebecca b. 28 Nov 1717
2 CONT p. 158 Mercy m. Moses Clark Jr. 6 June 1745 (birth record for Mercy not found)
2 CONT p. 158 Sarah m. Wigglesworth Law 12 Dec 1744
2 CONT p. 158 John m. Eunice Gillett 22 May 1748
2 CONT ORDWAYS (Windham Vital Records)
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 261 Daniel s/o Jacob and Rebeckah b. 3 Jun 1719/20
2 CONT p. 261 Sarah s/o Jacob and Rebeckah b. 5 Nov 1723
2 CONT p. 261 John s/o Jacob and Rebeckah b. 7 Dec 1725
2 CONT Rebecca Wright-4013 was the daughter of Abel Wright and Rebecca Terry. A bequest from her father may explain why her records appear in both Lebanon and Windham records. “But his greatest purchase was, May 30, 1717, of Rev. Samuel 
2 CONC Whiting, minister of Windham, of eight hundred and twenty-nine acres, partly in W. and partly in Lebanon, for 250 pounds, as the deed on record at Windham says. From these lands he afterwards deeds one hundred and for acres to his
2 CONC  daughter Rebecca and her husband Jacob Ordway, in 1718 and 1720…” [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT LYMANS (Lebanon Vital Records)
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 140 Isaac Lyman m. Rebecca Ordway [no date] Isaaac Lyman m. Sarah French 6 Aug 1745 Original Lebanon VR, Vol. 1, p. 175.
2 CONT p. 138 Benjamin s/o Isaac and Rebecca b. 30 Jan 1734/5
2 CONT p. 142 William s/o Isaac and Rebecca b. 10 Nov 1730
2 CONT [2]
2 CONT
