1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for MASSACHUSETTS with the rank of ADJUTANT.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A087320  DAR Ancestor #  A087320]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1739. Known as Captain Levi Pease. Service dates and locations unknown.<br/>
2 CONT At the commencement of the war, he resided in Blandford, MA.<br/>
2 CONT He and wife Hannah removed to Somers, CT and then Shrewsbury, MA about 1794.<br/>
2 CONT He outlived all his children. He died 28 Jan 1824, age 84.<br/>
2 CONT Widow Hannah died 14 Jun 1832, age 93. <br/>
2 CONT By trade, he was a blacksmith.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Ward's History of Shrewsbury, his children are:<br/>
2 CONT * Hannah, m. Thomas Henry Kemble of Boston, 1796
2 CONT * Levi, m. Mary Gill, settling in Northborough, died 20 Jun 1808 at age 40.
2 CONT * Lemuel, died 3 Sept 1816 in Shrewsbury, MA., aged 45.
2 CONT * Lorey or Loring, m. Rebecca Bruce of Northborough, MA on 18 Mar 1798, died Shrewsbury, MA 1811 at age 37.
2 CONT * Mary, m. Perry Chapin of Worcester, MA, in 1807 and died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Source: The Pease Family: Sixth Generation Continued. NEHGS 1847-1868<br/>
2 CONT Family of Nathaniel Pease & Miriam Pease.<br/>
