1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT from  EARLY HISTORICAL EVENTS IN THE DELAWARE VALLEY, by John T. Bradley ;    ( A series of historical articles of interest to everyone who resides in the Delaware section  of the county ).         COMING OF THE NOBLES   by John T
2 CONC . Bradley In the early days of Damascus village came Alvan Noble from a settlement in Connecticut. He pitched his tent along the pike on the flat near where the Eden bungalow is and started an upper leather tannery. In those times
2 CONC  it took a good seven years to make a pair of Sunday boots. Shoes were then the unknown quantity. How long Mr. Noble remained there we do not know but he migrated to the section now known as Calkin and pitched is tent in the wilde
2 CONC rness. He was the forbear of all the Nobles in that section. When in need of certain groceries he had to hike through the forest from his home to the pike crossing a fallen tree over the creek near the falls whence Fallsdale recei
2 CONC ved its name and hitting the pike at the home of Wheeler Mitchell, now the home of A.D.Bushnell. Then he had fairly good hiking to the stores in Damascus village. What he bought was toted home in a sack hung over his shoulder. Res
2 CONC iding then where James Smith now resides was James Monington and there our traveler always stopped for refreshments. A favorite dish in those days was mush and milk but Mr. Noble gave it the more euphonious name of "puddin" and th
2 CONC e hill soon took on the name of Puddin Hill which stuck to it even after a post office was established in 1878 with David Fortnam as postmaster. Just before the establishing of the post office and giving it the name of Tyler Hill,
2 CONC  it had been called Tylerville by some. The name Tyler Hill was in honor of Israel Tyler who was the nucleus of all business enterprises in the late years preceding its naming.
2 CONT
2 CONT A.J.Noble near C.B.Noble on 1872 Beers map
2 CONT
2 CONT 4/1/2003   From: jgmiller15@netzero.net  To: olsalte@aol.com I found your genealogy on mytrees.com while looking for new information about my ancesters. I thought you might like to know that Alva Noble was born in Massachusetts. H
2 CONC e died in Pennsylvannia and that he had 2 wives. Emeline was the daughter of Alva and Marie Buell. Here is what I have collected to this point. Much of what I have came from family records. Joyce Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT Alva Noble  (age 30) Removed  from Blandford Ma to, Damascus, Wayne, Pa in 1821 per WFT 35/0667 Alva was a Trapper/Taxidermist.  He married Marie Buel and settled in a log cabin in the Damascus Pa. area.  Part of they travels incl
2 CONC ude a trip down the Delaware River.  It was known in the area that he lived up to his name "Noble".  He was honest, hardworking and well respected. They had 11 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT dates per Garry Meyers Feb 2004 -      located at Damascus 1821 a tanner [8 children]  1834 moved to James E.K. farm, 1843 married Jane Sterling
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 census taken 21 jul 1870 lists: h/h 170 alvah noble  age 79  farmer  $3000/1000 born in MA jane  57  ny;  alvah j.  21 farmer  pa;  sophia  19  school teacher pa
2 CONT
2 CONT in the 1860 census alva noble  age 68 is living in the household of james? noble age 47 along with son alva noble jr. age 11...(no record of james noble age 47);   wife jane age 57 is apparently the second wife of alva noble...jan
2 CONC e baron...[maria buell noble having died in 1842]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 census lists in household 86: damascus Wayne pa alva noble  age 58  born in MA jane  age 37  b. in ny sexton  age 25  b. in pa alva  age 1  b. in pa martin stirling  14  ny phebe stirling  16  pa ann stirling  9  pa [the stir
2 CONC ling children are probably children of wife, jane baron, from a previous marriage...another stirling family lives next door...h/h 87..] note: same census shows two more noble children in household 85: william noble  age 26  b. in 
2 CONC pa  william cooley noble, son of alva and wife, eunice... unice noble  age  18  b. in pa
2 CONT
2 CONT 1840 census lists:   alva noble  0122101  1011001  alva's census age group: 40-50; alva's actual age c. 49...maria's census age group: 40-50; maria's actual age c. 44...
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830 census lists: alva noble 221001  0110  alva's census age group: 30-39; alva's actual age c. 39...oldest female census age group: 10-15?? where is wife, maria amelia buell?
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910  Census Sterling, Wayne, Pa  [who?] Adelaide M Noble 66  1844  single pa ct ct  1844
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 Census Sterling, Wayne, Pennsylvania [who?] A M Noble 79  1841 head pa ct ct single white female
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850  Census Mount Pleasant, Wayne, Pennsylvania Asa moon 55 VT farmer Laura 49 Oscar 8 Sarah M Noble 9 1841
2 CONT
