1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Turner was born 28 Oct 1683 in New London, Connecticut as the first child of Ezekiel Turner and Susannah Keeney. Her siblings included Lucretia, Sarah, Ruth, Mary, Lydia, Grace, Hannah, Susannah, Ezekiel, Eli
2 CONC zabeth and Abigail.
2 CONT
2 CONT When she was 17, she married Jonathan Calkins, son of David Calkins and Mary Bliss, on 11 Dec 1700 in of New London, New London, Connecticut. Jonathan Calkins was born on 09 Jan 1678/79 in Niantic, New London, Connecticut, as the 
2 CONC third child of David Calkins and Mary Bliss. He had seven siblings, namely: David, Ann, Peter, John, Mary, Joseph, and Lydia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Turner was the granddaughter of Mary Brewster granddaughter of Elder William Brewster of the Mayflower, daughter of Jonathan and Lucretia (Oldham) Brewster. Lucretia Turner, sister of Sarah, married Joseph, brother of Lt. Jo
2 CONC nathan Calkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Calkins and Sarah Turner had the following 6 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Calkins, b. 16 Sep 1701, d. after 1734
2 CONT Sarah (Calkins) Calkins, b. 7 Jul 1703, d. 03 Dec 1774; married Stephen Calkins
2 CONT Hannah Calkins, b. 20 Jul 1705, d. after 1725; married Richard Edgerton.
2 CONT Amos Calkins, b. 14 Oct 1708, d. 1775
2 CONT Grace (Calkins) Saxton, b. 23 Jun 1711, d. after 1731; married Ezekiel Saxton
2 CONT Thomas Calkins, b. 26 Jul 1713, d. 2 Jul 1750
2 CONT Sarah died on 15 Aug 1718 in New London, Connecticut, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Sarah's death when he was 40, Jonathan married Anne Pember on 08 Dec 1719 in New London, Connecticut, USA, daughter of Thomas Pember and Mehitable Agnes Way. Anne was baptized 2 April 1694 per "Baptisms," by Gurdon Saltonsta
2 CONC ll: 1694-1696, New London County, CT genWeb. Anne Pember was born on 15 May 1694 in New London, Connecticut, USA. Anne Pember was christened on 02 Apr 1694 in New London, New London, Connecticut, USA. No children were found for Jo
2 CONC nathan Caulkins and Anne Pember although they likely had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan died on 17 Jul 1750 in New London, Connecticut where he was buried in the Ancient Burying Ground.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per findagrave: Jonathan Calkins Birth: Jan. 9, 1678 Death: Jan. 17, 1750 Mary Bliss m. David Calkins 1672 New London, CT David Calkins 11/3/1642 Essex, MASS son of Hugh Calkins 1600-1690 & Ann Eaton 1605-1688 Hugh & Ann buried Ol
2 CONC d Norwichtown Cem. Mary & David had 8 children, perhaps more.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT No more info is currently available for Sarah Turner. Can you add to her biography?
2 CONT
