1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jonathan Calkins was born in July 9, 1678 and was baptized March 30, 1679 in New London, New London CT. He passed away in 1750. The son of Mary Bliss and David Calkins, m. 1672 New London, CT. David Calkins 11/3/16
2 CONC 42 Essex, MASS son of Hugh Calkins 1600-1690 and Ann Eaton 1605-1688 Hugh and Ann buried Old Norwichtown Cem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan was a Lieutenant in the French and Indian Wars. The Connecticut Colonial Records, Vol. 7, p. 94, show that by order of the Assembly, Session of May 11, 1727, he was appointed Lieutenant of Fourth Train-Band (or Company) o
2 CONC f Lebanon.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the age of 21, Jonathan Calkins m. Sarah Turner 1683-1718 daughter of Ezekial Turner & Susannah Keeney, on 11 Dec 1700 in New London, New London, Connecticut. Jonathan Calkins and Sarah Turner had the following 6 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Jonathan Calkins 16 Sep 1701-after 1734
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Sarah (Calkins) Calkins7 Jul 1703-3 Dec 1774 married Stephen Calkins
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Hannah Calkins 20 Jul 1705-after 1725 married Richard Edgerton
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Amos Calkins 14 Oct 1708-1775
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Grace (Calkins) Saxton 23 Jun 1711-after 1730 married Ezekiel Saxton
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Thomas Calkins 26 Jul 1713- 2 Jul 1750
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower connection through William Brewster as follows: William Brewster & Mary Love Wentworth Jonathan Brewster & Lucretia Oldham Mary Brewster & John Turner Ezekial Turner & Susannah Keeney Sarah Turner & Jonathan Calkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Above information supplied by FAG Member Sherry Hosford == JONATHAN CALKINS
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Calkins was born on 09 Jan 1678/79 in Niantic, New London, Connecticut, USA as the third child of David Calkins and Mary Bliss. He had seven siblings, namely: David, Ann, Peter, John, Mary, Joseph, and Lydia.
2 CONT
