1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [http://person.ancestry.com/tree/42722996/person/28685165579 Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 5 2017, 20:51:24 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=rthoden&id=I49
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Anne CUMMINGS Surname: Cummings Given Name: Anne Sex: F Birth: BEF 22 Feb 1634/1635 in Mistley, Essex Co, England Christening: 22 Feb 1634/1635 Death: 29 Jun 1689 in Enfield, , Hartford Co, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     According to letter I received from Bill Kingsbury 1958 SE Cates Circle,
2 CONT     Port St. Lucie, FL 34952 in October, 1992 (reviewing HIS ancestors) he states, MY Cummings line came to America with ISAAC in 1627 and settled in the Newbury, MA area. The Cummings trace back to the 4th century '''AD in Italy'
2 CONC ''. They went to England with William the Conqueror according to the Cummings Family Association.
2 CONT     Further the Isaac Cummings Family Association pages reads: Although Ann would have been rather young for a long voyage, Isaac probably left England in 1635 or early 1636 since he obtained land in Watertown in 1636 and probably
2 CONC  before. This fits well with Plummers' suggestion that Isaac may have in 1635 on the Great Hope of Ipswich, arriving in MA in August. Most probably the persecution of the Puritans at this time influenced his decision.
2 CONT
2 CONT     From: Cummings Genealogy - Isaac Cummings 1601-1677 of Ipswich in 1638 and some of his descendants, compiled and published by Albert Oren Cummins, Montpelier, VT, 1904., page 2:
2 CONT     Ann b. ______; married 10/8/1669 John PEASE of Salem (it being his 2nd
2 CONT     marriage), son of JOHN. He came in the Francis, from Ipswich, Suffolk Co,
2 CONT     England in 1634. He married (1) Mary ________ who died 1/4/1668. He died
2 CONT     7/8/1689. His wife Ann, died 6/29/1689. The moved to Enfield, CT in 1681.
2 CONT     Issue of marriage:
2 CONT     James Pease b 10/23/1670
2 CONT     Isaac Pease 7/15/1672
2 CONT     Abigail Pease b 10/15/1675; d 7/9/1689
2 CONT     He had John, Robert, Mary, Abraham and Jonathan by his first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT     From Cummings Memorial - Ann, born perhaps 1629, as she was said to be 60 years of age at her death Jun 29, 1689. She married 10/8/1669, John PEASE, his second marriage.
2 CONT     His father, John, came in ship Frances, from Ipswich, England. The son obtained a grant of land in 1681 in Springfield, MA; in town now known as Enfield, CT. He was surveyor and laid out the plan of that village. He died there
2 CONC  July 8, 1689. By his first wife, Mary, he had five children. She died 1/5/1668. (Pease Genealogy). By second marriage three children were born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Isaac CUMMINGS b: in Mistley, Essex, England c: 5 Apr 1601 in Easthrope, Essex, Engalnd Mother: Anne GREEN ? b: ABT 1605 in Mistley, Essex Co, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 John PEASE Senior b: 11 Feb 1631 in Great Baddow, , Essex Co., England c: 11 Feb 1631/1632 in St. Mary's Parish, Great Baddow, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married: 8 Oct 1669 in Enfield, Hartford, MA or Salem, Essex Co, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has Children James PEASE b: 23 Oct 1670 in Salem, Middlesex, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has Children Isaac PEASE deacon b: 15 Jul 1672 in Salem, , Essex Co, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has No Children Abigail PEASE b: 15 Oct 1675 in Salem, Middlesex, MA
