2 CONC se%26uidh%3dyd5&ssrc=&backlabel=ReturnRecord#?imageId=42521_b158316-00532 “Robert Pease”] in Great Migration, Vol 5, M-P, Page 419.  Ancestry.com. New England, The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, 1620-1635 [databas
2 CONC e on-line]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT November 1634: Sailed with his brother John on the ship Francis from Ipswich arrivinb at Boston late in 1634
2 CONT
2 CONT 1637, Salem: mentioned as having land in the early Salem Town Record. "Robert Pease and his Brother"
2 CONT
2 CONT 1643: Joined the church at Salem. At which time three of his children were baptized.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before his mother, his estate inventoried 3 Nov 1644 and the widow Marie appointed administrator. Widow Mare remarried Richard Haines of Beverly, MA taking the three other children with her.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Robert_Pease_%285%29 We Relate]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1607 (aged 27 on 30 Apr 1634), son of Robert Pease of Great Baddow, Essex. Came from Great Baddow, Essex, to Massachusetts Bay in 1634 on the "Francis" of Ipswich & settled in Salem. (On 30 Apr 1634, "Robert Pease," age
2 CONC d 27, was enrolled at Ipswich as a passenger for New England on the Francis. Died by 3 Jan 1644/5 (date of inventory). Married (1) by 1630, Lydia ____. (2) by about 1639, Mary ____. She married (2) by 1677 (& probably much earlier
2 CONC ) Richard Haynes. Robert Pease was brother of JOHN PEASE {1635, Salem}. Margaret (____) Pease , their mother, had arrived in Salem by an unknown date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bio by: [https://www.findagrave.com/user/profile/47062703 Linda Mac]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/68905222/robert-peas Find-A-Grave]
