1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography==
2 CONT She was not  the daughter of  https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-Kilham/6000000003897286868?through=6000000000421744475 b: 10 AUG 1558  & https://www.geni.com/people/Alice-Kilham/6000000003897339489?through=6000000000421744475 b: A
2 CONC BT 1560.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodale (1604-1682), progenitor of the Goodell/Goodale family in America, came from England with his wife and three children on the ship "Elizabeth" in 1634 and settled in Salem, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Elizabeth" left Ipswich, England on April 30, 1634 and landed at Boston in July. At that time, Robert Goodell was 30, his wife Katherine was 28, their daughter Mary 4 years old, their son Abraham was 2 and their baby, Isaac w
2 CONC as 6 months old. The first record of the Goodells in America indicated that they settled just north of Salem at Great Cove in the North Fields.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their 10 children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Mary b: 1630.  Married John Pease.
2 CONT # Abraham b: 1632.  Married Hannah Rhodes.
2 CONT #  Isaac  b: NOV 1633.  Married Patience Cook. 
2 CONT # Nehemiah b: 30 MAY 1636 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Hannah Haven.
2 CONT # Sarah  b: 1638 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  married John Batchelder.
2 CONT # Zachariah  b: 31 MAY 1640 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Elizabeth Beauchamp.
2 CONT # Jacob  b: 9 JAN 1642/43.  "Jacob Goodale d. in 1676, after being severely beaten by Giles Corey". Died without issue.
2 CONT # Charity  b: 1644 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts. Married Joh Abbe.
2 CONT # Hannah  b: 6 AUG 1645 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married Lot Kilham.
2 CONT # Elizabeth  b: ABT 1649 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married 1) John Smith.  2) Henry Bennett.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT 1st cousin of her husband?
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be '''Katherine'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth surname has also been reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/kilham Kilham]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/killiam Killiam]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/kilhern Kilhern]
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/surnames/killam Killam]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Disputed origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT See  Geni discussions: [https://www.geni.com/discussions/184256?msg=1233825 27 July 2018] & [https://www.geni.com/discussions/279683?msg=1703581 28 May 2024] 
2 CONT
2 CONT A christening report of 3/20/1606 Ropsley, Lincolnshire, England has been seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Common Errors to Avoid
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-338635
2 CONT
2 CONT Incorrect LNAB: Katherine, the first wife of the immigrant Robert Goodale, has in the past been incorrectly identified as Katherine Kilham, a daughter of Austin Kilham and Alice Gorball. [5] This is incorrect. Her maiden name has 
2 CONC not been discovered and her LNAB should be Unknown. A discussion of the error can be found in Anderson's Great Migration. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The error appears to have occurred because of a misinterpretation of the will of Elizabeth Goodale of Dennington, co. Suffolk of 1 March 1601/2. In it, she refers to "Henry Killam and Alice his wife my daughter." So there was cert
2 CONC ainly a connection between the Goodale and Kilham families, but the connection was not between Robert Goodale and a daughter of Austin Kilham. Also, the fact that a daughter of Robert Goodale ( Hannah) married a son of Austin Kilh
2 CONC am ( Lott) is another indication of the impossibility of the identification.
2 CONT Finally, Katherine couldn't be a daughter of Austin Kilham, because it is chronologically impossible. Austin Kilham married Alice Gorball on 8 September 1619. [6] Robert Goodale and his wife Katherine were married and having child
2 CONC ren by 1630.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References 
2 CONT * Anderson, Robert Charles. ''Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635'', Volume III, G–H. (Boston: NEHGS, 2003): pages 101-108. AmericanAncestors.org < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migration-imm
2 CONC igrants-to-new-england-1634-1635-volume-iii-g-h/image?pageName=101 link] > Page 107 ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206104918872 document attached])
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=zsQWAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA164&ots=7DcMvgMWzB&dq=John%20goodale%201679&pg=PA164#v=onepage&q=John%20goodale%201679&f=false ''Daughters of the American Revolution Magazine''], Volume 20.  Page 164.  113.
2 CONC  Goodale-thurston.  "Zachariah was a son of Robert Goodale, who embarked at Ipswich, England, with his wife '''Katherine''' in April, 1634, he in his 31st, and she in her 29th year. They brought with them three children, Mary, 4 y
2 CONC ears: Abram, 2 years, and Isaac, 6 months.—(Hist. Marlborough, Mass.. 1657-1861.) 
2 CONT * http://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/catherine-killiam_30374969
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=clcaldwell&id=I01025
2 CONT * http://www.usgennet.org/usa/vt/town/westminster/goodell.html Robert GOODELL married (1) KATHERINE KILHAM (or Catherine) about 1628/29 in England (b.of ch.). Katherine was born about 1606 (age 28, 1634) in England and is said to 
2 CONC have died in 1645 in Salem, Essex Co., MA.
2 CONT * https://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/New%20England%20Families/Goodale%20Family.html
2 CONT * http://www.wiggo.com/personal/genealogy/goodale_book/goodale_book.htm In the 9th year of the reign of King Charles, 1634, Robert Goodell3 and wife Katherine Kilham (daughter probably of Henry and Alice Goodale Kilham) sailed fro
2 CONC m the port of Ipswich, Suffolk County, England, on April 30 on the ship ‘Elizabeth,’ Capt. William Andrews, Master. With them were daughter Mary, 4, and sons Abraham, 2, and Isaac age one-half year.
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-338635
2 CONT *Anderson, Robert Charles. Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635, Volume III, G-H. (Boston:NEHGS, 2003):101-105, biography of Robert Goodale. AmericanAncestors.org < [http://tinyurl.com/jb9renk LINK] > ((paid)
2 CONT * Hotten, John Camden. ''The Original Lists of Persons of Quality...'' (London, 1874): page 280 and page 282. < [https://archive.org/details/originallistsofp00hottuoft/page/294/mode/2up Archive.Org] >  Robert Goodall (age 30) his 
2 CONC wife Katherine (age 28)  and three children sailed from the port of Ipswich, Suffolk County, England on the ship "Elizabeth" in 1634. 
