1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Goodell was born 16 August 1601 in Dennington, Suffolk, England and died 27 June 1682 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts. Children with Catherine Kilham:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.   Isaac  b: NOV 1633 in Dennington, Suffolk, England.  Married Patience Cook
2 CONT
2 CONT [Isaack Goodale married Patience (Cooke)  
2 CONT Marriage 25 Jan 1668
2 CONT Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT "Partner Trees: American Ancestors," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:3:MS44-BC5 : accessed 26 November 2023), entry for Patience Cooke; "User:jrpool49 Tree: John's Family Tree" file (2:3:2:MMMZ-TZ1), 
2 CONC submitted 29 March 2023 by johnpool1.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac was given a tract of land by his father, who also built them a house. (This house remained in the hands of descendants until 1915. In 1928 Dr. Robert L. Goodale and his wife of Ipswich, Mass. bought back the old house and mo
2 CONC ved it to their land in Ipswich and restored it to the original 17th century style. See "The Home of Isaac Goodale.") 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac was a farmer and died intestate in Salem before September 27, 1679. Wife Patience and brother-in-law John Pease were administrators of the estate, which was not settled for many years. In 1693 Isaac, Jr. replaced John Pease 
2 CONC as administrator. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=zsQWAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA164&ots=7DcMvgMWzB&dq=John%20goodale%201679&pg=PA164#v=onepage&q=John%20goodale%201679&f=false Daughters of the American Revolution Magazine,] Volume 20.  Page 164.  113. Good
