2 CONT ----
2 CONT Robert Goodell was born 16 August 1601 in Dennington, Suffolk, England and died 27 June 1682 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts. Children with Catherine Kilham:
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.  Elizabeth  b: ABT 1649 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts.  Married 1) John Smith.  2) Henry Bennett.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT  iv ELIZABETH GOODALE, b. say 1636; m. (1) by 1658 John Smith [ELR 1:39-40]; m. (2) Salem [blank] March 1674/5 Henry Bennett (this marriage record as published from the court copy gives the groom's name as "William," but in deeds 
2 CONC he is called "Henry," and these seem to be the more reliable records [ELR 6:66, 9:64]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married John Smith, had 5 children by him, then married William Bennett and had one daughter, Grace.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of her father's death in 1682 he names only his daughter Elizabeth Bennett (last name from her second marriage) and her son John Smith. (Her father had already provided for his other children via gifts during his lifet
2 CONC ime.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #  John Smith. He m. Ann Skerry, Feb. 6, 1689. He was a maltster (brewer) in Salem in 1692. 
2 CONT # Mary Smith. She m. Mark Haskell of Beverly, carpenter, March 20, 1677/8. 
2 CONT # Sarah Smith, b. Oct. 20, 1660; m. John Clark of Beverly, weaver. 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Smith, b. June 5, 1662; m. Humphrey Horrill of Beverly, Jan. 10, 1687/8. 
2 CONT # Abraham Smith. By deed and release from his brother and sisters he acquired the Goodale homestead, which had been left by his grandfather to his mother, and also the property deeded to her in 1678. He conveyed the estate to his 
2 CONC son Nathan in 1740. (Essex County Deeds 80: 75.) 
2 CONT # Grace Bennett, b. Feb. 1676; d. young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * The will of Robert Goodell of Salem, 1682, reads as follows:  "I, Robert Goodell being now aged & weake in body, as alsoe my wife and my daughter Elizabeth Bennett, hath taken care of me and therefore my will & desire is & I doe
2 CONC  will & bequeath unto my daughter Elizabeth Bennett & my grand child, John Smith, m y house & the orchard & all the meadowes that I now possess with the pasture which is about eight acres of upland be it more or lesse, all which h
2 CONC ouse, land & meadows my daughter Elizabeth Bennett, and my Grand child John Smith, shall enjoy after the lease, or terme, that it is now let for, is expired, they or either of them paying as much rent, yearly as the wife of the ab
2 CONC ovesaid Robert Goodell hath let it for which is to the value of twenty shillings in currant pay, dated the twelfth of October one thousand six hundred eighty two; & after my daughter Elizabeth's decease, the whole lands shall be m
2 CONC y grand child's John Smith. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seal.
2 CONT * From "The Ancestry of Lydia Harmon 1755-1836":  iv. ELIZABETH. She m. John Smith of Salem Village. It seems probable that after their marriage they lived with her father, Smith helping in the management of the farm. The evidence
2 CONC  in the case against him and his sister-in-law, the wife of Zachariah Goodale, in 1672, would seem to indicate that the marriage was not a particularly happy one. Smith d. before March, 1674/5, when Elizabeth m. William Bennett of
2 CONC  Salem. As her father states in his will, he and her stepmother lived with this daughter until his death. She was a widow in 1692, living with her son Abraham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * FamilySearch AFNs: 4JFN-56, BSFS-P8
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=clcaldwell&id=I00807
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gungazo&id=I03437
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [1]ELIZABETH GOODELL (Goodale) born about 1638 in Salem, Massachusetts (Bowen, 1646[2]). She married (1) JOHN SMITH about 1658. Their first child was born about 1660[3]. John died in 1672 (Torrey[4]).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born Salem, Massachusetts (North Fields):
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Smith born probably about 1658, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT John Smith, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Sarah (Smith) Clark, b. 1660, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Mary (Smith) Haskell, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT ELIZABETH, baptized 28 Aug., 1670.
2 CONT Elizabeth (Smith) Sturtevant b. aft. 1662, baptized 8 Aug., 1672.
2 CONT See the record for her husband John Smith regarding the court scandal with her sister-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Goodell deeded a portion of his Great Cove farm and the house on it to his son-in-law, John Smith in 1658. This seems to indicate that Elizabeth must have been married by 1658, since it is likely that this land was bequeath
2 CONC ed upon their marriage. From this it would seem that Elizabeth was probably born about 1638 and was the daughter of Robert and his first wife, Katherine. This is contrary to that which has been written in some previously published
2 CONC  genealogies which have said that Elizabeth was the daughter of Robert's second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married (2) WILLIAM BENNETT on 6 Mar 1673/4 (Torrey, 1675[4])[5]. They had one child, Grace Bennett, who died young. William probably died not long after, and before 1680. In 1680, Elizabeth was living with her father an
2 CONC d son, John Smith Jr. (probably born ca1660). See Bowen #10.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died some time after Dec 1692, when her son Abraham Smith agreed with his brothers and sisters to take care of his mother in return for her land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Elizabeth's husband John of Salem Village probably lived with her father and helped with the farm. Her father bequeath to her and her son John his house & orchard and "all the meddowes that I now possess".
2 CONT Robert Goodell deeded a portion of his Great Cove farm and the house on it to his son-in-law, John Smith in 1658. This seems to indicate that Elizabeth must have been married by 1658, since it is likely that this land was bequeath
2 CONC ed upon their marriage. From this it would seem that Elizabeth was probably born about 1638 and was the daughter of Robert and his first wife, Katherine. This is contrary to that which has been written in some previously published
2 CONC  genealogies which have said that Elizabeth was the daughter of Robert's second marriage.
2 CONT According to North America Family Histories 1500-2000 on 6 Dec 1692 Abraham Smith agreed with his brothers and sisters to take care of his mother Elizabeth Bennett during the remainder of her life in consideration of the land whic
2 CONC h she then possessed (Essex Deeds 9:67)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Goodale-13
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Elizabeth (Goodale) Bennett (1638 - aft. 1692)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Bennett formerly Goodale aka Smith, Goodell
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 11 Oct 1638 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Robert Goodale and Katherine (Unknown) Goodale
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Mary (Goodale) Pease, Abraham Goodale, Isaac Goodale, Nehemiah (Goodale) Goodell, Sarah (Goodale) Batchelder, Zachariah Goodale, Jacob Goodell and Hannah (Goodale) Kilham
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Smith — married 1657 in Essex, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Bennett — married 1674 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Mary Goodale (Smith) Haskell, John Smith, Sarah (Smith) Clark, Elizabeth (Smith) Sturtevant, Abraham Smith and Grace Bennett
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 1692 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colon
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 29 Sep 2020 | Created 14 Sep 2010
2 CONT
