1 OCCU Farmer
1 TITL Sergeant
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage: 15 Nov 1710 Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT James, second son of John Pease, Jr. and Margaret Adams, was born at Salem in 1679 and removed with his family to Enfield as an infant. He married Mary Abbe, Nov. 15, 1710 at Hartford, daughter of John Abbe, and settled in Somers.
2 CONC   He seems to have commenced operations in Somers by way of improvement as early as 1713, and is said to have spent his summers there, and his winters in their old settlement at Enfield until 1717. He was one of the first settlers
2 CONC , if not the first, of what is now Somers, and died there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Mary, born at Enfield, August 10, 1728
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. James, born at Enfield, 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Margaret, born at Enfield, 1715
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  Richard, born at Enfield, 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  Hannah, born at Enfield, 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  John, born at Enfield, 1725. d. July 25, 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Somers record)
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote: "It will be seen that some of the dates are subsequent to the removal of of Serg. James Pease ( as he was called)  to what is now Somers. Some of the births were at Somers, previous to the incorporation of the town, and 
2 CONC while it was all Enfield. There is a record of the death of his wife:  "Died, Mary Pease, wife of Serg. James Pease, Nov. 28, 1763."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT A genealogical and historical record of the descendants of John Pease, Sen., last of Enfield, Conn." Pages 11 & 12
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/83508490/james-pease
