2 CONT Married (1) in Enfield, January 30, 1745-6, THOMAS GEER, son of Shubael and Sarah (Abbe) Geer, born July 1, 1722; died 1751. Settled in East Windsor. See number 21.Married (2), November 15, 1752, SERGEANT NOAH PHELPS, born in Enfi
2 CONC eld, March 16, 1726, son of Israel and Rachel (Jones or Clark) Phelps. He was a farmer in Enfield and removed to East Windsor in 1774 or 1775, where he died. He served 40 days as a Sergeant in the Lexington Alarm, later enlisted i
2 CONC n Colonel Wolcott's Regiment, Captain Wells' Company, and is reported to have died in service.Children by first husband, Thomas Geer (mentioned in the will of their grandfather, 1758):170 Thomas Geer, jr., b. Oct. 5, 1746; m. Mary
2 CONC  Pease.171 Elihu Geer, b. May 3, 1749; m. Eleanor McClester.Children by second husband, Noah Phelps, born in Enfield:Noah Phelps, jr., b. May 6, 1753, was a lieutenant in the Revolution; d. at Valley Forge; not m.Hannah Phelps, b.
2 CONC  Sept. 9, 1755; settled in Westfield, Mass. Married Perkins and had a daughter, Hannah, b. about 1780, who m. Colonel Foote of Middlefield, Mass.. Daniel (1) Phelps, b. March 16, 1759; d. June 16, 1759.172 Abigail Phelps, b. July 
2 CONC 20, 1760; m. John Ward.173 Daniel (2) Phelps, b. Oct. 19, 1763; m. (1) Elizabeth Pelton; (2) Ruth Pelton.174 Obadiah Phelps, b. Feb. 24, 1767 ; m. Lucy Pelton.
