1 NAME Samuel /Warner/
2 GIVN Samuel
2 SURN Warner
2 _MARNM Warner
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 24 JAN 1688
2 PLAC Hadley, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 JUN 1755
2 PLAC Stafford, Tolland, Connecticut, United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Warner-Jr/6000000006727971945?through=6000000007574245501 who married https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Pease/6000000007574245501?through=6000000006727971945
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Warner was born on 24 January, 1688, at Hadley, Hampshire, Massachusetts. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was the second son of Nathaniel Warner and his wife, Johanna, to be given the first name of Samuel as he had an older brother, also named Samuel who was born on 15 January, 1687 (1686/7), and died the same day, at Hadley, H
2 CONC ampshire, Massachusetts. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of 12 First Settlers of Stafford, Connecticut in 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel married first Phebe Hutchison, and had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Phebe Warner who married Moses Brown/Bronson of Tolland, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Samuel married second Abigail Church and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Abigail b Aug 14 1724 [MAYBE: d. Monson, MA 11 Apr 1771 m. in Somers Ct, Jacob Kibbe Jr., although since she is not mentioned in the will, its probably that this Abigail was the daughter of Samuel's brother John). [Shows as wife
2 CONC  of Abner Chapin]
2 CONT # Joanna b 19 Jun 1726 m in Pomfret, CT Stephen Farnam
2 CONT # Mehitable b 19 Mar 1728 d in Bolton (Vernon) CT 16 Nov 1783. m in Coventry, CT Asahel Root
2 CONT # Experience b 4 Sep 1729 m Ebenezer Allis
2 CONT # Jemima (mentioned in will), no further information
2 CONT
2 CONT 3, Samuel married third Martha ________, his wife mentioned in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Last will and testament of Samuel Warner names wife Martha, daughter Phebe from first wife, daughter Joanna, grandson Samuel Root, granddaughter Naomi Allis, daughters Mehitable, Experience and Jemima, son Asel Root, [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel had two other brothers also born at Hadley, Hampshire, Massachusetts who removed to Stafford, CT: [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel, born 7 August, 1690;
2 CONT John
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel, born 16 April, 1696; [Removed to Springfield]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/genealogiesofhad00bolt/page/20/mode/2up page 21
2 CONT
2 CONT CHURCH 5. Samuel, s. of Samuel, (3) d. abt. 1737. M. (1) July 7, 1692, Abigail Harrison, who d. Sept. 7, 1717 ; m. (2) Aug. 12, 1720, Abigail Strong. She m. (2) Oct. 12, 1738, Ebenezer Chapin. Children — Samuel, d. April 28, 1703 
2 CONC ; Martha, b. Sept. 23, 1694, m. Jan. 5, 1715, John White ; '''Abigail, b. Dec. 25, 1696, m. May 7, 1723, Samuel Warner'''; child, b. and d. June 16, 1699 ; Richard, b. Sept. 20, 1700 ; Nathaniel, b. Feb. 7, 1704 ; Samuel, b. Aug. 
2 CONC 21, 1706 ; Experience, b. Feb. 2, 1710, m. June 14, 1733, Joseph Wright ; Joseph, b. Jan. 28, 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Samuel Warner (1688-1755)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Warner-1272 : accessed 27 January 2026).
2 CONT #Massachusetts Vital Records to 1850, (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001-2010), Hadley - V1, p. 76, http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/massachusetts-vital-records-to-18
2 CONC 50/image/?volumeId=14507&pageName=76&rId=264963111, accessed 19 July, 2015.
2 CONT # Estate No. 5680. Hartford County Probate Court. View on Ancestry. Image
2 CONT #The History of the Descendants of Elder John Strong, Volume 2, by Benjamin Woodbridge Dwight (page 955)
2 CONT # Radasch, Katharine W, and Arthur H. Radasch. ''Register of the Ancestors and Descendants of Samuel⁷ Warner of Wilbraham, Mass: With Descendants to the Seventh Generation of John² (william¹) Warner of Ipswich, Mass. Springfield, 
2 CONC Mass.: Samuel Warner Association'', 1956. Pages 21-22. https://archive.org/details/registerofancest00rada_0/page/20/mode/2up
