1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Phineas Pease enlisted 1775 at Norfolk, Connecticut as fifer in Capt. Isaac Bostwick's company, Col. Webb's regiment. In 1779 served in Capt. Relief Dutcher's company to repel the British on the Connecticut seacoas
2 CONC t at the burning of Norfolk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://books.google.com/books?id=7HgZAQAAIAAJ&pg=RA1-PA55&lpg=RA1-PA55&dq=Peletiah+McDonald+Dorcas+Stuart&source=bl&ots=NZK4C21m4W&sig=ICm9kcPAAnpv8FkqRH74Em7yu34&hl=en&sa=X&ei=bEv7U_O7DsiV8gHPi4GIBw&ved=0CD4Q6AEwBA#v=onep
2 CONC age&q=Peletiah%20McDonald%20Dorcas%20Stuart&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT American Revolutionary War Soldier
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas Pease (1755-1836) enlisted, 1775, at Norfolk, Connecticut, as a fifer in Captain Isaac Bostwick's company, Colonel Webb's regiment.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1779 served in Captain Relief Dutcher's company to repel the British on the Connecticut sea-coast at the burning of Norfolk, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1833 he was a pensioner of Berkshire County, Massachusetts, where he died. He was born in Enfield, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT in the 81 year of his age
