1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Mary Johnson Bartholomew=
2 CONT * BIRTH 10 Apr 1642 Roxbury, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BAPTIZED 24 April 1642 Roxbury, Suffolk Co., Massachusetts (the 2nd. month was Apr. for their calendar).
2 CONT * DEATH Jul 1705 (aged 63) Branford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Woodstock Hill Cemetery, Woodstock, Windham County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Latitude: 41.9492125, Longitude: -71.9733514
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  49522725 photos added by Caleb & Sally Davis, Informant: Jocelynn Bailey (48959328) 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Johnson Bartholomew father Capt. Isaac Johnson was born in 1617 in Herne, East County, England; and sailed to New England, settling in Roxbury, Massachusetts in 1630 with his father's family, probably in the company of Govern
2 CONC or Winthrop. Isaac Johnson was a freeman on March 4, 1685 (CD504 Early New England Settlers, 1600s-1800s in King Philip's War 1675-1677, Beginning of Hostilities in King Philip's War. Broderbund Software, Inc, Banner Blue Division
2 CONC ). Isaac was the son of John Johnson of Roxbury. John Johnson came to New England with the Wintrop Fleet in 1630(?). John was chosen by the General Court as Constable of Roxbury, Massachusetts, in 1630. John was born in Emgland, a
2 CONC nd married (1) Margery ? in England. John died in Roxbury, Massachusetts; on September 30, 1659. Captain Isaac Johnson married ELIZABETH PORTER. on January 20, 1636/37 in Roxbury, MA. Isaac died on December 19, 1675 in the Great S
2 CONC wamp Fight fight with the Narragansett Indians in South Kingstown, Rhode Island. Elizabeth died August 13, 1683 in Roxbury, Suffolk, MA.(Bowen, Clarence Wintrop, PhD. LL.D. The History of Woodstock Families (8 vols). Norwood, MA.:
2 CONC  Plimpton Press, 1962. Schultz, E.B. and M/J/ Tougias. King Phillip's War. Woodstock, VT.: Countryman Press, 262)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Isaac and Elizabeth (Porter) Johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Bartholomew ~ married December 17, 1663
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Capt. Isaac Johnson 1615–1675
2 CONT Elizabeth Porter Johnson 1610–1683
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT William Bartholomew 1640–1697 (m. 1663)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Elizabeth Johnson Bowen 1639–1702
2 CONT Isaac Johnson 1643–1720
2 CONT Nathaniel Johnson 1647–1698
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Isaac Bartholomew 1664–1727
2 CONT Andrew Bartholomew 1670–1755
2 CONT Abigail Bartholomew Paine 1672–1752
2 CONT Elizabeth Bartholomew Chamberlain 1675–1746
2 CONT Benjamin Bartholomew 1677–1748
2 CONT Joseph Bartholomew 1682–1724
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Descendant Details==
2 CONT 1. Elizabeth Johnson was born December 24, 1637 and married Henry Bowen, son of Griffith Bowen and Margaret Fleming, on December 20, 1658. Henry was born in Wales in 1633 and he died at the age of 90 years on March 13, 1723/4 in W
2 CONC oodstock, Connecticut. Henry was a lieutenant and he was in the Swamp Fight.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John Johnson was born on November 3/8, 1639 in Norfolk, Roxbury, MA. He married Elizabeth Maverisk on October 14, 1650 John died on December 16, 1661 in Roxbury, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mary Johnson was born April 24, 1642. She married William Bartholomew on December 17, 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Isaac Johnson was born on November 7, 1643 and baptized on January 7, 1644. Isaac married Mary Harris, the daughter of Daniel Harris, on October 26, 1669; and removed to Middletown, Connecticut. Isaac died February 3, 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Joseph Johnson was born on November 9, 1645; and was baptized on November 9, 1645 in Roxbury, MA. He died on February 3, 1729/20 in Middletown, Connecticut (FTM CD 367 - Notable British Families, 1600s-19oos, American Families 
2 CONC with British Ancestry).
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Nathaniel Johnson was born May 1, 1647 in Branford. Nathaniel married Mary Smith in 1667, and sometime after 1688 removed to Marlborough (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.angelfire.com/mi/RedBearsDream/Metcalfe.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49522725/mary-bartholomew
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of Captain Issac and Elizabeth (Porter) Johnson, and granddaughter of John Johnson who held the title of Surveyor of all ye Kings armies in America."  Both the grandfather and father represented Roxbury many 
2 CONC years in the General Court and held high, social rank.  Capt. Issac Johnson was killed 19 Dec., 1675, in the famous "Narragansett Fort Fight," leading his men over the bridge (a fallen tree) into the Indians fort. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in the spring of 1697.  Mrs. Mary was born 24 April, 1642, and was living, in 1705, in Brandford, Conn.
