1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Rebecca Frisbie Bartholomew=
2 CONT * BIRTH 14 Nov 1679 Branford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 18 Nov 1738 (aged 58) North Branford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA Alternate date
2 CONT * DEATH 18 May 1738 (aged 58) North Branford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Congregational Church Cemetery, North Branford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 139410933
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Frisbie was born on 14 November 1679 at Branford, New Haven, Connecticut. She was the daughter of John Frisbie and Ruth Bowers. She married Isaac Bartholomew in 1694 at Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts and  died on 18 May 1
2 CONC 738 at North Branford, New Haven, Connecticut, at age 58. She was buried at North Branford, Connecticut.  The estate of Rebecca was administered 4 July 1738.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is argued by some that Rebecca Frisbie was not the proven wife of Isaac Bartholomew. Jacobus makes this argument in "Families of Ancient New Haven" and sets this Rebecca's date of birth as between 1694 and 1712 making her the y
2 CONC oungest child in the family, and says she died without issue. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT An article in TAG 19:129-132 argues there that there is no proof who the wife was, only that her name was Rebecca and likely not the daughter of John Frisbie & Ruth (Bowers).  The Bartholomew Genealogy states that she was the only
2 CONC  Rebecca known to have been living in Branford who could have married Isaac and that her children were named for her brothers and sisters and that her brother was named their guardian after her husband's death and concludes: "Ever
2 CONC y other known fact agrees; still this may possibly be wrong."  The TAG article author suggests that another town may have been the birthplace of Isaac's wife. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT John Frisbie 1650–1693
2 CONT Ruth Bowers Frisbie 1657–1736
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Isaac Bartholomew 1664–1727 (m. 1694)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT John Frisbie II 1676–1736
2 CONT Edward Frisbie 1677–1741
2 CONT Hannah Frisbie Bartholomew 1681–1741
2 CONT Joseph Frisbie I 1688–1758
2 CONT Lydia Frisbie Rogers 1693–1751
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT William Bartholomew 1695–1765
2 CONT Rebeckah Bartholomew Collines 1702–1767
2 CONT Abraham Bartholomew 1708–1798
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT 1 Compiled by Hon. Ralph D. Smyth, "Edward Frisbie of Branford". 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/139410933/rebecca-bartholomew
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Additional Data==
2 CONT Rebecca married Isaac Bartholomew, son of William Bartholomew (1641-1697) and Mary Johnson (1642-1705) in 1694 in Branford, New Haven , CT. Rebecca was the daughter of John Frisbie (1650-1694) and Ruth Bowers (1657-1736).
