1 NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> CAPT.
2 CONT AGED 12 AT REVOL. WAR BREAKOUT HE STAYED HOME, KEPT THE FARM AND CAREDFOR HIS ELDERLY PARENTS WHILE ELDER BROS. SERVED IN THE MILITARY.  HEDID PAY FOR A MILITARY SUBSTITUTE FOR THE 7 YRS. OF THE WAR, AND LATERGAVE HIM A HOME FOR L
2 CONC IFE.  HE KEPT THE FAMILY FARM LIFELONG, ALSO ATRAVELER'S STOPOVER FACILITY ON THE MAIN ROUTE FROM BOSTON TO NYC.COMMANDED FOR OVER 30 YRS. A CRACK MILITIA CAVALRY TROOP NOTED AS THEBEST DISCIPLINED IN CT.  HE AND SIX SONS, ALL SIX
2 CONC  FOOT 200 POUNDERS,WERE AT ONE TIME MEMBERS. OF THE 6 SONS ONE WENT TO THE WEST INDIES,CAUGHT YELLOW FEVER. 5 OF THE 6 BROS. CARED FOR HIM AND 5 DIED OF THATSAME FEVER.
2 CONT REFN: 5
