1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Atwater Robinson BIRTH	31 Mar 1662 New Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	17 Oct 1746 (aged 84) Durham, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA BURIAL	 Old Durham Cemetery Durham, Middlesex County, Con
2 CONC necticut, USA Add to Map MEMORIAL ID	22080705 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Pictures added by Susan Czaja
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Atwater, dau. of David Atwater and Damaris Sayrer, b. of record Mar. 31, 1662 in New Haven, Conn. She d. Oct. 17, 1746 in Durham, Conn. (g.s.). 
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct. 22, 1688 of record in New Haven, Mary m. (1) Ichabod Stow, s. of Rev. Samuel Stow and Hope Fletcher, b. of record Feb. 20, 1652/3 in Middletown, Conn. where he died Jan. 25, 1694/5 (g.s.) Two known daughters were born of t
2 CONC he marriage in Middletown: Abigail on Jan. 25 (bp Jan. 29), 1692/3 who d. Oct. 19, 1700; Hope on Oct. 30 (bp Nov. 4), 1694, who would marry.
2 CONT
2 CONT On an unrecorded date and place before 1697, Mary m. (2) as his second wife, David Robinson, s. of Thomas and Mary Robinson of Guilford, CT. By this marriage were born four known children: Thomas, Mary, Ebenezer and Hannah. David 
2 CONC Robinson d. Jan. 1, 1747/8 in Durham, Conn. (g.s.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Edited 3/9/2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents	 David Atwater, 1615–1692	 Damaris Sayre Atwater, 1625–1691
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses	 Ichabod Stow, 1653–1695 (m. 1688)	 David Robinson, 1660–1748 (m. 1697)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Mercy (Mary) Atwater Austin, 1647–1683	 Damaris Atwater Punderson, 1649–1711	 David Atwater, 1651–1735 Joshua Atwater, 1652–1681 John Atwater, 1654–1748	 Jonathan Atwater, 1656–1726	 Samuel Atwater, 1664–1742	 Ebenezer At
2 CONC water, 1666–1702
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Abigail Stow, 1693–1700	 Hope Stow Hawley, 1694–1763	 Thomas Robinson, 1698–1774 Mary Robinson Parsons, 1700–1780	 Ebenezer Robinson, 1702–1789	 Hannah Robinson Miller, 1705–1796
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT Here lies ye Body of Mrs. Mary ye wife of Mr. David Robinfon died Octor ye 17th 1746 aged 83 Years
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on Mary's recorded date of birth (Mar. 31, 1662), on the day she died she was 84 years old, and Ætatis suæ (i.e., Æ, "Aged," in the XX year of her Age) 85, not 83 as inscribed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The most recent photo of her gravestone reflects digging below the ground to reveal the entire inscription.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/22080705/mary-robinson
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
