1 OCCU Major, Married Mercy Glover May 5 1664
1 TITL Major
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 60, 346, 660, 1137
2 CONT
2 CONT "Major; Judge"
2 CONT
2 CONT The town of Mansfield, Connecticut, settled in 1686, was originally called Ponde-Town, but was re-named after Major Moses Mansfield, who was an early settler and mayor of the town when it was incorporated in 1702. The Indian name 
2 CONC for the town was "Noubesetuck."
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Major in the King Phillip's War, which is the highest Military rank of the time, he defeated the Indians, near the town of Mansfield, which is named after him. He was a member of of the General Court of Assembly, Judge of
2 CONC  the Probate, and the County Court.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Richard Mansfield, he married Mercy, daughter of John Glover, on December 17, 1673. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Richard Mansfield (1611 - 1655)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Abigail Yale Mansfield (1660 - 1708)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #   Abigail Mansfield Atwater (1664 - 1717)*
2 CONT #   Mercy Mansfield Bradley (1667 - 1745)*
2 CONT #   Moses Mansfield (1674 - 1740)*
2 CONT #   Samuel Mansfield (1689 - 1705)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: HERE - LYETH - INTERRED THE - BODY - OF - MAJOR MOSES - MANSFIELD ASIST't AGED 67 DECEASED Ye 3d OF OCTOB ANNO - DOM 1703
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Grove Street Cemetery  New Haven New Haven County Connecticut, USA Plot: Buried in the New Haven Green - tombstone along the north wall. Tombstone is either missing or unreadable.
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Nareen, et al Record added: Mar 10, 2009  Find A Grave Memorial# 34670526
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses  Mansfield  was  born  in  1639,  the  same  year  that  his  father,  Richard  Mansfield,  came  from  Exeter,  Devonshire,  England  and  became  one  of  the  first  settlers  of  New  Haven, Connecticut.  Moses took the 
2 CONC freeman’s oath on May 1, 1660 at the age of 21.   On  May  5,  1664,  he  married  Mercy  Glover,  daughter  of  Henry  Glover,  an  early  settler  and prominent man.  Together they had nine children – five daughters and four son
2 CONC s. The family lived in the homestead formerly owned by Moses’ father at the corner of the present Elm and Church  streets  in  New  Haven.    Following  the  death  of  his  first  wife,  Moses  married  Abigail Yale, daughter of 
2 CONC Thomas and Mary Yale. They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.mansfieldct.gov/filestorage/1904/5800/major_moses_mansfield.pdf
