1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. Benjamin, was born at Stratford in 1672. In 1693  he married Elizabeth Andrews. She was born in 1674  and died' April 27th, 1732. She was daughter of  Samuel Andrews and Elizabeth (Peck) Andrews, of  New Haven,
2 CONC  who were married in 1661. Samuel  Andrews was born in England in 1632. He was a son  of William Andrews of Hampsworth, England, who  came to America in the ship ''James" in 1635. He  landed in Boston and was freeman there the sam
2 CONC e year.  Was at New Haven with Eaton and Rev. John Davenport. His first wife's name is not known; she was the mother of all his children. His second wife was Anna,  widow of William Gibbons, colonial secretary in 1657.  William An
2 CONC drews died in 1676 at East Haven. Samuel  Andrews took the oath of fidelity in 1654, and died in  1704. His wife, Elizabeth Peck, was daughter of  Deacon William Peck of New Haven, who was born  in London, England in 1601 and was 
2 CONC a merchant there.  He was a representative to the General Assembly in  New Haven in 1646. He held many positions of trust  and was an influential citizen of New Haven. Dr.  Benjamin Hull was a prominent physician in Wallingford, a
2 CONC nd died there March 3rd, 1741. His wife died  1732. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Hull Family in America:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/charles-h-weygant/the-hull-family-in-america-gye/page-38-the-hull-family-in-america-gye.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT 20. Dr. Benjamin Hull, 1672-1741, of Stratford and Wallingford, Conn., son of (3) Dr. John and Mary Jones Hull, was married in 1693 to Elizabeth Andrews, 1674-1732, daughter of Samuel Andrews and his wife Elizabeth Peck. Both the 
2 CONC Andrews and Peck families hold prominent places in the early history of New England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *84. Andrew Hull, b. Aug. 17, 1694; d. 1717. 
2 CONT *85. Mary Hull, b. Aug. 31, 1696; m. Eben Bronson. 
2 CONT *86. Elizabeth Hull, b. Apr. 8, 1698; m. 1723, Nathaniel Merriman 
2 CONT *87. Damaris Hull, b. Feb. 4, 1700; d. 1787; m. 1722, Elnathan Street 
2 CONT *88. Abigail Hull, b. 1702; m. 1719, Ensign E. Merriman. 
2 CONT *89. Dr. John Hull, b. Nov. 13, 1704; d. May 22, 1762; m. 1727, Sarah Ives. 
2 CONT *90. Samuel Hull, b. 1706; d. 1789; m. 1733, Sarah Hall. 
2 CONT *91. Sarah Hull, b. Mar. 30, 1710; m. 1733, Samuel Hall. 
2 CONT *92. Benjamin Hull, b. July 6, 1712; m. 1735, Hannah Parmelee. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT #20. DR. BENJAMIN HULL, 1672-1741, of Stratford and Wallingford, Conn., son of (3) Dr. John and Mary Jones Hull, was married in 1693 to Elizabeth Andrews, 1674-1732, daughter of Samuel Andrews and his wife Elizabeth Peck. [Mrs. El
2 CONC izabeth Hulls d 1732 Apr 27 LR5 528; Benjamin d 1741 Mar 30 LR5 549]
2 CONT
2 CONT children: see http://genforum.genealogy.com/hull/messages/2891.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT 84. Andrew Hull, b. Aug. 17, 1694; d. 1717. [1694 Aug.17 LR1 158] 85. Mary Hull, b. Aug. 31, 1696; m. Eben Bronson. [1696 Aug 31 LR 1 159] 86. Elizabeth Hull, b. Apr. 8, 1698; m. 1723, Nathaniel Merriman. [“Eleasebeth” 1698 Apr 8 
2 CONC LR1 53; died 1698 Apr 7 LR 695 – it appeared the days in question are reversed but I wrote it as it appeared in the vital records. The data on death puts marriage in question and maybe belonged to “child born” above.] 87. Damaris 
2 CONC Hull, b. Feb. 4, 1700; d. 1787; m. 1722, Elnathan Street. [“Dammarrus” 170- Feb 3 LR2 795] 88. Abigail Hull, b. 1702; m. 1719, Ensign E. Merriman. [1704 Feb 14 LR2 795] 89. Dr. John Hull, b. Nov. 13, 1704; d. May 22, 1762; m. 1727
2 CONC , Sarah Ives. [see above or 1702 Oct 6 LR2 795; marriage – 1727 June 21 by Capt. Yale to John Hulls LR5 510]] 90. Samuel Hull, b. 1706; d. 1789; m. 1733, Sarah Hall. [1707 Sep 1 LR2 795] 91. Sarah Hull, b. Mar. 30, 1710; m. 1733, 
2 CONC Samuel Hall. [1710 Mar 30 LR2 795] 92. Benjamin Hull, b. July 6, 1712; m. 1735, Hannah Parmelee [“Benjamine”1712 Jul 6 LR2 796; marriage – 1733 Jan 22 by Mr. Whitting LR5 509; a child named Benjamin b 1741 Oct 20 LR8 533]
2 CONT
2 CONT source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/hull/messages/2891.html
2 CONT
