1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=33942938&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	May 16, 1665 New Haven New Haven County Connecticut, USA Death: 	Jul. 9, 1703 Wallingford New Haven County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of  ancestors, NATHANIEL & JOAN LINES MERRIMAN, he married Mary Preston on July 9, 1690 in Wallingford, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT His estate was valued at 439 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children: Moses Merriman b. Oct. 30, 1691 Elizabeth Merriman b. May 4, 1693 Eliasaph Merriman b. May 21, 1695 Phebe Merriman b. June 17, 1697 Hanna Merriman b. Sept. 10, 1698 Phebe Merriman b. Sept. 16, 1699 Lydia Merriman b
2 CONC . Dec. 31, 1701 Lydia Merriman b. Nov. 12, 1702
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Nathaniel Merriman (1613 - 1694)
2 CONT   Joan Lines Merriman (1628 - 1709)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Mary Preston Merriman (1674 - 1755)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Eliasaph Merriman (1695 - 1758)*
2 CONT   Phebe Merriman Munson (1699 - 1772)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Center Street Cemetery  Wallingford New Haven County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Nareen, et al Record added: Feb 17, 2009  Find A Grave Memorial# 33942938
2 CONT
2 CONT CALEB MERRIMAN [304g] (New Haven, May 1663/6-Wallingford, Conn., July 19, 1703) married Mary Peston [304gm] (Stratford, Conn., April 18, 1674-Wallingford, Nov. 28, 1755) daughter of Deacon El??ph and Mary (Wilcoxen) Preston and ma
2 CONC rried 2nd, Samuel Munson, seven children: (Gen. 8) Moses Merriman [304ga] (b. Oct. 31, 1691); Elizabeth Merriman [304gb] (b. May 4, 1693) married Nov. 7, 1712, Henry Turhand [304g??n] married 2nd, Joseph Royce [304ghmm]; Eliasaph 
2 CONC Merriman [304g??] (May 21, 1695-Aug. 14, 1758) married Dec. 10, 1719, Abigail Hall [304gcm] (killed by lightning, Aug. 4, 1758) eleven children; Hannah Merriman [304gd] (Sept. 10, 1697-Sept. 28, 1738) married Wallingford, July 19,
2 CONC  1714, John Andrews [304gdm]; Phebe Merriman [304ge] (Sept. 11, 1699-Dec. 1772) married Dec. 10, 1719. Waltstill Munson [304gem]; Lydia Merriman [304gf] (Sept. 8, 1701--d. young); and Lydia Merriman, again [304gg] (Nov. 12, 1702-a
2 CONC ft. 1777) married Ephraim Cook [304ggm]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: New Haven, Connecticut]] [[Category:Wallingford, Connecticut]]
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT === Birth ===Caleb Merriman, son of Nathaniel and Joan, was born May 1665, in New Haven, Connecticut.<ref name="Jacobus">Jacobus, Donald Lines (compiler). ''Families of Ancient New Haven, Vol I-VIII. and Index Vol IX'' New Haven: 
2 CONC 1931. Reprint, Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1974, 1981, 1997. Originally published as New Haven Genealogical Magazine, Volumes I-VIII. Rome, NY and New Haven, CT 1922-1932. p. 1168</ref><ref name="NHV"> [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/details/vitalrecordsofne01orde Vital Records of New Haven 1649-1850 Part I.] Hartford: The ConnecticutSociety of the Order of the Founders and Patriots of America, 1917 p.22</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Christening ===He was baptized at the First Congregational Society of New Haven on 25June 1665, by the Rev. John Davenport<ref> Connecticut Church RecordsIndex: New Haven First Congregational Church 1639-1937. Vol. J-Z. Hartfo
2 CONC rd: Connecticut State Library, 1947.</ref><ref>"Baptisms in the Church  in New Haven, Conn. during the Ministry of Rev. John Davenport" New England Historical and Genealogical Register 9:361 (1855) [https://archive.org/stream/newe
2 CONC nglandhistor1855wate#page/725/mode/2up p. 361]</ref>  
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===Calab Merriman married [[Preston-46|Mary Preston]] 9 July 1690 in Wallingford.<ref name=WallingfordVR >Connecticut Vital Records to 1850 "Wallingford" (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic G
2 CONC enealogical Society, 2011.) From original typescripts, Lucius Barnes Barbour Collection, 1928. p. 220</ref> Mr. Thomas Yale performed the ceremony on that date.<ref>"Wallingford Vital Records 1671-1706." The American Genealogist V
2 CONC ol 14 p. 29</ref>  She outlived him and married 2nd Samuel Munson<ref name="Jacobus" />
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===Corporal Caleb Merriman died 19 July 1703, in Wallingford.<ref name="Jacobus" /><ref name=WallingfordVR />
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT The children of Caleb and Mary were born in Wallingford.# [[Merriman-127|Moses Merriman]] Moses was born 31 October 1691<ref name=WallingfordVR /># [[Merriman-256|Elizabeth]] was born 4 May 1693<ref name=WallingfordVR /># [[Merrim
2 CONC an-300|Elliasaph]] was born 20 May 1695<ref name=WallingfordVR /># [[Merriman-303|Hannah]] was born 10 September 1697<ref name=WallingfordVR /># [[Merriman-28|Phebe]] was born 11 September 1699<ref name=WallingfordVR /># Lydia was
2 CONC  born 8 September 1701 and died soon.<ref name="Jacobus"><ref> This record was mostly illegible by the time the Barbour Collection was created.</ref># [[Merriman-4|Lydia]] was born 12 November 1702<ref name=WallingfordVR />
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />Merriman, Mansfield. ''[[Space:Reunion of Descendants of Nathaniel Merriman at Wallingford, Conn., June 4, 1913|Reunion of Descendants of Nathaniel Merriman at Wallingford, Conn., June 4, 1913]]'' (Donald L. Jacobus,
2 CONC  New Haven, Conn., 1914) [https://archive.org/stream/reunionofdescend00merr#page/144/mode/1up p. 144/5]</ref>
2 CONT
