2 CONC arnah an. The Wetmore family of America and its Collateral Branch es. Albany,New York:Munsell and Rowland, 1861.<br>ELIZABETH, b. --, 1648; m. Oct. 8, 1673, Josiah son of Will iam Adkins,<br>of East Hartford; removed to Middletown
2 CONC ; had I Sarah,<br>July 16, 1674, d. Feb. 25, 1719; II Abigail, b. Sept. 11, 1 676,<br>m. Robert Hubbard 1703; III Solomon, b. July 25, 1678;<br>IV Josiah, b. March 9, 1680; V Benjamin, b. Nov. 19, 1682;<br>VI Ephraim, b. March 9, 
2 CONC 1685; VII Elizabeth, b. Aug. 11,<br>1687, m. Samuel Ward, 1711.<br>Josiah Adkins1 Sen. d. Sept. 12, 1690; will dated March 1 , 1690; inventory, by John Hall Sen., Nathaniel Stow, and S amuel Stow, Jan. 1, 1691. Their son Solomon w
2 CONC as elected dea con of the First congregational society of M., Jan. 8, 1735 ; d. Oct. 5, 1748, aged 70. William Adkins came from Wales.
