1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children with Peter McGregorie:
2 CONT *1. Hugh, 
2 CONT *2. Catherine (married John Evans), 
2 CONT *3. Patrick, Jr., 
2 CONT *4. Jane (married man named Lawrence) and 
2 CONT *5. John (b. 1687 Kingston, NY)
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Patrick Mc Gregorie was killed in the Leisler affair in 1691, at which time Margaret was driven from her home in Quassaick by her heartless, land hungry son-in-law Col. John Evans, and she went to live in New York City, where
2 CONC  she appears on tax lists until 1699, living near a Lawrence family, presumably that of another daughter's husband. Tax lists- South Ward of NY "New York Tax Lists Vol I, 1695-1699 " Thomas Lowrense Mrs. Magregory 
2 CONT
2 CONT She then disappears from New York City and a Margaret is seen as ye goodwife of William Sutherland in Quassaick. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret petitioned for restoration of the title of her first husband's land in 1710, and Patrick, Jr., was granted 160 acres, 9 Aug., 1720, beginning at southeast corner of land of William Sutherland.  Patrick, Jr. deeded it to h
2 CONC is daughter Mary and her husband David Sutherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with William Sutherland I:
2 CONT *1. David ,Sr (1697-1776)
2 CONT *2. William (1698-1772)
2 CONT *3. Alexander (1700-1777)
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:
2 CONT *Andrew Toshack 
2 CONT *Birth 1620 in , Aberdeenshire, , Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:
2 CONT *Catherine Campbell
2 CONT *Birth 1630 in Scotland 
2 CONT *Death 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother was Katherine Campbell whose sister married Patrick Roy McGregor, Clan chieftain in the mid 1600's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother (see story for William Sutherland I):
2 CONT *DAVID TOSHACK
2 CONT **Birth 1655 in , Aberdeenshire, , Scotland
2 CONT **Death 1687   
2 CONT
2 CONT David Toshach called himself the "Last Laird of Monzievaird." The estate of Monzievaird is near the village of Muthill, a small town near the city of Crieff in Perthshire, Scotland. (This contradicts, however, the research done by
2 CONC  Gordon MacGregor on the Tosheoch family, which continued to hold the estate after David's death.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts gathered from the Red Book of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Tosheoch-of-Monzievaird.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Acted as executor for her father in 1665, who died in January of that year (indicating she was of an age of majority by this time, hence, born before 1647).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Arrived in New Jersey from Aberdeen, Scotland aboard the Henry and Francis in July 1684.
