1 NOTE {geni:about_me}     Patrick Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT     In 1697 he was married to his "first wife" and had a son. The son seems to be
2 CONT
2 CONT     dead by 1728 when Patrick made his will and mentions only grandson Gregor and
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mary's family.
2 CONT
2 CONT     In 1724 he gave land to David Southerland and his daughter Mary. This is
2 CONT
2 CONT     probably around the time of their marriage. So I estimate Mary was born c
2 CONT
2 CONT     1704 and David perhaps a few years earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT     In 1728 in the will, David and Mary had sons Patrick and David. The
2 CONT
2 CONT     birthdates for these two are usually given as much later. I don't know where
2 CONT
2 CONT     these dates come from. If they are correct, the two boys must have died young
2 CONT
2 CONT     and two others given the same names. This is certainly possible since David
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jr. married Hannah McDonnell who was born in 1745.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1684 Arrival in USA
