1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Jared Spencer===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	say 1650 - Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT * Death:	Jan 1 1712 - Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT * Parents: Sgt. Thomas Spencer and Sarah Bearding
2 CONT * Wife:	Hannah Pratt (daughter of John)
2 CONT * Children:	Nathaniel Spencer, Nathaniel Spencer, Mary Pease (born Spencer), Sarah Bigelow (born Spencer), Hannah Anna Spencer
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as Gerard, Gerald ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT The earliest documentation for Thomas puts him in the Colonies by the end of 1633, apparently arriving as a single man. He first settled in Cambridge, Mass and moved by 1636 to Hartford, Conn. This would place him among the earlie
2 CONC st of Hartford settlers. He was referred to in his estate papers as "Sergeant Thomas Spencer". He had been a constable in Hartford. I'm not sure if the "Sergeant" refers to his position as "constable" or a military reference. He w
2 CONC as a furniture maker and left his son, Jared, his shop and tools. He lived a full and long life and died at the age of 80 years old on Sep 11, 1687, in Hartford, Connecticut. He married first, Anne Dorryfall in 1634, and had three
2 CONC  children by her. She died by 1645, leaving three small children. He then married Sarah Bearding in 1645 and they had six more children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT S1.	Bedfordshire parish registers (Stotfold 1559-1812)
2 CONT
2 CONT S2.	Jacobus, Donald Lines, “The Four Spencer Brothers: Their Ancestors and Descendants,” The American Genealogist, Vol. 27-28, 1951
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________
