2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John is the son of John and Hephziba (Williams) Fenn.[1] He enlisted for one year in Colonel Jedediah Huntington’s Regiment of the Connecticut Line of the Continental Army. In 1777, he enlisted for another three years in Colonel S
2 CONC amuel Blachley Webb’s 2nd Connecticut Regiment. He was engaged at Monmouth and White Marsh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fenn relocated to Ashtabula County around 1820. John died on November 30th, 1838.
