2 CONT Also see: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~jimward52/fenn.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >I have conceded the fact that Benjamin & Sarah Baldwin Fenn had no son named Edward.  If anyone can prove the parentage of Edward Fenn, born about 1644 in CT., please email me!  
2 CONT
2 CONT >One who questioned the connection gave me info on the known children of Benjamin & Sarah, and is sending the info.  According to her, the children are:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Benjamin, 1640 - 1689
2 CONT # Joseph, 1642 - 1671
2 CONT # Sarah,  1645 - ?
2 CONT # Mary,  1647 - 1671/72
2 CONT # Martha,  1650 - ?
2 CONT
2 CONT >According to the source above and Benjamin's Will, the children of Benjamin Fenn and second wife  Susannah Ward were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel, b.1665, d. 1666
2 CONT # Susannah, b. 4 March 1667 
2 CONT # Samuel, b. 1672, d. young
2 CONT # Samuel
2 CONT # James  (a Lieutenant?)
2 CONT
2 CONT >Benjamin's Will  states his children as being Benjamin, Samuel, James, Sarah, Mary, Martha, and Susannah.  There's no mention of Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr05/rr05_063.htm Pane-Joyce Genealogy] cites Edward as a son of Benjamin Fenn and Sarah Baldwin Fenn on the other hand. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Fenn. Born ca 1644 in Milford, CT. Edward died on 2 Feb 1728 in Wallingford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 Nov 1688 Edward first married Mary Thorpe, daughter of Samuel Thorpe (ca 1646-2 Feb 1728) & Mary Benton (2 Feb 1641/2-1 Mar 1718), in Wallingford, CT.31 Born on 31 Oct 1666 in New Haven, CT.74 Mary died in Wallingford, CT, o
2 CONC n 24 Jul 1725; she was 58.31
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT # Mary Fenn (27 Sep 1689-20 Dec 1760)
2 CONT # Sarah Fenn (24 Nov 1694-)
2 CONT # Theophilus Fenn (31 Jan 1698-18 Dec 1748)
2 CONT # Hannah Fenn (13 Dec 1704-9 Sep 1760)
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26 Jan 1726 Edward second married Abigail Williams in Wallingford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 583, 598
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~jimward52/fenn.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Fenn (c. 1644–1728) was an early settler of Wallingford, Connecticut, and a patriarch of one of the two primary Fenn lineages in colonial America. Noted genealogist Donald Lines Jacobus found no proven link between the Milf
2 CONC ord and Wallingford Fenn families, treating them as distinct colonial branches.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Key Biographical Facts'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth & Death: He was born around 1644 and died on February 2, 1728, at approximately 83 years of age. He is buried in the Center Street Cemetery in Wallingford.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriages:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Thorpe: Married on November 15, 1688. She was the mother of his nine children, including Sarah Fenn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Williams: Married on January 26, 1726, following Mary's death in 1725.
2 CONT Ancestry Debate: While some records list him as the son of Benjamin Fenn of Milford,
