1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sarah Fenn (1694–1781)''' was the second wife of Theophilus Jones (b. 1690). She was a prominent member of the Wallingford and New Haven communities, connected to several founding families of Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biographical Details'''
2 CONT Birth: Born on November 24, 1694, in Wallingford, Connecticut.
2 CONT Parents: She was the daughter of Edward Fenn (1644–1728) and Mary Thorpe (1666–1725).
2 CONT Marriages:
2 CONT Solomon Moss: Married on August 1, 1728. They had several children before his death in 1752.
2 CONT Theophilus Jones: Married on September 22, 1755, in Wallingford. As both were in their 60s at the time of this marriage, they did not have children together.
