2 CONT Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, Vol. 8, pg. 1977 < [https://archive.org/details/familiesofancien00jaco_2/page/1976/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT "from Farm[ington] to W[allingford]". WILLIAMS, fam. 1. James d 3 Nov 1725 WV ; from Farm to W; m 1691 Sarah da. Thomas & Mary Richason, b 25 Mar 1669 FarmV, d 25 Dec 1729 WV. (No parents listed)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Town and City of Waterbury, Connecticut by Sarah Johnson Prichard, pg. 154
2 CONT
2 CONT Fairfield, CT: Families of Old Fairfield.  Vol. 2, page 1070.  < [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/fairfield-ct-families-of-old-fairfield/RecordDisplay?volumeId=7472&pageName=1070&rId=7521585 AmericanAncestors] > Correc
2 CONC tions to Volume 1... Abbott, George (Page 5). His second wife was, we may suppose, Johanna (Linn) Williams, widow of William Willams of Boston. They were married at Boston, 17 July 1660, and the Williams children were... James Wil
2 CONC liams Sr. Born 18 Sep 1670 "[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Williams-29967
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT from Savage vol 4pg 572:
2 CONT
2 CONT "WILLIAM, Boston, m. 19 July 1660, Joanna Lynn, had...James, 18 Sept. 1670" [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Williams married in 1691 Sarah Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT from Hickock:
2 CONT
2 CONT "24. HANNAH HICKOCK, dau. of Samuel (4); born 21 April 1699; bapt. at Milford; died before 21 January 1788; married (1) 13 November 1722, Samuel Williams, born June 1700, died 26 July 1725, son of James (d. 3 Nov. 1725) and Sarah 
2 CONC (Richason) Williams. Sarah Richason was born 25 March 1669; died 25 Dec. 1729; mar. 1691, James Williams, and was dau. of Thomas and Mary Richason." [2]
2 CONT
