1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fuller Merrell Funeral Rites Held Tuesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral rites honoring Fuller Remington Merrell, 85, who died in St. George, Utah, Friday following a heart attack was conducted Tuesday at 1 p.m. in the Naples Ward LDS Chapel, under the direction of Bishop Orlo Goodrich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prayer at the Vernal Mortuary was given by Melby Lybbert, a son-in-law of the deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prelude and postlude music at the chapel was rendered by Mrs. Lloyd T. Pope. "Oh My Father" was sung by a mixed chorus consisting of Frances Southam, Donna Merrell, Elva Manwaring, Rhea Goodrich, Reve Risner, Fay Horrocks, Verdin 
2 CONC Goodrich, Norman Haslem, Vere Wilson, Lowe Goodrich, Phillip Manwaring and Jerome Goodrich, accompanied by Mrs. Pope.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashel Manwaring of the Uintah Stake High Council, offered the invocation and the obituary and remarks was given by Bishop Goodrich.
2 CONT
2 CONT A vocal solo, "In The Garden" was sung by Don M. Walker, accompanied by Ruth Walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Byron Goodrich, Patriarch of the Uintah Stake and former bishop of Naples Ward, was the speaker, followed by the closing hymn, "Abide With Me," sung by the mixed chorus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Harrison of the Uintah Stake High Council, offered the benediction,and burial was in the Vernal Memorial Park cemetery, with Leo A. Merrell, a son, dedicating the grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers were six grandsons of the deceased: Robert Cook, Phillip Merrell, Boyd Merrell, Marvin Merrell, Dale Merrell and Norman Merrell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Serving as honorary pallbearers were members of the Uintah High Priest Quorum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Merrell was born December 23, 1877 in Parasdise, Cache Valley, Utah, a son of Porter William and Harriett Amelia Remington Merrell.
2 CONT
2 CONT While he was yet a small child his parents moved to the Uintah Basin, settling first at Ouray, on the White River and later moving to Dry Fork, Jensen and Ioka, respectively, finally to Vernal.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 18, 1902 he was married to Sarah Christine Angus in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. This was a rather unique occasion being a double wedding as his brother, Franklin R. Merrell, married Mary Jane Angus, a sister to Sarah Ch
2 CONC ristine.
2 CONT
2 CONT They traveled together by wagon from Vernal to Salt Lake City for the wedding. The couples celebrated their 60th wedding anniversary in September.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Merrell were the parents of twelve sons and daughters, eleven of whom are still living and are survivors as is his wife, Harold A., John Ross and Grant Merrell and Mrs. Thayrel (Pearl) Cook and Mrs. Thomas L. (Mable) 
2 CONC Handay, all of Vernal; Karl, Ray and Delroy Merrell, all of Salt Lake City; Mrs. Melby (Bessie) Lybbert of Cardston, Alberta, Canada; Leo A. Merrell and Mrs. James (Marie) Jensen, both of Provo; and one sister, Mrs. A. G. (Lydia) 
2 CONC Goodrich, Moses Lake, Washington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Merrell have spent the past twelve years doing temple work in the Salt Lake and St. George Temples.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the numerous out-of-town visitors attending the services were: Mrs. Delroy Angus, Fuller Remington, Mrs. Laura Teeples, Mr. and Mrs. Karl Merrell and family, Mr. and Mrs. Ray Merrell, Mr. and Mrs. Delroy Merrell and family, 
2 CONC Mr. and Mrs. Marvin Merrell and family, Arthur Goodrich, Sr., and Arthur Goodrich, Sr., all of Salt Lake City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Delbert Angus, Draper; Mr. and Mrs. Elmer Angus, Blythe, California; Reed and Dean Angus, Idaho; Mr. and Mrs. Floyd Angus, Lapoint; Mr. and Mrs. Volt Roper and family, Provo; Mr. and Mrs. Lamont Shupe and family, Ogden; Mr. a
2 CONC nd Mrs. Luther Gale and Mr. and Mrs Hosea Lisonbee, Orem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bishop and Mrs. Hugh Percivalle and family and Mrs. Bertha Angus, Ioka; Mr. and Mrs. Theo Anderson, Myton; Mr. and Mrs. Glen Reymound, Duchesne; Mr. and Mrs. James Jensen and Mr. and Mrs. Leo Merrell and family, Provo; Mr. and Mrs
2 CONC . Melby Lybbert, Cardston, Alberta, Canada and Mr. and Mrs. Gordon Robinson, Raymond, Alberta, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Ray Dunn, Tooele; Mr. and Mrs. James Bird, Mr. and Mrs. Lee Lisonbee and Mr. and Mrs. Bernard Winkler, all of Bluebell; Edward L. Murphy and Mr. and Mrs. John Lemon of Upalco and Mrs. Florence Williams of Roosevelt.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Vernal Express, February 28, 1963, transcribed by Rhonda Holton
2 CONT
2 CONT Children not listed below: Pearl Merrell Cook
