1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ROXANA MOTT DIES MONDAY AT NAPLES HOME  Funeral services for Roxana Merrell Mott, 72, Naples, who died at her residence at 9 a.m. Monday after a lingering illness were conducted Wednesday in the Naples Ward Chapel by Bishop J. Ros
2 CONC s Merrell. Mrs. Mott was born in Naples August 8, 1880, a daughter of Porter and Harriet Remington Merrell. She was married to Albert Mott. Surviving her besides her husband are two sons and two daughters, Golden, Mott, Los Angele
2 CONC s; Vern, Mott, Mrs. Ruth DeMille and Mrs. Alberta Ross, all of Vernal; 19 grandchildren and four great-grandchildren.  Prior to the services, prayer was offered at the home by Alvin Weeks. Opening song "Sometime We'll Understand" 
2 CONC was sung by the Naples mixed quartet followed by invocation offered by John Eaton. "That Wonderful Mother of Mine" was sung by a Lapoint ladies chorus. First speaker was Bishop Ross Merrell, followed by a guitar selection "Whisper
2 CONC ing Hope" by Mr. and Mrs. Armon Eaton and Helen Freestone.  Second speaker was Alvin E. Weeks followed by "Oh My Father" sang by the mixed quartet. Bishop Harold E. Hullinger offered the closing prayer and Bishop Phil Watkins dedi
2 CONC cated the grave.  -Vernal Express, August 28, 1952, transcribed by Rhonda Holton    Family links:   Parents:
