1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Samuel Cook Sr
2 CONT *Born 30 Sep 1641 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT *Died 25 Dec 1703 in Wallingford, New Haven, Connecticut
2 CONT *Son of Henry Cook and Judith Birdsall
2 CONT * Husband of 1) Hope Parker 2) Mary 3) Mary Mallory 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Wallingford, Conn. by Charles Henry Stanley Davis.  Page 672 [https://archive.org/details/historyofwalling00daviiala/page/672 Archive.Org] Genealogies - Part 1, pg. 672, 673
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuel Cook came to New Haven in 1663, m Hope, daughter of Edward Parker of New Haven, May 2, 1667. They went to Wallingford in April, 1670, with the first plant­ers. He was, perhaps, the first and only shoemaker and tanner of le
2 CONC ather in the place. After the decease of his wife Hope, he married Mary Roberts, July 14, 1690. He was regarded as a very good man by his friends and neighbors, and was frequently called to fill offices of responsibility and trust
2 CONC  in the village, and in the church of which he was a member. He died March, 1702. He left an estate of L340. His widow m Jeremiah How, sen., April 9, 1705.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Book of Gideon: Cook 4-6”  [https://funwithfamilyhistory.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/046-chapter4-book-of-gideon.pdf pdf] numbered page 352, pdf Page 6:
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 1st Marriage to Hope Parker:
2 CONT *1 Samuel, b March 3, 1667-8, in New Haven ; 
2 CONT *2 John, b Dec. 3, 1669, in New Haven; 
2 CONT *3 Hannah, b March 3,1671-2, in Wallingford ; 
2 CONT *4 Isaac, b March 10, 1673, d April 7, 1673;
2 CONT * 5 Mary, b April 23, 1675, m Nathaniel Ives, April 5, 1699; 
2 CONT *6 Elizabeth, b August 22, 1677, d young; 
2 CONT *7 Judith, b Feb. 29, 1679, m Jeremiah How jr., April 20, 1704, she d March 20, 1708 ; 
2 CONT *8 Isaac, b Jan. 10, 1681; [Note: The birthdate does not match the Barbour VRs. “p 91 - Isack, s. Sam[ue]ll, b. 10th, seventh, 1673/4 - Vol PR, p 15.”
2 CONT *9 Joseph, b Feb. 25, 1683 ; 
2 CONT *10 Hope, b Sept. 27, 1686, m Joseph Benham, Dec. 18, 1706, she d Jan. 30, 1731. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 2nd marriage to Mary (unknown):
2 CONT *11 Israel, b May 8, 1692 ;
2 CONT *12 Mabel, b June 30, 1694; [SIC: Mehitabel]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Cook by 3rd marriage to Mary Mallory, widow of Eli Roberts:
2 CONT *13 Benjamin, b April 8, 1697, d 1717, unmarried, was a tanner and currier; 
2 CONT *14 Ephraim, b April 19, 1699; 
2 CONT *15 Elizabeth, b Sept. 10, 1701, m Adam Mott, Aug 28, 1717."
2 CONT
2 CONT See also https://sites.google.com/site/webstergriggsfamilies/williams/cook?tmpl=%2Fsystem%2Fapp%2Ftemplates%2Fprint%2F&showPrintDialog=1<br/>
2 CONT 2nd wife Mary Unknown: <br/>
2 CONT Ca 1691 when Samuel was 49, he second married Mary3, in Wallingford, CT.3,11 Born ca 1656.3 Mary died in Wallingford, CT, on 4 Sep 1695; she was 39.3,9 4 Dec 1695 per Wallingford records.<br/>
2 CONT They had the following children:<br/>
2 CONT *  22 i. Israel (1692-)
2 CONT *  23 ii. Mehitabel (1694-1732)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cook-3312
2 CONT *Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 190, 435
2 CONT *History of Wallingford, Conn. by Charles Henry Stanley Davis Genealogies - Part 1, pg. 672
2 CONT *https://funwithfamilyhistory.files.wordpress.com/2012/08/046-chapter4-book-of-gideon.pdf
2 CONT *https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Samuel_Cook_%2842%29
2 CONT * Cook, in Jacobus, Donald Lines. Families of Ancient New Haven. (Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Pub. Co., 1974), 2:435. "Samuel (Cook), b 30 Sep 1641 (Salem Vital Records), d Mar 1703; …"
2 CONT *Samuel Cook, in Savage, James. A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England: Showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692, on the Basis of Farmer's Register. (Boston: Little, Brown, and Co, 1860-
2 CONC 1862), 1:450. "Samuel (Cook), New Haven, m. 2 May 1667, Hope, d. of Edward Parker, had Samuel, b. 3 Mar. 1668; John, 3 Dec. 1669; and a d. without name; rem. to Wallingford 1673, where the residue of his ch. nam. in his will, twel
2 CONC ve in all, were b. Mary Ives, Judith, Isaac, Joseph, Hope, Israel, Mabel, Benjamin, Ephraim, and Eliz. A sec. w. Mary, he had, but we kn. not, wh. of these ch. if any, were hers. He made his will Mar. 1703, and soon d. [Additions 
2 CONC and Corrections] [Savage 4:679] [Vol. 1] P. 450 l. 15 for and a d. without name r. Mary, 3 Mar. 1672;"
2 CONT *https://sites.google.com/site/webstergriggsfamilies/williams/cook?tmpl=%2Fsystem%2Fapp%2Ftemplates%2Fprint%2F&showPrintDialog=1
2 CONT *GEDCOM Source Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut  Lucius Barnes Barbour, Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut (1982 Genealogical Publishing Company)   Page  435 
2 CONT *GEDCOM Source The Leonards and Related Families; 1993 (revised 2  Clark M Leonard, The Leonards and Related Families; 1993 (revised 2002) (unpublished, available)   Page  my#668:22 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LKKM-H3F/samuel-cook-1641-1703
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Cook
2 CONT 30 September 1641–after 12 March 1703 (Age 61)
2 CONT Salem, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The Life Summary of Samuel
2 CONT
2 CONT When Samuel Cook was born on 30 September 1641, in Salem, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Henry Cooke, was 26 and his mother, Judith Birdsall, was 30. He married Hope Parker on 2 May 1667, in New Ha
2 CONC ven, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 4 daughters. He died after 12 March 1703, in Wallingford, New Haven, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, at the age of 61, a
2 CONC nd was buried in Wallingford, New Haven, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America.
