1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of Wallingford, Conn. by Charles Henry Stanley Davis Genealogies - Part 1, pg. 672, 673, 675 [https://archive.org/details/historyofwalling00daviiala/page/673 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuel Cook, son of Samuel and Hope Cook, married Hannah Ives, daughter of William of New Haven, March 3, 1692, John Moss Esq. officiating. She died May 29, 1714. He then married Elizabeth Bedel, of Stratford. He died Sept. 18, 1
2 CONC 725, ae. 58 years, at Wallingford. His widow married Capt. Daniel Harris, of Middletown, Conn. Fie was a farmer in the western part of the township, near the line which now divides Cheshire from Wallingford. Some of his descendant
2 CONC s are still occupying the same land. Estate, L390.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with 1st wife:
2 CONT *16 Hannah, b May 28, 1693, m Jeremiah Hull, she died Nov. 22, 1735, ae. 43 years; 
2 CONT *17 Samuel, b March 5, 1695; 
2 CONT *18 Aaron, b Dec. 28, 1696 ; 
2 CONT *19 Lydia, b Jan. 13, 1699, m Daniel Dutton, d Oct. 12, 1738; 
2 CONT *20 Moses, b Jan. 4, 1700, d Dec. 25, 1711 ;
2 CONT * 21 .Miriam, b Nov. 4, 1703, m Benjamin Curtis, Dec. 12, 1727; 
2 CONT *22 Thankful, b Dec. 24, 1705, d Aug. 19, 1714 ; 
2 CONT *23 Esther, b March 8, 1707, m Abel Yale, July 22, 1730 ; 
2 CONT *24 Eunice, b Feb. 25, 1709 ; 
2 CONT *25 Susan­nah, b Sept. 5, 1711, in Joseph Cole, Dec. 1, 1735 ; 
2 CONT *26 Hope, d Sept. 18, 1728. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 2nd marriage: 
2 CONT *27 Moses, b Nov. 6, 1716; 
2 CONT *28 Thankful, b Nov. 14, 1718, m Stephen Hotchkiss, Dec. 31, 1742 ; 
2 CONT *29 Asaph, b June 23, 1720; 
2 CONT *30 Hannah, b Nov. 4, 1721, m Zephaniah Hull, of Cheshire, and settled at Bethlem."
2 CONT
2 CONT
