1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * In 1743 he and his wife, Eleanor Johnson, moved some of their family to Goshen, Connecticut.  Joseph COOK was counted among the most prominent men in the town of Goshen in Litchfield County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Joseph Cooke Born: 1682-1683, Wallingford, New Haven, Connecticut Died: Nov 7, 1764, Goshen, Litchfield, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Samuel Cooke (1641-1701) & Hope Parker (1650-Bef 1690)
2 CONT * Married: Eleanor Johnson on Oct 14, 1714. (Eleanor Johnson was born in 1677-1703)
2 CONT
