1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''The descendants of William and Elizabeth Tuttle, who came from old to New England in 1635, and settled in New Haven in 1639, with numerous biographical notes and sketches : also, some account of the descendants
2 CONC  of John Tuttle, of Ipswich; and Henry Tuthill, of Hingham, Mass. (1883) Vol.2
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil02tutt#page/152/mode/2up
2 CONT *Simon Tuttle & Abigail
2 CONT **I. Daniel, b. Nov. 11, 1680; m. Oct. 18, 1716, Ruth Howe.
2 CONT **II. Timothy, b. 1682, m. Nov. 2, 1706, Thankful Doolittle; (2) June 9, 1729, Mary Rowe, wid. of Stephen; (3) May 17, 1739, Mary Humiston; (4) June 28, 1749, Mrs. Sarah Humiston.
2 CONT **'''III. Abigail, m. June 5, 1706, Isaac Curtis.
2 CONT **IV. Thankful.
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil02tutt#page/334/mode/2up/search/curtis
2 CONT *'''93. Abigail Tuttle, m. Jan. 5, 1706, Isaac Curtis of Wallingford; sup. the same who received deed of land in Waterbury, Conn., Sept. 11, 1732. Isaac C., jr., received deed thr. Jan. 17, 1733 and Daniel Curtis of Wall'd receive
2 CONC d deed of land thr. Feb, 7, 1733, lying in the north part (Plymouth). --Waterbury Record..
2 CONT **I. Daniel Curtis, b. Aug. 7, 1707; m. Lettice.
2 CONT **II. Isaac Curtis, m. 1727, Mary Tuttle.
2 CONT **III. Phebe Curtis, April 4, 1718.
2 CONT **IV. Joshua Curtis, April 26, 1719.
2 CONT **V. Ebenezer Curtis, Jan. 17, 1721. The Wallingford Rec. says the last three are "chil. of Isaac and Abigail Curtis."
2 CONT *<nowiki>----------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT *'''History of Wallingford, Conn: from its settlement in 1670 to the present ... By Charles Henry Stanley Davis
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=UN4TAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA725&lpg=PA725&dq=Isaac+Curtis+1683&source=bl&ots=zH48luMw7G&sig=_oNmT9KNKLFEIoPQ-zFdqWkCHbg&hl=en&ei=YkLnTMP-B5L6sAOZjvywCw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CBsQ6AEwAj
2 CONC gK#v=onepage&q=Isaac%20Curtis%201683&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.725
2 CONT *Richard Curtis, who was among the first planters in Wallingford, was the father of Isaac Curtis, who married Sarah Ford, of Branford, Aug. 13, 1682, and died July 15, 1712. Richard Curtis died in Wallingford, Sept. 17, 1681, ae. 
2 CONC 70 years. Estate, (english pound)50.
2 CONT **Children: 62 Isaac, b. Nov. 6, 1683; 63 Sarah, b. June 11, 1685; Joseph, b. July 18, 1689, m. Ann Stevens, Jan. 11, 1713; 65 Ebenezer, b. Oct. 6, 1691, d. July 20, 1717; '''66 Isaac, b. March 8, 1693-4, m. Abigail Tuttle'''; 67 
2 CONC Elizabeth, b. Aug. 10, 1701; 68 Benjamin, b. March 2, 1702-3; 69 Moses, b. Aug. 9, 1706; 70 Phebe, d. Aug. 5, 1718; 71 Joshua, d. July 20 1719.
2 CONT *'''62. Isaac.  (I WOULD THINK THIS SHOULD BE 66. Isaac)
2 CONT *'''Isaac Curtis married Abigail Tuttle; she died, and he married Mary Tuttle, Oct. 1, 1729.
2 CONT **Children by 1st marriage; 72 David, b. Aug. 7, 1707; 73 Phebe, b. April 4, 1718; 74 Joshua, b. April 26, 1719; 75 Ebenezer, b. Jan. 17, 1720.
2 CONT *<nowiki>----------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT On 5 Jun 1706 when Isaac was 22, he first married Abigail Tuttle (19669) , daughter of Simon Tuttle (7920) (1647-16 Apr 1719) & Abigail [Tuttle] (-Aug 1722), in Wallingford, CT.31 Abigail died on 6 Dec 1728 in Wallingford, CT.31
2 CONT
2 CONT Child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 	30587 	i. 	Abigail Curtis (9 Apr 1712-6 Feb 1791)
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 Oct 1729 when Isaac was 45, he second married Mary Abernathy (12689) , daughter of William Abernathy (ca 1658-Feb 1717/8) & Sarah Doolittle (4173) (-bef 1711), in Wallingford, CT.31 Born on 27 Mar 1679/80 in Wallingford, CT.3
2 CONC 1
2 CONT
2 CONT sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Isaac Curtis. Born on 6 Nov 1683 in Wallingford, CT.31
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Paul Herbig (@1997), "Herbig-Cracken Family Chronicles," p.97, prfssrpah@aol.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Curtis married 5 June 1706 Abagail Tuttle
