1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the early 1600s Simsbury was inhabited by the Wappinger Indian Tribe. An off shoot of the Algonquians. Between 1640 and 1650 white settlers began farming the land, but the settlement was not established until 16
2 CONC 70. The Saxton's were among the first 13 permanent residents. Rumors of unrest among the indigenous people began to surface. In 1675 King Philip's War began, a war between the tribes and English settlers that were ordered to keep 
2 CONC night watches, and to work in their fields in armed groups. Soon the situation was considered serious enough that the residents of Simsbury had to move to safety in Winsor. In 1676 the town of Simsbury was first pillaged, then bur
2 CONC ned to the ground. This destruction has been described "as the most extensive of any event of any Indian War in New England". In late 1677 the settlers began to return and to start rebuilding. This included John and Mary Saxton. F
2 CONC inally in 1678 a treaty was signed.
