2 CONT *GERRARD or JERRARD SPENCER, the founder of the Haddam and Saybrook, Connecticut, families of this name, born in Stotfold, England, bap. April 28, 1634, was the son of Gerrard Spencer and nephew of Sir Richard. He came to New Engl
2 CONC and in 1632, and was admitted March 9, 1637, a freeman of the Massachusetts Bay Colony March 9, 1637.   . . . .  
