2 CONT **	IX. Rebecca, married 1st John Kennard, of Haddom, about 1692; he died Feb. 1689; she married 2nd John Tanner, of Lyme, Conn.
2 CONT **	X. Ruth, married Joseph Clark.
2 CONT **	XI. Timothy.
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''BRAINARD, Daniel 
2 CONT *'''d. 1 APR 1715 Haddam, Middlesex, CT.
2 CONT *Family:
2 CONT *'''Spouse: SPENCER, Hannah 
2 CONT *b. 1640 Lynn, Essex, Mass.
2 CONT *Parents:
2 CONT *Father: SPENCER, Jared 
2 CONT *Mother: HILLS, Hannah 
2 CONT *'''Children:
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Daniel 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Hannah 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, James 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Joshua 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, William 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Chileab 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Caleb 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Elijah 
2 CONT **BRAINARD, Hezekiah 
2 CONT *From: http://www.genealogyofnewengland.com/f_232.htm#24 _________________
2 CONT *'''Deacon Daniel Brainerd
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	1641  Essex, England
2 CONT *'''Death: 	Apr. 1, 1715  Haddam, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *'''Daniel Brainerd was brought to America when he was eight yrs. old and lived with the Wadsworth family in Hartford, Connecticut in or about the year 1641 He remained with the family until 1662 when he took up residence in Hadda
2 CONC m CT. Unfortunately, there is no documentation to support this or the widely accepted belief that Daniel was from Braintree, England. There are a few family stories concerning Daniel's arrival at such a young age. One, that he was
2 CONC  kidnapped from England and sold for his passage to the Wadsworth family of Hartford. Daniel was to live with and work for the Wadsworths until he reached the age of 21. Another version has it that Daniel's parents sent him to Ame
2 CONC rica due to unrest in England. Daniel Brainerd is the ancestor of all the Brainerds/Brainards to live in the United States. 
2 CONT *'''In 1662, Daniel, along with 27 other men settled in an area now known as Haddam, Connecticut. Daniel's first home was reported to have been a cave. Soon, however Daniel became the largest land owner and one of the most influen
2 CONC tial men in Haddam, serving as constable. He was the first Deacon and the first Justice of the peace in Haddam. He was also a surveyer,town assessor, plotter of land and roads, along with other offices. Daniel was also appointed C
2 CONC ommisioner to the General Assembly in Hartford.
2 CONT *Visiting the Haddam area today, '''one could view the Brainerd Family burial plot where Daniel is buried, the Brainerd Memorial Library, Brainerd Hall and the plaque honoring the Original Proprietors of Haddam, to name a few of t
2 CONC he Brainerd family historical site. 
2 CONT *'''Daniel Brainerd was born abt,1641 in Braintree, ESS, ENG d: 01 Apr 1715 Haddam, Middlesex, CT. He was a Col. and a Deacon. 
2 CONT *'''About 1663, Daniel married Hannah Spencer, of Lynn, MA,''' dau. of Ensign Gerard Spencer and Hannah Joannis Hills. 
2 CONT *'''From that marriage eight children were born and the Brainerd family roots began to take hold in America.
2 CONT *Children-
2 CONT **1. Daniel, BRAINERD, Jr. was a Haddam farmer b: 02 Mar 1665/66 Haddam, Middlesex, CT d: 28 Jan 1742/43 buried Cove Cemetery, East Haddam, Middlesex, CT 
2 CONT **2. Hannah Brainerd Gates (83) (1667 - Sept. 7, 1750)m. Thomas Gates b. Cove Cemetery, East Haddam, Middlesex, CT 
2 CONT **3. James Brainerd(6/2/1669-2/10/1742)Haddam,Middlesex, CT 
2 CONT **4. Joshua Brainerd 7/20/1671- 5/13/1755 East Haddam, Middlesex, CT. Mary (wife) died Dec. 25, 1705 East Haddam  m. Mehittabell Dudley, Jul 12, 1710
2 CONT **5. William Brainerd Mar. 30 1673. 
2 CONT **6. Caleb Brainerd( Nov. 20, 1676 - Jul 11, 1742 Haddam, CT
2 CONT **7. Elijah Brainerd May 26, 1678 - Ap. 20, 1740 m. Mary Bushnel b. 1675 (My ancestor) 
2 CONT **8 Hezekiah b. May 24, 1680 Haddam CT. D. May 24 1727 Hartford CT. father of famous missionary to the Cherokee Indians (David Brainard b. Apr. 20, 1718 d. Oct. 9, 1747)
2 CONT *Probate; 2 May 1715; Haddam, Middlesex Co., CT 8. Invt. and Agreement in Vol. IX, Page 37 Name: Daniel Brainard Location: Haddam
2 CONT *Invt. œ834-10-03. Taken 19 April, 1715, by Nathaniel Spencer, Gerrard Spencer and Joseph Arnold.
2 CONT *An agreement, dated the 2nd of May, 1715: A distribution of the estate by an agreement among the children, Daniel, James, Joshua, William, Caleb, Elijah and Hezekiah (sons), Thomas Gates and Hannah his wife (only daughter): Our f
2 CONC ather's will not being so full and clear as we could wish, we have thought best to agree upon a distribution of the estate of our hond. father. And having first come to a loving agreement with our hond. mother-in-law, Hannah Brain
2 CONC ard, we have proceeded to make the following distribution: I, Thomas Gates, acting in behalf of my wife Hannah, and we, Daniel, James, Joshua, William, Caleb, Elijah and Hezekiah, have fully and freely made up our hond. father's D
2 CONC aniel Brainard his estate, and do hereby promise and engage, for ourselves and heirs, each to take up satisfied of lands heretofore set down to us and to make no more challenges or demands of any more lands or rights, neither by v
2 CONC irtue or under color of any deed of gift received from our father in his life-time or upon any other color or pretense whatsoever, and that we do receive sd. lands and every parcel of them as our sd. father held them the day of hi
2 CONC s death, each running the risk of the title our father had to them, and being obliged to defend the same for his own part if there (was) occasion. Moreover we the sd. Daniel, James, Joshua, William, Caleb, and Elijah, do hereby (d
2 CONC eclare) that we have received œ8-01-00 apiece out of the personal estate. I, Thomas Gates, do acknowledge that I have received œ33-01-00, and I, Hezekiah Brainard, have received œ32-12-00. Moreover we do all and each of us for our
2 CONC selves and heirs hereby covenant and promise that we shall make no more demands of estate, real or personal, that was our father's, and that we will in no wise disturb or annoy each other, but each of the eight aforementioned and 
2 CONC their heirs may quietly enjoy his part aforementioned. Under the full ratification of all which premises we have all and each of us hereunto set our hand and affixed seal this 2nd May, 1715.
2 CONT *Daniel Braynard, ls. James Braynard, ls. Joshua Braynard, ls. William Braynard, ls. Caleb Braynard, ls. Elijah Braynard, ls. Hezekiah Braynard, ls.
2 CONT *To Thomas Gates, acting in behalf of his wife Hannah (only daughter to our hond. father) 50 acres of land bought of Mr. Blackleach, on the north side of Haddam bounds in Colchester bounds more, in personal or moveable estate. Tot
2 CONC al, œ45-10-00.
2 CONT *Court Record, Page 253--14 April, 1715: Adms. granted to Daniel and Hezekiah Brainard jointly. They exhibited an invt. of sd. estate and also an agreement for a division of the estate, which was accepted by the Court.
2 CONT *Source: The Genealogy of the Brainerd-Brainard Family in America, 1649-1908, 
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Spouses:
2 CONT *'''  Hannah Spencer Brainerd (1641 - 1691)*
2 CONT *'''  Elizabeth Wakeman Arnold (1630 - 1698)*
2 CONT *'''  Hannah Spencer Sexton (1653 - 1715)*
2 CONT *''' Children:
2 CONT **  Daniel Brainerd (1665 - 1743)*
2 CONT **  Hannah Brainerd Gates (1667 - 1750)*
2 CONT **  James Brainerd (1669 - 1742)*
2 CONT **  Joshua Brainerd (1672 - 1755)*
2 CONT **  William Brainerd (1673 - 1747)*
2 CONT **  Caleb Brainerd (1676 - 1742)*
2 CONT **  Elijah Brainerd (1677 - 1740)*
2 CONT **  Hezekiah Brainerd (1681 - 1727)*
2 CONT *'''Burial:  Thirty Mile Island Plantation Burial Yard, Haddam, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 47491853
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=47491853
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Judge Daniel Brainerd
2 CONT *'''Birth: 	Mar., 1641  Essex, England
2 CONT *'''Death: 	Apr. 1, 1715  East Haddam, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *'''Burial:  Thirty Mile Island Plantation Burial Yard, Haddam, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 72463158
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=brainerd&GSfn=daniel&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSst=8&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=72463158&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of the early settlement of Haddam Neck is involved in obscurity, but it is supposed to be about 1710 or '12, by the following persons, some of them settling later than others: William BRAINERD, his wife Sarah BIDWELL, and
2 CONC  their children; James BRAINERD jr., his wife Anne; Thomas SELDEN, his wife Sarah, and their children; Sylvester DUDLEY; Gideon GOFF jr., and perhaps his father; Jabez BROOKS Esq., and perhaps Thomas BROOKS; Dr. Joshua and Deacon 
2 CONC Gideon ARNOLD, their sisters, and possibly their father, John; ____ CONE; Robert CHAPMAN; Benajah CLARK, and perhaps Deacon Ebenezer SMITH and William MARKHAM; _____ STOCKING. Of these, William BRAINERD, the fifth child of Daniel 
2 CONC and Hannah (SPENCER) BRAINERD, one of the original proprietors of Haddam, married Sarah BIDWELL, December 13th 1698, and built his house between the foot of Quarry Hill and the house of the late Cyprian S. BRAINERD. Their children
2 CONC  were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sarah, married Deacon Gideon ARNOLD, one of the settlers. 2. Sergt. William J. married Esther _____. 3. Hannah, married William SMITH. 4. Samuel, married Esther BRAINERD, daughter of Jabez and Hannah (CLARK) BRAINERD, and settl
2 CONC ed in BRAINERD District in Haddam. 5. (Rev.) Chiliab, graduated at Yale, minister in Eastbury, town of Glastonbury. 6. Lieut. Josiah sen., twice married. He built his house on Quarry Hill in 1737. The house was torn down in 1883. 
2 CONC He served in two expeditions to Canada; was with Gen. Wolfe, at the capture of Quebec; and also served in the Revolutionary war. 7. Nathan, twice married. He built his house where the house of Oliver B. ARNOLD now stands.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Reference: [http://dunhamwilcox.net/town_hist/haddam_neck_hist.htm Dunham-Wilcox]
