1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Thomas Spencer===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth:	Mar 29 1607 - Stotford, Bedfordshire, England
2 CONT * Death:	Sep 11 1687 - Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT * Parents:	Gerard Spencer,, Alice Whitebread
2 CONT * Married:  1) Ann Derifield 2) Sarah Bearding
2 CONT
2 CONT ===supporting data===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.gravesfa.org/gen345.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gerard (1) Spencer (1614-1685) along with his older brothers, William (1601-1640), Thomas (1607-1687), and Michael (1611-1653) were among the very first settlers in New England under the auspices of the Massachusetts Bay Company.
2 CONC  Their sister, Elizabeth Spencer, also was a pioneer as the wife of Timothy Tomlins. Almost certainly all were among the first passengers of the Winthrop Fleet when the first contingent of eleven ships reached New England in 1630.
2 CONC " [Jack T. & Edith W. Spencer, ''Gerard Spencer, A Pioneer of Cambridge'', Lynn & Haddam; Connecticut Nutmegger, Sept 1997, pgs 188-614, as cited in http://ketchum.bobaddleman.com/spencer_family.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Our New England ancestors and their descendants, 1620-1900: historical ... By Henry Whittemore
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/ournewenglandanc00whit
2 CONT **Spencer and Allied Families
2 CONT *Pg. 49-84
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/ournewenglandanc00whit#page/104/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 53
2 CONT *   Prof. Ray T. Spencer while making researches in his own line, discovered among the church records of St. George's Parish, Stotfold, Bedfordshire, England. much interesting data, concerning the line of Gerrard Spencer, the fath
2 CONC er of William, '''Thomas''', Michael and Gerrard the emigrants, from which it appears that the above named Gerrard was the son of Michael who also had a brother Gerrard, and they were the sons of John. Thus three generations prece
2 CONC ding the emigrants are definitely established. The church records of St. George's Parish, above referred to, show that "June 9, 1558, John Spencer, Sen., was buried." 
2 CONT *   There is evidence to show that this John was the father of Michael and of the first Gerrard mentioned. 
2 CONT **		FROM NOTES OF GEO. T. SPENCER. 
2 CONT *   The ancestry of Gerard Spencer and his brothers William, Thomas and Michael Spencer, appears from the parish registers of Edworth and Stotfield in Bedfordshire, Eng., and other contemporaneous documents. 
2 CONT *Jan. 25, 1555, Michael Spencer and Annis Liuur were married (the last name of Annis is so poorly written in the record that is cannot be definitely determined.)
2 CONT *April 20, 1557, John, son of Michael Spencer baptized.
2 CONT *May 27, 1558, was baptized Michael, son of Michael Spencer.
2 CONT *April 15, 1560, buried Michael, son of Michael Spencer.
2 CONT *23 Feb. 1561, Annis, the wife of Michael Spencer, was buried.
2 CONT *20 Aug., 1564, Joan, the daughter of Michael Spencer, was baptized.
2 CONT *30 Aug., 1566, Alice, daughter of Michael Spencer, was baptized. }Twins.
2 CONT *30 Aug., 1566, Michael Spencer, was baptized,} Twins
2 CONT *24 July, 156?, Ann, daughter of Michael Spencer baptized.
2 CONT *30 July, 1568, Jarratt Spencer and Ellen Whitson were married, whose will was proved at London, 20 May, 1577; he was brother of Michael the elder.
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/ournewenglandanc00whit#page/106/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 54
2 CONT *12 March, 1571, Thomas, son of Michael Spencer was baptized.
2 CONT *20 May, 1576, Gerat Spencer, son of Michael Spencer, and Elizabeth his wife, baptized.
2 CONT *9 July, 1580, Richard, son of Michael and Elizabeth Spencer, baptized.
2 CONT *18 Nov., 1599, Elizabeth, wife of Michael Spencer, was buried.
2 CONT *It is quite probable that Michael Spencer of Edworth, and Gerrard Spencer of Biggleswade, were sons of John Spencer, Senior, and Ann Spencer who burials are recorded in Edworth register, the former June 9, 1558, and the later Jun
2 CONC e 16, 1569: Nothing more is known of them than what is disclosed by these records .... etc. ________________________
