2 CONT ==Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sergeant Thomas Spencer''', Cambridge; freeman, May 14, 1634; removed in 1637 to Hartford, where he was one of the original proprietors; his home-lot in 1639 was on the east side of Main St., near what is now the junction of Ma
2 CONC in and Windsor Streets.; he served in the Pequot War; chimney-viewer, 1650; constable, north side, 1658; surveyor of highways, 1672; he was sergeant of the trainband in 1650, and received in 1671 a grant of 60 acres, "for his good
2 CONC  service in the country." He married (1)____;(2) September 11, 1645, Sarah, only child of Nathaniel Boarding, of Hartford. He died September 11, 1687.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children of 1st wife:==
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Obadiah, Hartford; freeman, 1658; married Mary, daughter of Nicholas Disborough; died 1712.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Thomas; freeman, 1658; married Esther, daughter of William Andrews, of Hartford; removed to Suffield.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Samuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children of 2d wife:==
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Gerard, Hartford; married December 22, 1680, Hannah, daughter of John Pratt, Jr., of Hartford; died 1712.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Sarah, married Thomas Huxley, of Suffield; died October 24, 1712.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Elizabeth, baptized March 26, 1648; in.. Samuel Andrews, of Hartford, vii. Hannah, born April 15,1653.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. Mary, born May 18, 1655. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ix. Martha, born March 19, 1657-8; married Benton.
2 CONT
