2 CONT * .... etc
2 CONT *'''   (I) Thomas Spencer, who with his wife came to Hartford in the company of Thomas Hooker. He was representative to the General Court, and had a grant of land given him for his services.
2 CONT *   (II) Samuel Spencer, '''son of the above''', moved to Windham (now Scotland), Connecticut.
2 CONT *   (III) John Spencer, son of Samuel, born in Windham, died a violent death during the raising of a church, and is furied in Scotland. He had five sons in the Revolutionary war.
2 CONT *   (IV) Jonathan Spencer, son of John, born in Windham, was one of those who "turned out" at the "Lexington Alarm." He marriad a Miss Brown, of Brooklyn, Connecticut.
2 CONT *   (V) Ichabod Spencer, .... etc. __________________________
2 CONT *'''Commemorative biographical record of Hartford County, Connecticut : containing biographical sketches of prominent and representative citizens, and of many of the early settled families (1901) Volume Part 2
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/commemorativebio12jhbe
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/commemorativebio12jhbe#page/1110/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 1110
2 CONT *MRS. HARRIET ARABELLA (SPENCER) FULLER .... etc.
2 CONT *The Spencer family is descended from (I) Michael Spencer and his wife Elizabeth, ....
2 CONT *   (II) Jerad Spencer, son of Michael, ... married Alice .... children '''Thomas''', John, William, Jerad, Michael
2 CONT *'''   (III) Thomas Spencer, known as Sergeant Thomas, was the progenitor of the Suffield branch. He was born March 27, 1607, at the old home in Bedfordshire, England, and on coming to America with his four brothers located first 
2 CONC at Cambridge, Mass., in 1632. In 1635 he removed to Hartford with Rev. Thomas Hooker's company, being among the first settlers in that town. He served in the Pequot war in 1637, being promoted to the rank of sergeant, and later he
2 CONC  received a grant of sixty acres of land for his good service. By his first wife, he had three children:''' Adaiah, Thomas and Samuel. '''By the second there were six children, viz.:''' Jarad; Sarah, who married Thomas Huxley; Eli
2 CONC zabeth, who married Samuel Andrews, of Hartford; Hannah; Mary; and Martha, who married a Mr. Benton.
2 CONT *   (IV) Thomas Spencer, the next in the line of descent, was born in Hartford, Conn., and settled at Suffield, Conn., in time to be made a voter at the first town meeting. He located on a tract of land known as the "Norton & Morg
2 CONC an Place," on Main street, originally High street, and there engaged in farming. He died July 23, 1689, and was buried in Suffield. His wife Esther (Andrews), daughter of William Andrews, died in Suffield March 6, 1698. They had s
2 CONC even children: Abigail, Thomas, Samuel, William, Anna, Elizabeth and Esther.
2 CONT *   (V) Samuel Spencer was born in Suffield, where he was engaged in farming many years, his death occurring Nov. 23, 1743. he was married, March 18, 1700, to Elizabeth Mancroft, a daughter of Daniel Mancroft, of Roxbury, Mass., a
2 CONC nd two children were born to them:  .... etc. __________________________________________
