2 CONT *'''Thomas, Cambridge MA; freeman, May 14, 1634; removed in 1637 to Hartford, CT, where he was one of the original proprietors; his home lot in 1639 was on the east side of Main Street, near what is now the junction of Main and Wi
2 CONC ndsor Streets; he served in the Pequot War; chimney-viewer, 1650; constable, north side, 1658; surveyor of highways, 1672; he was sergeant of the trainband in 1650, and received in 1671 a grant for 60 acres, "for his good service 
2 CONC in the country".
2 CONT *'''The progenitor of the Suffield's Spencer family is memorialized on a large family monument. 
