2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration|needs=Footnotes}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Thomas was born before 1607. He is the son of [[Spencer-2940|Jarrard Spencer]] and [[Whitbread-55|Alice Whitbread]].  He passed away in 1687.
2 CONT '''Sergeant Thomas Spencer,''' Cambridge; freeman, May 14, 1634; removed in 1637 to Hartford, where he was one of the original proprietors ;his home-lot in 1639 was on the east side of Main St., near what is now the junction of Ma
2 CONC in and Windsor Sts.; he served in the Pequot War;chimney-viewer, 1650; constable, north side, 1658; surveyor of highways, 1672; he was sergeant of the trainband in 1650, and received in 1671 a grant of 60 acres, "for his good serv
2 CONC ice in the country." He m. (1) -; (2) Sept. 11, 1645, Sarah, only child of Nathaniel Bearding, of Hartford. He d. Sept. 11, 1687.-Ch. of 1st wife : i. Obadiah, Hartford; freeman, 1658; m. Mary, dau. of Nicholas Disborough; d. 1712
2 CONC . ii. Thomas; freeman, 1658; m. Esther, den. of William Andrews, of Hartford; removed to Suffield iii. Samuel. Ch. of 2d wife: iv. Gerard, Hartford;m. Dec. 22, 1680, Hannah, dau. of John Pratt, Jr., of Hartford; d. 1712. v. Sarah,
2 CONC  m. Thomas Huxley, of Suflield; d. Oct. 24, 1712. vi. Elizabeth, bapt. March 26, 1648; m. Samuel Andrews, of Hartford. vii. Hannah, b. April 15, 1653. viii. Mary, b. May 18, 1655. ix. Martha, b. March 19, 1657-8; m. - Benton. :: '
2 CONC 'The Founders of Hartford''
2 CONT
2 CONT === Note ===
2 CONT A short biography of this man and the documentary evidence relating tohim is given in The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England1620-1633, Volumes I-III (Online database: NewEnglandAncestors.org, New England Historic Ge
2 CONC nealogical Society, 2002), (Orig. Pub. New England Historic Genealogical Society. Robert Charles Anderson, The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III, 3vols., 1995). : [http://www.newenglandance
2 CONC stors.org/database_search/gen_GreatMigrations.asp?f=F:\INETPUB\WWWROOT\NEHGS\RESEARCH\DATABASE\GREATMIGRATIONS\CONTENT\0808.HTM New England Ancestors]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===DNA===* Paternal relationship is confirmed through Y-chromosome DNA testing.[[Spencer-7007|Frank Spencer]] and [[Spencer-2442|Chet Spencer]] match on 64 out of 67 markers (see YSearch IDs BVDU9 and 23V7R) thereby confirming the
2 CONC ir direct paternal lines back to their MRCA [[Spencer-628|Gerard Spencer]].
2 CONT
