1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. Cornelius W. Larison, in The Larisun Famili ... [sic] (1888), p. 384, states that "The bodies of all these individuals [i.e., Jared Sexton, his wife Anne Larison, and her second husband, Benjamin Parke] were bu
2 CONC ried in the ancient Parke-Larison Cemetery which was near the center of James Larison's homestead." Ralph Ege, in Pioneers of Old Hopewell (1908), p. 239, states that "Judge [Jared] Sexton ... is buried in the family plot on the f
2 CONC arm." It is not clear whether "the family plot" was the Parke-Larison burial ground, or possibly the nearby Sexton family burial ground; see GMNJ 27:14 (Jan. 1952). Note: See GMNJ 71:16 (1996)
