1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ambrose Fowler Sr.'''
2 CONT * BIRTH	6 May 1625 - Dalbury Lees, South Derbyshire District, Derbyshire, England
2 CONT * DEATH	18 Oct 1704 (aged 79) - Westfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL	Old Burying Ground, Westfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID	37524734 · View Source
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37524734/ambrose-fowler
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrose Fowler was born in Dalbury Lees, England, the son of William Fowler and Sarah (Tapp) Fowler. He married Jane Alvord on 06 May 1646 in Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children are: 
2 CONT # Abigail, 
2 CONT # John, 
2 CONT # Mary, 
2 CONT # Samuel, 
2 CONT # Hannah, 
2 CONT # Elizabeth and 
2 CONT # Ambrose
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT 1995 Inventory by Walter Ayers, Westfield Historic Commissioner
2 CONT
2 CONT From: "Genealogical and family history of the county of Jefferson, New York; a record of the achievements of her people and the phenomenal growth of her agricultural and mechanical industries" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrose, only son of William Fowler, was at Windsor as early as 1640. The records of that town mention the burning of his house and barn in 1675. He was married there May 6, 1646, to Jane Alvord, who died May 6, 1684, at Westfield
2 CONC . He died October 18, 1704. His will was made in 1692 and proved in 1706. His children, all. of whom were residents of Windsor, Connecticut, were: Abigail, John, Mary, Samuel, Hannah, Elizabeth and Ambrose. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigrated 1640 to Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT William Fowler was a magistrate of colonial New Haven, Connecticut. His name is listed among the members of Rev. John Warham's church in 1640. In 1641, William worked on a committee to settle boundaries betweenPoquonnuck and Uncow
2 CONC ny. A genealogy of his son Ambrose is noted below.
2 CONT On 06 May 1646 at Windsor, Connecticut, Ambrose Fowler married Jane Alvord.<ref>Connecticut: Vital Records (The Barbour Collection), 1630-1870 (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 201
2 CONC 1.) From original typescripts, Lucius Barnes Barbour Collection, 1928. (marriage to Joane Alford). Windsor p. 102</ref> Ambrose's house and barn burned down in 1675 at Windsor, Connecticut. Ambrose's will was proven in 1706, he na
2 CONC med seven children, all recorded at Windsor:
2 CONT #Abigail, b 1 March 1646, m(1) Increase Sikes on 22 March 1670;
2 CONT #John b. 06 Nov 1648, m(1) Mercy Miller of Northampton;
2 CONT #Mary, b. 15 May 1650, m(1) Fearnot King 14 May 1677;
2 CONT #Samuel, b. 18 Nov 1652, m. Abigail Brown;
2 CONT #Hannah, b. 20 Dec 1651, m. James Sexton of Westfield;
2 CONT #Elizabeth, b. 02 Dec 1656, d. unmarried;
2 CONT #Ambrose, b. 08 May 1658, m. Mary Baker. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
