2 CONT == Biography ==William Fowler was a magistrate of colonial New Haven, Connecticut.  His name is listed among the members of Rev. John Warham's church in 1640.  In 1641, William worked on a committee to settle boundaries between Po
2 CONC quonnuck and Uncowny.  A genealogy of his son Ambrose is noted below. 
2 CONT On 06 May 1646, Ambrose Fowler married Jane Alvord.   Ambrose's house and barn burned down in 1675 at Windsor, Connecticut.  Ambrose's will was proven in 1706, he named seven children, all recorded at Windsor: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Abigail, b 1 March 1646;
2 CONT *John b. 06 Nov 1648;
2 CONT *Mary, b. 15 May 1650;
2 CONT *Samuel, b. 18 Nov 1652;
2 CONT *Hannah, b. 20 Dec 1651;
2 CONT *Elizabeth, b. 02 Dec 1656;
2 CONT *Ambrose, b. 08 May 1658. Samuel m. Abigail Brown on 06 Nov 1683 in Windsor, Connecticut.  The couple moved to Westfield, Massachusetts, and had ten children.
2 CONT *Samuel, b. 29 Jan 1683; m. Mercy ___?*Jonathan, b. 19 Oct 1685; m(1) Catharine Marshall; m(2) Hannah Pettibone;
