2 CONT John Pynchon III (abt. 1672 - 1742)
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel John Pynchon III
2 CONT Born about 1672 in Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap [uncertain]
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of John Pynchon II and Margaret (Hubbard) Pynchon
2 CONT Brother of Margaret (Pynchon) Downing and William Pynchon
2 CONT Husband of Bathshua (Taylor) Pynchon — married 18 Feb 1702 (to 20 Jun 1710) in Westfield, Massachusettsmap
2 CONT Husband of Phebe (Sexton) Pyncheon — married 3 Nov 1711 in Enfield, Hartford, Connecticutmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Elizabeth (Pyncheon) Colton, William Pynchon, John Pynchon, Joseph Pynchon, Mary (Pynchon) Dwight, Bathshua (Pynchon) Harris, Unnamed Infant Pynchon, Martha Pynchon, Edward Pynchon, Nathanael Pynchon, George Pynchon, Cha
2 CONC rles Pynchon and Margaret Pynchon
2 CONT Died 12 Jul 1742 at about age 70 in Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Marie Chantigny private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 22 Jan 2023 | Created 24 Oct 2014
2 CONT This page has been accessed 1,517 times.
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT 1 Biography
2 CONT 1.1 Birth
2 CONT 1.2 First marriage and children
2 CONT 1.3 Second marriage and children
2 CONT 1.4 Career
2 CONT 1.5 Death
2 CONT 2 Sources
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pynchon was born about 1672[1], probably in Ipswich, MA, to John Pynchon and Margaret Hubbard[2][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT First marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT John married first Bathshua Taylor in Springfield on 18 Jul 1702.[5][6][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bashshna and John had at least 6 children[8][9]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, b. 27 Dec 1702[10]; m. Benjamin Colton of Longmeadow, MA; d. 26 Sep 1776
2 CONT William, b. 11 Nov 1703[11]; m. 14 Dec 1738 to Sarah Bliss; d. 11 Jan 1783
2 CONT John (twin), b. 7 Feb 1704[12];d. 6 Apr 1754[13]
2 CONT Joseph (twin), b. 8 Feb 1704[14]
2 CONT Mary, b. 10 Oct 1706[15]; m. Brigadier General Joseph Dwight
2 CONT Bathshua, b. 11 Jan 1709[16]; m. Robert Harris 18 Feb 1730; d. 1760
2 CONT Bathshua died in 1710, age 27 years.[17]
2 CONT
2 CONT Second marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT John married second Phebe Sexton of Enfield, Ct. in 1711.[18][19]
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe and John had at least 7 children, probably all born in Spirngfield[20][21];
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha, b. ; d. 8 Dec 1712[22]
2 CONT Edward, b. 9 Apr 1713[23]; m. 15 Dec 1763 to widow Rebecca (Stoughton) Bliss of Windsor, CT; d. 3 Nov 1777
2 CONT Nathaniel, b. 3 Mar 1715[24][25]; d. 10 Oct 1722[26]
2 CONT George, b. 20 Apr 1717[27]; m.(1) 21 Dec 1738 to Hannah Bartlett; m. (2) ; Abigail Pense of Enfield; d. 25 Ju 1797
2 CONT Charles, b. 31 Jan 1719[28][29]; m. 30 Jul 1749 Anna Dwight of Hatifeld; d. 18 Aug 1783
2 CONT Margaret, b. ; d. 27 Oct 1722[30][31]
2 CONT Phebe died in Springfield in 1722, age 36.[32]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT After attending college in Boston for a couple of years, John's grandfather procured for him the office of Clerk of the Court of Common Pleas and Court of Sessions, at Springfield. For some years he lived with his grandfather who 
2 CONC was First Justice of the Court. He was later appointed County Registrar.[33]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT John died in 1742, in Springfield where he was buried.[34][35][36][37][38]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
