1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT The birth of [[Gilbert-5757|Ebenezer Gilbert]] is evidently not recorded, but he is known to have died in infancy or young childhood, and the record of deaths in Springfield, Massachusetts, includes this somberline:
2 CONT "Ebenezer the son of Thomas Gilbert of Brookfeild was Sicke & died Jan4: 91:"
2 CONT This date translates -- with the inclusion of a required 10-day addition -- to 14 January, 1692, New Style.
2 CONT Ebenezer is likely to have been an early child of the second marriage of Thomas Gilbert III, to Anna Bancroft (later widowed and remarried name: Anna Sexton); it is however possible, in the absence of a birth record, that -- as in
2 CONC dicated in the 1953 genealogy "The Gilbert Family:Descendants of Thomas Gilbert" -- Ebenezer might have been a late child by Thomas's first wife, Abilene, prior to her death in November of 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Died''' Died in infancy. ≤ref>email 1/31/06 from Ellen Baker, Washington, U.S.A.; ancestry.com ID EllenBaker80 (defunct emails: dab@bossig.com; dab@3-cities.com)≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />* Death: Massachusetts: Vital Records, 1621-1850 (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001-2016); https://www.americanancestors.org/DB190/i/46055/1694/1320126007 (subscr
2 CONC iption required)
2 CONT * The Gilbert Family: Descendants of Thomas Gilbert, 1582(?)-1659, by Homer Worthington Brainard, Harold Simeon Gilbert, and Clarence Almon Torrey, Edited with a Foreword by Donald Lines Jacobus; New Haven, Connecticut, 1953, p. 8
2 CONC 8; ebook available online (cost): https://www.ancestorstuff.com/E-Books/the-gilbert-family-descendants-of-thomas-gilbert-of-mt-wollaston-braintree-windsor-and-wethersfield-1582-1659.html
