1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Thomas Bancroft=
2 CONT * BIRTH 14 Dec 1626 Swarkestone, South Derbyshire District, Derbyshire, England
2 CONT * DEATH 1684 (aged 57–58) Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Springfield Cemetery, Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * GPS-Latitude: 42.1019732, Longitude: -72.5750519
2 CONT * PLOT Willow Avenue 2-97
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 112539557 photo added by Angie Robinson
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biogaphy==
2 CONT Thomas Bancroft of Enfield (son of John Bancroft and his wife) was born 14 Dec 1626 at Swarkestone, South Derbyshire District, Derbyshire, England.  According to Springfield records Thomas arrived in Springfield 1653, resided in S
2 CONC pringfield 31 years until his death in 1684 as the first settler of Freshwater Brook, now Thompsonville, Enfield, Connecticut. In 1668 he resided in Westfield, Massachusetts, where he was a selectman (legislator). On March 1680 he
2 CONC  sold his property and moved back to Enfield, CT.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He 1st married Margaret Wright Dec. 8, 1653 daughter of Deacon Samuel Wright and had eight children together before her death.  He then married in Westfield, MA Hannah Gardner and had three additional children with her before he d
2 CONC ied 1684 (aged 57–58) at Enfield (then Massachusetts, now Connecticut).  His cattle mark was "Ye top of both ears cut off and a little piece cut out of ye off ear."  He’s buried at the Springfield Cemetery, Springfield, Hampden Co
2 CONC unty, Massachusetts at the Old Burial Ground, First Parish Congressional Church. He had the oldest tombstone in Wakefield. Where Common Burial Ground is now. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His will is recorded in Springfield, dated November 1684. It gave to his eldest son, Thomas Jr., 15 acres of land on south side of the Waxanoak River. To his sons Samuel, John and Nathaniel (married Ruth Hale), he gave equal share
2 CONC s in Enfield. He gave seven pounds to each of his daughters Anna and Rebecca. To his loving wife, he gave the house and contents. Since this will was not signed, by witnesses, it could not be settled until 1703.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT John Errington Bancroft 1596 - 6 Aug 1637 
2 CONT Jane Bonython/Bonithon Bancroft 1595 - 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses'''
2 CONT Margaret Wright Bancroft 1633–1699 m. Dec. 8, 1653 daughter of Dea. Samuel Wright
2 CONT Hannah Gardner Barber 1650–1711 m. 22 Nov 1676 in Hadley, Hampshire, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 11x with Margaret 8x*, Hannah 3x**
2 CONT *Lidia Bancroft Apr 6, 1655-
2 CONT *Margaret Bancroft Oct 16, 1656-
2 CONT *Anna Bancroft Sep 1, 1658-Aug 30, 1659
2 CONT *Thomas Bancroft Jan 21, 1659-
2 CONT *Anna Bancroft Sexton May 5, 1663-  m1 Thomas Gibert, m2 James Sexton
2 CONT *Julia Bancroft -July 30, 1666
2 CONT *Samuel Bancroft Jan 25, 1667-Jan 30, 1667
2 CONT *Lieut Samuel Bancroft 1669–1742
2 CONT **Ruth Bancroft Stiles Aug 29, 1670–1714
2 CONT **Rebecca Bancroft Gillett Feb 23, 1680–1725 m. Samuel Gillett
2 CONT **Rev Nathaniel Bancroft 22 Oct 1683–20 Jan 1753 m. Elizabeth "Ruth" Hale 19 Dec. 1687 Stowe, Middlesex, MA
2 CONT
