2 CONT Anna Bancroft, Jul 01, 1658, Enfield, CT; - 1757, Enfield, CT; m. Thomas Gilbert, Apr 09, 1690, Springfield, MA.
2 CONT Thomas Bancroft, 1659, Nov 21, 1659, Enfield, CT; d. 1753, Cape May, New Jersey, arrived there by 1700. 
2 CONT Anna Bancroft, b. May 05, 1663; d. March 16, 1773, Westfield, MA; m. (1) James Sexton; m. (2) Thomas Gilbert.
2 CONT Julia Bancroft, b. July 30, 1666, Enfield, CT; d. July 30, 1666, Springfield, MA.
2 CONT Sarah Bancroft, 165719, Mar 14, 1657/58, Reading Middlesex, MA - Jun 19, 1661, Reading Middlesex, MA.
2 CONT -Nathaniel Bancroft, 1683, b. October 24, 1683, Enfield, Hartford, CT; d. August 26, 1764, Granville, MA.
2 CONT -Ruth Bancroft, 1670, b. August 29, 1670, Westfield ,Hartford, CT; d. 1714, Hartford, CT; m. JOHN STILES, Westfield, MA.  Ruth and John had 13 children. They had 2 sets of twins. She died in childbirth. 
2 CONT -Rebecca Bancroft, b. February 03, 1679/80, Springfield, MA; d. December 31, 1725, Suffield, CT; m. Samuel Gilbert, January 22, 1701/02, Suffield, CT21; b. Suffield, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Bancroft-of-Dedham-and-Reading/6000000002702080557
2 CONT
2 CONT A number of interesting articles have appeared in The American Genealogist (TAG) about the family of Thomas Bancroft, who died in Enfield, in 1684. At the end of one of these articles, Donald Lines Jacobus, one of the very best of
2 CONC  the ‘modern’ genealogists and the former editor of TAG, wrote; “So many false and improbable statements have appeared in print concerning the early Bancrofts that a careful appraisal of these claims in light of what the records a
2 CONC ctually prove (and they fail to prove very much) was long overdue ...”
2 CONT
