2 CONT ∼
2 CONT Husband of Hannah Gardner Bancroft 1650- Father of Nathan Bancroft 1683-
2 CONT Hannah Gardner was the last wife of Lieutenant Thomas Bancroft. Our ancestors is the heir of his house and property, and is listed as his only wife in his last will.
2 CONT Thier son listed here:
2 CONT Nathaniel Bancroft
2 CONT b. October 22, 1683 North Boston, Wakefield, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.
2 CONT d. 20 Jan 1753, Springfield, Hampshire) Hampden County, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT US.
2 CONT m. 19 Dec. 1687, to Elizabeth (Ruth) Hale /Heald Bancroft.
2 CONT Stowe, Middlesex, Massachusetts b. 1714 - d. aft. 1753.
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS FATHER-
2 CONT Thomas Bancroft 1622 - December 14, 1691. Born a native Englishman, in Chellaston, Derbyshire, England. Son of John Errington Bancroft 1596 - 6 August 1637 and Jane Bonython/Bonithon Bancroft 1595 - 1644. They emigrated with the P
2 CONC ilgrims in 1630, He was 5 years old. As his father died in Lynn, Essex County, Massachusetts on August 6, 1637. --Their uncle Robert Bancroft emigrated latter, and joined the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife:
2 CONT Hannah Gardner 1650 -1711 
2 CONT His only wife, listed in his will, married in Hampshire, Massachusetts on 22 November 1676. They are both buried in Wakefield, Mass. At the Old Burial Ground, First Parish Congressional Church. He had the oldest tombstone in Wakef
2 CONC ield. Where Common Burial Ground is now. He was married 22 November 1676, in Hadley, Hampshire, Massachusetts, United States, and is listed there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son: our ancestor -
2 CONT Deacon Nathaniel Bancroft, b. 22 October 1683 - d. 25 December 1752-3. Born in (or: Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut.) Died in Springfield Hampden County, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT He married Ann or Elizabeth Ruth Hale/Heald on 20 November 1708, in Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts.
2 CONT Mass Grave location.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son married Elizabeth 'Ruth'. Hale or Heald. 
2 CONT Her parents:. Gershom and Ann Hale
2 CONT Robert Bancroft when he followed His brother and relatives to the New World, he likely accompanied His relatives. And helped to protect his nieces and nephews.
