2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Frederick Saxton BIRTH	22 Mar 1748 Sheffield, Berkshire County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	28 Apr 1796 (aged 48) Shelburne, Chittenden County, Vermont, USA BURIAL	Buried or Lost at Sea, Specifically: drowned in Lake Champlain, 
2 CONC Shelburne Vermont Add to Map MEMORIAL ID	190668016 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War veteran
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents	 James Saxton, 1702–1783	 Abilene Gilbert Saxton, 1710–1774
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	 Rhoda Messenger Saxton, 1750–1813
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings	 Jasper Saxton, 1739–1798
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	 Horace Saxton, 1779–1848
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/190668016/frederick-saxton
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From Aunt Louisa's bible, Nehimiah Saxton's father was Frederich and his mother Rhoda, of Shelburn, Chittendon Co., Vermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also listed as Colonel F. Saxton, died crossing Lake Champlain to Wilsboro. Realize that "Col." was a nickname given to Frederick and that he was actually a Sergeant in Captain John Holmes' company of minutemen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently Col. Frederick Saxton was killed when a boat full of grain that he and two others were taking across lake Champlain overturned and all three men were drowned. This happened in April of 1796.
2 CONT
2 CONT (DCW)
