1 NAME John /Burbank/ IV of Suffield
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Burbank
2 NSFX IV of Suffield
2 _MARNM Burbank
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 13 MAY 1640
2 PLAC Rowley, Essex Co, Massachusetts
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 JUN 1709
2 PLAC Suffield, Hartford Co., Connecticut
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Burbanks were from Rowley, Mass., the adjoining town to Newbury.  John, Sr., lived at Haverhills, Mass., after his marriage to Susannah Merrill on Oct. 15, 1663, and removed to Suffield in 1680, being a proprie
2 CONC tor.  His wife died 16 Oct., 1690, and he married twice again to Sarah Hart in 1692 and last to Mehitable Saunders in Jan 1694. He lived at the north end of Feather Street, near the river.  His son John, husband of Mary Granger, w
2 CONC as also prominent in all town matters.  He was elected surveyror, tithingman (an important office), constable, gauger, and sealer of casks, assessor, town treasurer, and served repeatedly as selectman.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Burbank, son of John of Rowley, married Susannah  Merrill, October 15, 1663, and lived at Haverhill. He removed his wife and several children to Suffield, about 1680. His wife died October 10, 1690. Married second and third w
2 CONC ife; the last bore him a daughter " Susannah." He was a large land-holder, and much employed by Major  Pynchon in building, and clearing lands in Suffield. He was one of the few qualified voters when the Town was organized, but ne
2 CONC ver held an office. His name is found in Major  Pynchon's account book oftener than any Suffield man; and be must have been a man of business. His sons, John, Jr., and Ebenezer, were afterward prominent men in Town matters. His ho
2 CONC mestead was at the north end of Feather street. He died June 1, 1709.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Suffield, in the Colony and Province of the Massachusetts Bay, New England
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=QidMAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA58&lpg=PA58&dq=John+Caleb+Burbank,& page 58] of Descendants of John Gamage of Ipswich, Mass
2 CONT
2 CONT >2. Abraham (Reginald1) was b. in Exeter, England, 1622. He m. 1655, Lydia, daughter of Caleb and Martha Burbank of Rowley, Mass. ('Caleb Burbank was son of John, 1 of Rowley, who was freeman there May 13, 1640. In his will, made 
2 CONC April 5, 1681, he names his wife, Jemima, and children: '''John''', Caleb and Lydia - Savage.) He was sixteen years of age when he came with his father to New England. He resided in Ipswich, Mass., where he died, January 25, 1711.
2 CONC  He left no will; but divided his estate among his family by deed. He joined the Church in full communion April 12, 1674. He was 76 years of age Sept. 26, 1698, as stated in deposition concerning land of Rev. John Norton. He is ca
2 CONC lled a yeoman.
