2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy was born May 30, 1668 the son of John Burbank and Susannah Merrill of Haverhiill, Massachusetts[1] [2] [3] [4] [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family lived in Haverhill, Mass and then moved to Suffield, CT, where his brothers were prominent, however Timothy stayed in Massachusetts. In 1681, his grandfather John Burbank's 1681 will left a sum to his son John, and to h
2 CONC is son Timothy, who liveth with Captn Saltenstall, after he cometh to the age of majority, of three pounds[6]. A likely candidate for this Captain Saltonstall is Nathaniel, of Salem Witch Trial fame, whose career in the local mili
2 CONC ta eventually earned him the rank of Colonel. The other Haverhill in Saltonstalls were either the wrong age in 1681, or not involved in any business that would result in the honorific Captn.
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 3, 1695, Timothy Burbank married Rebecca Darling in Salem, Massachusetts[7] [8] [9][10], and their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane, born March 24, 1699[11] and baptized August 9, 1702[9] [10], who married John Smallage[12]
2 CONT Timothy, born 13 October 1703[13], and baptized Oct 17, 1703[9] [10], who married Mary Kempton[14]
2 CONT John, born january 19, 1704[15] and baptized Jan 21, 1704/05[9] [10], who married Elizabeth Tower[16]
2 CONT Samuel , born October 16, 1706[17] and baptized Oct 20, 1706[9] [10], who married Mary Read[18]
2 CONT Timothy Burbank died circa 1707, and his widow remarried in early 1708[10] [19]
