1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jedediah Strong Sr.=
2 CONT * BIRTH 7 May 1637 Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 22 May 1733 (aged 96) Coventry, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  36163752    Bio by Sherman-Thomas (47749330) (1/27/2018)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jedediah Strong was born May 7, 1637 at Hingham, Suffolk County, Massachusetts to John and Abigail Ford Strong. The family didn't live very long in Hingham, moving around to several settlements, and by 1646, they lived in Windsor,
2 CONC  Connecticut and by 1659, they had settled in Northampton, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. Jedediah, a farmer, married Freedom Woodward in Northampton December 18, 1662 and their children were: Abigail, Jedediah Jr., Ford (a son)
2 CONC , a daughter, Hannah, Thankful, John, Sarah, Lydia, Mary, Experience, Preserved and John (again). After the death of Freedom, Jedediah married Abigail Bartlett, widow of John Stebbins, December 28, 1681 at Northampton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a daughter, Mary, in addition to the children Abigail had with John Stebbins. From 1677 - 1679, Jedediah was paid 18 shillings a year to blow a trumpet he owned to notify the townspeople of meetings. In 1683, he was a con
2 CONC stable in Northampton. After the death of Abigail in 1689, Jedediah married Mary Hart, widow of John Lee, January 5, 1692. She had several children by John Lee, some who eventually married his children. Jedediah was father or step
2 CONC -father to 32 children. On October 10, 1710, Jedediah and Mary started out on a horseback trip from Northampton to Coventry, Connecticut to visit some of their children. Near South Hadley, Massachusetts, the horse they were riding
2 CONC  slipped on some smooth stones "near the falls", injuring Mary. She died the next morning. In 1710, Jedediah moved to Coventry, moving in with his son Preserved. He died May 22, 1733 at Coventry, Tolland County, Connecticut and is
2 CONC  possibly buried in the Nathan Hale Cemetery there, aged 96.
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT Jedediah Strong (son of Elder John Strong of Northampton and Abigail Ford) b. May 7, 1637, (and bapt. April 14, 1639), m. Nov. 18, 1662, Freedom Woodward, bapt. at Dorchester, Mass., in 1642 (dau. of Henry Woodward, afterwards of 
2 CONC Northampton, and " one of the pillars of the church," there, and Elizabeth hU wife). He was a farmer at Northampton until 1709, when at the age of 70 years and upwards he removed with his family to Coventry, Ct., where 24 years af
2 CONC terwards he d. May 22, 1733, aged 96 ; during the years 1677-8 & 9, he was paid 18 shillings a year for blowing the trumpet on Sunday to summon the people to church. His wife Freedom d. May 17, 1681, and he m. Deo. 19, 1681, for 2
2 CONC d wife Abigail Stebbins b. Sept. 6, 1660 (dau. of John Steb- bins, of Northampton, and Abigail Bartlett — dau. of Robert and Anne Bartlett, of Hartford, and afterwards of Northampton). She d. July 15, 1689, and he m. Jan. 5, 1691-
2 CONC 2, for 3d wife Mrs. Mary (Hart) Lee widow of John Lee, of Farmington, Ct., and dau. of Stephen Hart, of Farmington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived with his first wife 19 years, with his second 7, and with his third wife 9, and notwithstanding his three marriages spent 33 years as a widower, and 61 unmarried. His wife Mary d. Oct. 10,1710, from the injury which she r
2 CONC eceived the day previous, by the fall of the horse on which she was riding (on a pillion behind her husband), when just started well upon their way to Coventry, together, to visit their children. The record reads thus at Northampt
2 CONC on : " Oct. 9, 1710, Jedediah Strong, and wife set out early in the morning to visit their children, at Coventry ; but when they came against the Falls (at S. Hadley) among the broad smooth stones, the horse's feet slipped up and 
2 CONC he fell flat on the off side and by the fall killed the woman : though she was not quite dead then, but had life in her until the next day—yet never spoke a word." He was constable in 1683.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Elder John Strong Sr 1605–1699
2 CONT Abigail Ford Strong 1608–1688
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses''' [2]
2 CONT Freedom Woodward Strong 1641–1681 m. 11/18/1662
2 CONT Abigail Bartlett Stebbins 1637–1689 m. 12/28/1681
2 CONT Mary Hart Lee Strong 1630–1710 m. 1/5/1692
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Thomas Strong 1637–1689
2 CONT Return Strong 1640–1726
2 CONT Ebenezer Strong 1643–1729
2 CONT Abigail Strong Pomeroy 1645–1704
2 CONT Elizabeth Strong Parsons 1647–1736
2 CONT Experience Strong Filer 1650 – unknown
2 CONT Samuel Strong 1652–1732
2 CONT Joseph Strong 1652–1662
2 CONT Mary Strong Clark 1654–1738
2 CONT Sarah Strong Wells 1656–1733
2 CONT Hannah Strong Clark 1659–1694
2 CONT Hester Strong Bissell 1661–1726
2 CONT Thankful Strong Baldwin 1663–1726
2 CONT Jerijah Strong 1665–1754
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Half Siblings'''
2 CONT John Strong III 1631–1697
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' with Freedom 15x*, Abigail 1x**, Mary*** b. in in Northampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts
2 CONT *Elizabeth Strong Wright "twin" 1/9/1664- 2/17/1691 m. Ebenezer Wright
2 CONT *Female Strong 1/9/1664-1669 "twin"
2 CONT *Abigail Strong King 7/9/1666-7/25/1689 m. Thomas King
2 CONT *Jedediah Strong Jr 8/7/1667–10/12/1709 in Wood Creek, NY m. Abiah Ingersoll in 1692
2 CONT *Ford Strong 9/2/1668-11/1/1668 died young
2 CONT *Joseph Strong "twin" abt. 10/11/1669-1669 died young
2 CONT *Hannah Strong Carpenter 2/3/1670-3/20/1762 in Coventry, Tolland County, CT m. Benjamin Carpenter
2 CONT *Thankful Strong Root 4/15/1672–174215 m. Thomas Root (grandparents of Hon. Jessie Root
2 CONT *John Strong 11/15/ 1673-1699
2 CONT *Sarah Strong Cushman 1674–1726
2 CONT *Lydia Strong Lee 12/28/1675–7/16/1718 in Coventry, Tolland, CT m. David Lee on 9/5/1695  Northampton, MA
2 CONT *Mary 1677-1677 died in infancy
2 CONT *Experience 1678-1678 died in infancy
2 CONT *Preserved Strong 1680-1765 m.Tabitha Lee, ancestors of Capt. Nathan Hale and Lady Diana Spencer
2 CONT **Mary Stebbins Pixley m. Ebenezer Pixley
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT The photo posted on Find A Grave is NOT Jedediah Strong. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Hart Lee was Jedediah's son Preserved Strong's mother-in-law.
