1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Loomis was born at Westfield, Massachusetts or Windsor, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Burial=
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=loomis&GSfn=william&GSbyrel=all&GSdy=1820&GSdyrel=before&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=83201718&df=all& Find A Grave Memorial# 83201718]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children of William Loomis, Westfield, Mass.=
2 CONT # Martha, b. Feb. 24, 1704, d. April, 1804, œ. 100 years and 2 months, Granby, Conn.
2 CONT # Joshua, b. Aug. 24, 1706, m. Abigail Langdon April, 1735. He d. in 1779. - Joshua, son of William Loomis, was born August 24, 1706, at Westfield, and died in 1779. He married at Westfield, May 22, 1735. Abigail Langdon, who died
2 CONC  April 23, 1795, daughter of John and Abigail (Phelps) Langr'on. Children, born at Westfield: Seth, born May 22, 1737: John, December 27, 1739; Abigail. October 28, 1742; Lois, August 10, 1744: Martha. January 31, 1747; Joshua, Se
2 CONC ptember 23, 1748; Enoch, August 25, 1750; Justus, June 19. 1752; Abigail, June 30, 1754; Ann, July Id. I7?8.
2 CONT # Benjamin, b. Aug. 30, 1708, m. 1st, Elizabeth Noble, March, 1734 ; m. 2d, Rachel . He removed to Southwick, Mass., in 1773 and d. 1787.
2 CONT # Ann, b. Aug. 27, 1710.
2 CONT # William, b. Sept. 15, 1712; m. Experience Smith of Farmington Oct., 1739.
2 CONT # James, b. Nov. 15, 1714, m. Eunice Stridden Sept., 1739. He removed to Lanesboro, Mass., in 1764.
2 CONT # Thankful, b. Nov. 19, 1716.
2 CONT # Jonathan, b. Jan. 23, 1719, m. Hannah Selden of Springfield May 11, 1747. He removed to West Springfield and d. 1798.
2 CONT # Hezekiah, b. March 14, 1721, was living in 1746, an idiot.
2 CONT # Capt. Noah, b. May 12,1724, m. Rhoda Clark Nov. 5,1747, who d. Nov. 30,1806, œ. 81. He d. Aug. 9,1808, Southwick, Mass. - Captain Noah Loomis, youngest child of William and Martha (Morley) Loomis, was born in Westfield, May 12, 
2 CONC 1724, and died at Southwick, Massachusetts, August 9, 1808. He is credited with being Southwick's second settler, was selectman many times, commanded a company of minute-men at Lexington, and later enlisted in Captain Lebbens Ball
2 CONC 's company, Colonel Timothy Daniel- son's regiment. He married, November 5, 1747, Rhoda L. Clark, died November 30, 1806, aged eighty-one years, daughter of William and Abigail (Bush) Clark. Their children were all born in Westfie
2 CONC ld : Rhoda, Mercy, Tirzah, Noah, of further mention, Shem, Ham, Japhet and Grace.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Grandparents=
2 CONT * Joseph Loomis - born circa 1590, died 11/25/1658. 
2 CONT * Mary White, daughter of Robert White and Bridget Allgar, 
2 CONT * Married 30 June 1614 at Messing, County Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children of Joseph Loomis and Mary White==
2 CONT # Joseph Loomis Jr.+ b. c 1615, d. 26 Jun 1687
2 CONT # Sarah Loomis+ b. 1617
2 CONT # Elizabeth Loomis+ b. c 1619
2 CONT # Mary Loomis+ b. c 1620, d. 19 Aug 1680
2 CONT # Deacon John Loomis+ b. c 1622, d. 1 Sep 1688
2 CONT # Thomas Loomis+ b. 1624, d. 28 Aug 1689
2 CONT # Nathaniel Loomis+ b. c 1626, d. 19 Aug 1688
2 CONT # Lt. Samuel Loomis+ b. c 1628, d. 1 Oct 1689
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''Joseph Loomis'' by Elisha S. Loomis:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Joseph was a woolen-draper in Braintree, Essex county, England; sailed from London April 11, 1638, in the ship Susan and Ellen, and arrived at Boston July 17, 1638, tarrying about 1 year at Dorchester, Mass., it is thought. It is
2 CONC  mentioned in the town records of Windsor, Vol. I, that on the 2nd of Feb., 1640, he had granted him from the plantation 21 acres adjoining Farmington river, on the west side of the Connecticut river, this 21 acres including the s
2 CONC ite of the first English settlement made in Conn; also several large tracts of land on the east side of the Connecticut, partly from the town and partly by purchase.
2 CONT
2 CONT "He therefore probably came to Windsor in the summer or autumn of 1639, and he is generally supposed to have come in company with Rev. Ephraim Huet, who arrived at Windsor, Aug. 17, 1639. He brought with him five sons, all of whom
2 CONC  were freemen, Oct. 7, 1669, and three daughters. His house was situated near the mouth of the Farmington River on "The Island," so called because at every great freshet it became temporarily an island by the overflowing of the Co
2 CONC nnecticut River."
2 CONT
2 CONT =Parents=
2 CONT * Lieutenant Samuel Loomis  son of Joseph Loomis and Mary White
2 CONT * Elizabeth Judd Loomis - daughter of Thomas Judd. Elizabeth Judd
2 CONT * Married on 27 December 1653.
2 CONT
2 CONT Purchased the Witchfield place, Broad St.,, site of the present Grace church. Made freeman 1654. Moved to Westfield, Mass between 1672 and 1675. Sold his dwelling house in Windsor in 1679. Elizabeth was still living in Westfield i
2 CONC n 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children of Samuel and Elizabeth Loomis==
2 CONT #  Samuel Loomis+
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Loomis
2 CONT #  Ruth Loomis b. 14 Jun 1660
2 CONT #  Sarah Loomis b. 3 Feb 1662 or 1663
2 CONT #  Joanna Loomis b. 22 Oct 1665
2 CONT #  Benjamin Loomis b. 11 Feb 1667 or 1668, d. 1726
2 CONT #  Nehemiah Loomis b. 15 Jul 1670, d. 4 Feb 1740
2 CONT #  William Loomis+ b. 18 Mar 1672, d. 1738
2 CONT #  Philip Loomis+ b. 22 Feb 1675, d. 1 Dec 1746
2 CONT #  Mary Loomis b. 16 Aug 1678
2 CONT
2 CONT =Burial=
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Loomis&GSfn=william&GSiman=1&GSby=1700&GSbyrel=before&GSdy=1780&GSdyrel=before&GSob=n&GRid=83201718&df=all& Find A Grave Memorial# 83201718]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note''': This monument memorializes several generations of Loomis men and was obviously erected some time after William Loomis's death. It is not clear which, if any, of them are buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT # Martha born February 24 1704 died April 1804 at Granby Connecticut aged one hundred years two months 
2 CONT # Joshua married Abigail Landon ten children 
2 CONT # Benjamin born August 30 I708, removed to Southwick Massachusettts in I773 and died in 1787 He married first Elizabeth Noble in March I734 married second Rachel 
2 CONT # Anna August 27 1710 
2 CONT # William September 15 1712 married Experience Smith of Farmington four children 
2 CONT # James married Eunice Stricklen and removed to Lanesboro, Massachusetts in 1764 
2 CONT # Thankful November 19 1716 
2 CONT # Jonathan married Hannah Selden and removed to West Springfield eleven children 
2 CONT # Hezekiah March 14 1721 
2 CONT # Captain Noah May 12 1724 married Rhoda Clark died August 9 I808 in Southwick Massachusetts eight children 
