1 NOTE RFN: 21777
2 CONT LETTER re Revoulutionary War Records: 17 Oct 1933 MORLEY Notebook p
2 CONT 50.
2 CONT "He enlisted in Glastonbury, Connecticutt, in Dec 1775, and served one
2 CONT year as private in Captain Samuel Wright's company, Colonel Samuel
2 CONT Wylls' Connecticutt regiment, and was in the battle of Long Island and
2 CONT in the engagements in the vicinity of New York.
2 CONT John Morley was allowed pension on his application executed, June 1,
2 CONT 1818, at which time he was living in Bristol, Trumbull County, Ohio.
2 CONT In 1820 his wife was about sixty-six years of age, he at this time
2 CONT referred to children, one a son twenty-five years of age, he did not
2 CONT give any names. In 1823 a granddaughter, Celestina Barns, was nine
2 CONT years of age.
2 CONT Joel Morley was referred to in 1820 and John Barns to in 1823; their
2 CONT relationship tp the family not shown
