1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Capt Samuel Terry Jr.=
2 CONT * BIRTH	18 Jul 1661 Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH	2 Jan 1731 (aged 69) Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL	Enfield Street Cemetery, Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA, MEMORIAL ID 25777009, Photos by Richard Bailey & Ralph Welliver
2 CONT
2 CONT In Springfield Mass he held at times such local offices as constable, and selectman.  He was several years the ensign of the local militia and became captain of it in 1716.  "He was a man of exemplary piety, prominent in the churc
2 CONC h and is styler 'gentleman' in the public record of his appointment as administrator of his father's estate.  He lived in Enfiedl and his main occupation was that of a farmer.   CBW Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT First married Hannah Morgan 17 May 1682 and had four children; Hannah, Samuel, Rebecca and Ebenezer. Hannah died 17 Jan 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, married Martha Boardman, the daughter of Samuel and widow of Benjamin Crane Jr. They were married 04 Jan 1698 and had st least two children: Benjamin Terry (who married Hannah Pease and fathered Submit Terry and Jacob Te
2 CONC rry)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT Here lyes the
2 CONT Body of Capt.
2 CONT Samuel Terry Who
2 CONT Deceafed Janr. 2nd
2 CONT 1730/1 in ye 70th
2 CONT Year of his Age
