2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Here lyes the
2 CONT Body of Capt.
2 CONT Samuel Terry Who
2 CONT Deceafed Janr. 2nd
2 CONT 1730/1 in ye 70th
2 CONT Year of his Age
2 CONT
2 CONT On the day Capt. Samuel died he was 69 years old, and Ætatis suæ (i.e., Æ, "Aged," in the XX year of his Age) 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note
2 CONT Samuel B Terry is the Great Great Great Grandfather of Charles Carroll Terry who is one of the founders of Seattle Washington.  He was part of the Denny party and started the first store in Alki which is now West Seattle
