2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Buell was born in 1740 in CT to Samuel and Ann Buell. He married Sarah Holmes July 3 1760. Sarah Holmes died 29 July 1772, 19 days after the birth of Ichabod, so probably childbed fever. The Buell family history lists her f
2 CONC ather as Israel Holmes of Litchfield, but the History of Yates Co. states she was the daughter of Peleg Holmes of Kent, CT. The History of Yates County reports Samuel moved to Benton in 1792, was a soldier during the last French a
2 CONC nd Indian war, was a Captain in the Revolution, and served at Fort Edward, where his son Cyrus was captured by the British. He married 2nd to Susan Morse.
2 CONT
2 CONT His grandson Elias Buell wrote that Samuel was born in Hebron CT, moved to Kent Ct with his father in 1758 and after his father died, Samuel sold his inheritence, married Sarah and moved to Ft. Edward in May 1763. Elias had a rawh
2 CONC ide bound record that Samuel kept, which recorded the death of his father, his marriage, and the birth of the children with Sarah:
2 CONT Sarah, b. May 7 1761 Samuel, b. Oct. 7, 1763 (father of Elias) Samuel Buell
2 CONT
2 CONT Cyrus, b. Sep 26 1765 Polina, b. Apr. 14, 1768 Betsy, b. May 19, 1770 Ichabod, b. July 10, 1772
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Sarah died July 29, 1772. After Samuel married Susan Morse, he recorded two births Henry, b. Dec 24, 1774; d. 1790 Catherine, b. Sep 7, 1776. Susan (Morse) Buell died in Chautauqua Co NY, with Elias' Aunt Matilda Bunnell.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Revolutionary War, he raised a volunteer troop for Ft. Ann, serving as a Captain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Buell was born on month day 1740, at birth place, Connecticut, to Joseph Buell and Anna Submit Buell (born Colton). Joseph was born on August 24 1710, in Killingworth, New London County, Connecticut Colony. Anna was born on
2 CONC  September 13 1714, in Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts. Samuel had 13 siblings: Molly Buell, Judith Buell and 11 other siblings. Samuel married Sarah Buell (born Holmes). Sarah was born on May 1 1742, in Plympton, Plymouth, Ma
2 CONC ssachusetts, USA. They had 6 children: Samuel Holmes Buell, Betsey Bennett (born Buell) and 4 other children. Samuel married Unknown. They had 8 children: Esther Buel, Catharine Buell and 6 other children. Samuel passed away on mo
2 CONC nth day 1809, at age 68 at death place, New York. He was buried at burial place, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
