1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There was a family tradition in our family that we were somehow related to the Revolutionary War hero Ethan Allen.  It is through Naomi's sister Sarah that this connection exists, however distant.  Sarah was a sist
2 CONC er-in-law to Ethan Allen having married Heber Allen.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/17855303/naomi-soper
2 CONT
2 CONT Naomi Owen Soper BIRTH	17 Mar 1751 DEATH	10 Apr 1836 (aged 85) Vermont, USA BURIAL	 Miltonboro Cemetery Milton, Chittenden County, Vermont, USA MEMORIAL ID	17855303 · View Source SHARE  SAVE TOSUGGEST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWE
2 CONC RS 6 wife of Mordecai Soper (married: 4 Apr 1770 in Salisbury Connecticut)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Mordcai is buried in Milton Village in the Plains Cemetery)
2 CONT
2 CONT Naomi was the daughter of Elijah and Patience (Wright) Owen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Elizabeth Soper 16 Oct 1770 in Salisbury, Connecticut
