2 CONT Name Meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT Chapin
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry
2 CONT French and Spanish: from Old French eschapin, Spanish chapín ‘type of overshoe made of cork’, applied as a nickname for someone who habitually wore this type of footwear or a metonymic occupational name for someone who made them.
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT English: variant of Chopin , more commonly surviving in England as Chopping and Chappin.
2 CONT Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006.
