1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Had ten sons and three daughters, nine of whom lived to be more than three score and ten, and five sons lived on farms practically adjoining the homestead. (NEB genealogy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Chapin (1677), the fourth son of Japhet, married 1 Dec. 1702, Ruth Janes. They lived in Enfield and Sorners, Conn. and he had thirteen children, nine of whom lived to more than three score years and ten. Five sons lived i
2 CONC n the same town with their father, at Somers, their farms adjoining. It is not surprising that their community was called Chapinville. Ruth Janes Chapin, however, died 18 Jan. 1736, and Ebenezer remarried; consequently not all of 
2 CONC these 13 were her children. The father died 13 Dec. 1772, and was buried at Enfield. (NEB genealogy)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
