1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bliss-114
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bliss was born about 1635, in England, son of Thomas Bliss and Margaret Hulings Bliss.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1638 Immigration
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration: 1638, Came to America with his brother (and presumably his parents). [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1667 Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Patience Burt on Oct 07, 1667 in Tauton, Springfield, Massachusetts, daughter of Henry Burt and Eulalia Marche.She was born Aug 18, 1645 in Springfield, Massachusetts, and died Oct 25, 1732 in Springfield, Massachusetts
2 CONC . [4][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1688 House in Northampton for sister
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1688 John built a house in Northampton Massachusetts for his sister Mary (Bliss) Parsons. In 1981 the structure was owned by the Northampton Historical Society. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bliss died Sep 20, 1702 in Longmeadow, Massachusetts.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried in the Springfield Cemetery in Springfield.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Bliss and Patience Burt are: [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Son or Son Bliss, born 1668.
2 CONT # Child Bliss, born Sep 08, 1668; died Sep 20, 1668.
2 CONT # John Bliss, born Sep 07, 1669 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Sep 20, 1747 in Lebanon, Connecticut. John Needs to be merged into this!
2 CONT # Nathaniel Bliss, born Jan 26, 1671 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Mar 12, 1750 in Lebannon, Connecticut.
2 CONT # Thomas Bliss, born Oct 29, 1673 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Aug 12, 1758.
2 CONT # Joseph Bliss, born 1676 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Mar 01, 1754.
2 CONT # Hannah Bliss, born Nov 16, 1678 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Jul 26, 1760. On May 242, 1705 she married Henry Wright; born Jan 06, 1677; died 1769.
2 CONT # Henry Bliss, born Aug 15, 1681 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Nov 30, 1684.
2 CONT # Ebenezer or Ebenezer Bliss, born 1683 in Springfield, Massachusetts; died Nov 04, 1761 in Springfield, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
