1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nathaniel Dewey''' was born on 20 February 1673 in Westfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts to parents Josiah Dewey and Hepzibah Lyman. He had a twin brother, Ebenezer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Burroughs on 24 January 1699 in Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children, all born in Lebanon:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Nathaniel, b. 12 December 1700
2 CONT # Margaret, b. 5 May 1702; m. Cornelius Phelps on 18 January 1721/2 in Lebanon, ''possibly'' in the portion that later became Hebron
2 CONT # Samuel, b. 5 July 1704; m. Elizabeth Allen on 6 March 1732 in Lebanon
2 CONT # Noah, b. 13 May 1706
2 CONT # Sarah, b. 2 August 1709
2 CONT # Thomas, b. 20 January 1713
2 CONT # Hepzibah, b. 28 December 1715
2 CONT # Tamer, b. 20 October 1717; m. Ebenezer Wright on 8 November 1739 in Lebanon; d. 22 March 1741, likely during or related to birth of son ''-- listed as "Tamor" at birth and "Tamer" thereafter, except for being listed as "Tamar" i
2 CONC n a published family history''
2 CONT
2 CONT Neither Nathaniel nor Margaret has a death record in Lebanon. Additionally, the Daughters of the American Revolution do not endorse a date or place of death for either.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
