2 CONT Born 1675 Dec Springfield, MA
2 CONT Died 1733 Oct 21 Springfield, MA
2 CONT Married
2 CONT Abigail Phelps in 1697 North Hampton, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT *************************
2 CONT SECOND marriage 1676 Feb 21 Springfield, MA
2 CONT Sarah Heald or Hale Leonard Parsons TILTON
2 CONT (she first married John Leonard)
2 CONT Sarah Died 1711 Nov 23
2 CONT Sarah's third marriage 1690 Nov 3 Springfield,was to Deacon Peter Tilton of Hadley MA
2 CONT *************************
2 CONT Timeline
2 CONT Birth 1625 1 May
2 CONT Beaminster, Dorset, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration, perhaps with brother Joseph
2 CONT 1651
2 CONT Age: 26
2 CONT first record Nov 4-1651 at Springfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIRST Marriage to Sarah Vore
2 CONT 1653 6 Oct
2 CONT Age: 28
2 CONT Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT Father Richard Vore, Mother Ann of Windsor, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1656 Benjamin testifies for his sister-in-law Mary Bliss, accused by Sarah Bridgman of being a witch.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1669 Jan 14 Benjamin owns a grant of 30 acres in Enfield, CT. Also has land grant at Stony River-Suffield, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1670 Oct Benjamin along with John Pynchon and others petitioned General Court of Mass for the plantation of Suffield, CT. Also served on the committee of Springfield men to layout and establish town of Longmeadow.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1676 Jan 15 wife Sarah Vore dies
2 CONT
2 CONT SECOND Marriage to Sarah Heald or Hale (widow of John Leonard)
2 CONT 1677 21 Feb
2 CONT Age: 51
2 CONT Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1679 Aug 14 A member of a committee of five appointed by town of Springfield to manage the corners of the proposed plantation at the Falls and at Freshwater (Enfield, CT)
2 CONT 1679 Dec 3 Committee grants a home & out lots to Benjamin Parsons
2 CONT
2 CONT 1689 Benjamin granted a tract of land for erection of a saw mill at Scantick
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamins Will
2 CONT 1689 20 Feb
2 CONT Age: 62
2 CONT probated March 30 1690
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin died 1689 Aug 24
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandsons
2 CONT 1688
2 CONT Age: 63
2 CONT John Parsons, John & James Dorchester, Benjamin & John Munn and John Richards.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons Benjamin, Samuel, Joseph, Ebenezer and Hezekiah.
2 CONT Daus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death 1689 24 Aug
2 CONT Age: 64
2 CONT Springfield, Hampden, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT Title
2 CONT (Deacon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Parsons:
2 CONT MARRIAGE: Mr. Parsons md. (1) Sarah Vore, dau of Richard of Windsor, who was a member of the Rev. John Warham's church in Dorchester, and accompanied him to Windsor in 1635. She d. at Springfield 1 Jan 1676; He md. 2nd Sarah, reli
2 CONC ct of John Leonard in 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: Deacon Parsons d. 24 Aug 1689. Benjamin Parsons' will (Probate Records at Northampton, Vol. 1, page. 269) mentions grandsons John Parsons, John Dorchester, James Dorchester, Benjamin Munn, John Munn, John Richards.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Younger brother of Cornet Joseph Parsons; was among the first settlers of Springfield; prominent citizen and a gentleman of exemplary moral character; of great worth and respectability. He was Deacon of the church and a
2 CONC  chief instrument in its formation in Springfield as appears from his correspondence with the Rev. Dr. Increase Mather. In the civil affairs of the town, no one held more responsible offices, or discharged them with greater fideli
2 CONC ty.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Parsons in the Massachusetts, Town and Vital Records, 1620-1988
2 CONT Name: Benjamin Parsons
2 CONT Event Type: Death
2 CONT Death Date: 29 Aug 1689
2 CONT Death Place: Springfield, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon Benjamin Parsons was baptized 1625 May 1 at St. Mary's Church in Beaminster, Dorset, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/112010978/benjamin-parsons
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Springfield Records Benjamin arrived in Springfield in 1651, resided in Springfield 38 years until his death 1689. Appointed 4 Nov 1651 fence viewer in Springfield, MA.
2 CONT
