1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54533539/hannah_hitchcock
2 CONT ___
2 CONT
2 CONT HANNAH CHAPIN, b. December 02, 1644, Springfield, Hampden, MA; d. May 21, 1719; m. JOHN HITCHCOCK, September 27, 1666; b. September 27, 1642, Springfield, Hampden, MA; d. February 09, 1711/12, Springfield, Hampden, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for HANNAH CHAPIN:
2 CONT
2 CONT COMMENTS: This couple had 9 children, all born in Springfield. Six grew to adulthood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah's Father, Deacon Samuel Chapin lived on the home lot next south of the Ministry lot in the centre of the then village of Springfield. His son Japhet owned one half of said premises, but sold his right therein (by deed beari
2 CONC ng date November 19, 1667) to Deacon John Hitchcock, who had married said Japhet's sister Hannah 
2 CONT
