1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Notes for JOHN HITCHCOCK:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hitchcock received a Lieutenant's commission after being shot at Turners Falls. 
2 CONT
2 CONT DEACON JOHN2 HITCHCOCK (Luke1) son of Luke and Elizabeth (Gibbons) Hitchcock, married Sept. 27, 1666, Hannah Chapin, dau. of Dea. Samuel and Cicily Chapin of the Plantation of Norwottuck. She was born Dec. 2, 1644. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a record of June, 1655 that John Hitchcock received some land from his Uncle William Gibbons of Hartford, who is called in Hartford records a "London Merchant." "In order of Seating in the Meeting House, Feb. 23, 1662, Ol
2 CONC d Style, John Hitchcocke was put In ye Backer Seate above the Pillars on the North Side." He was sworn constable of Springfield in 1672. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1676, May 19, he was wounded in the fight at Turner's Falls, one arm shot through and the other broken. Major Pynchon solicited the Governor to give Ensign John Hitchcock a lieutenant's commission for gallant conduct. He was Fr
2 CONC eeman in 1682. In 1686, Nov. 9, he was one of a committee for the "settlement of the town of Quaboag," now Brookfield; and in 1688 he was with five others sent to the relief of Brookfield and also "to make fortifications in Quaboa
2 CONC g." He was a deacon in the church at Springfield. He died Feb. 9, 1712. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS CHILDREN WERE: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i. DAUGHTER3, b. and d. Sept. 4, 1667. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. ii. HANNAH, b. Sept. 10, 1668; m. Samuel Parsons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. iii. JOHN, b. April 13, 1670; m. Mary Ball. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. iv. SAMUEL, b. Aug. 21, 1672; m. Sarah Weller. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. v. LUKE, b. March 23, 1674--5; m. Elizabeth Walker. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. vi. NATHANIEL, b. Aug. 28, 1677; m. Abigail Lombard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. vii. DAVID, b. Feb. 7, 1678--9; m. 1st, Wid. Elizabeth Batt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. JONATHAN, b. Nov. 26, 1682; d. Feb. 26, 1683--4. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ix. SARAH, b. Jan 11, 1686--7; d. April 17, 1690. 
2 CONT
2 CONT . 
2 CONT
