1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT if you insist on adding JR as a suffix, we need the plain John Hitchcock as alternative spelling, so we can find possible duplicates and sources.  And I KNOW there were a lot more alternate spellings for John Hitchcock,  where did
2 CONC  they go?
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT John Hitchcock, Jr. was the son of John and Hannah (Chapin) Hitchcock. He married Mary Ball, the daughter of Samuel and Mary (Graves) Ball, on September 24, 1691 in Springfield, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary had 11 known children: John III, Mary (died young), Sarah, Mercy, Mary, Abigail, Nathaniel, Thankful, Jerusha, Margaret and Samuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === His will was proved in 1781. ===
2 CONT His will was proved in 1781.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Extra children ===
2 CONT Page 213 of the attached book "The genealogy of the Hitchcock family" shows that there are only 11 children instead of 14.  Can someone confirm this?
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === !1.  Hitchcock Genealogy, A6, c8, pp 211 ===
2 CONT !1.  Hitchcock Genealogy, A6, c8, pp 211 No. 3 2.  Marr:  From IGI, 1988;  orignal Sl-s, 14 Sep 1948 SL. 3.  sub by Emma P. Walton, Centerville, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === GEDCOM line 5168 not recognizable or too ===
2 CONT GEDCOM line 5168 not recognizable or too long: (SLGC) 2 FAMC @F308@
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ===  John Hitchcock was English. ===
2 CONT John Hitchcock was English.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === MarDee's genealogy -- Ped 10 - M  #2 -- John Hitchcock  L7JR-D92 ===
2 CONT MarDee Adams  genealogy -- pedigree 10 -M  #2 --   7 ggf -- John Hitchcock L7JR-D92 Also known as Ensign John Hitchcock  or John Hitchcock Jr.
2 CONT
