1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/242620971/samuel_hitchcock
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of the Towns of New Milford and Bridgewater, Connecticut, 1703-1882 by Samuel Orcutt
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 47 The "First Church of Christ" was organized by the council on the day of the ordination of Mr. Boardman, and gave the call to the minister, which he accepted, and the ordination followed. The record Mr. Boardman made of the o
2 CONC rganization of the church is thus rendered:
2 CONT
2 CONT "New Milford, Nov. 21, 1716. An account of the Bretheren of the church at the first settlement of the ministry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recommended ye Planters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Boardman, John Bostwick, Samuel Brownson, Zacariah Ferris, Samuel Beebe, Samuel Hitchcock, John Weller, Roger Brownson
2 CONT
2 CONT Female Members Mary Noble, widow, Sarah Hitchcock; ye wife of Samuel Hitchcock, Hannah Beebe, ye wife of Samuel Beebe, Recommended from Danbury
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Brownson, ye wife of Samuel Brownson, Dorcas Brownson, ye wife of Roger Brownson
2 CONT
2 CONT "Quickly was added to the church, by admission, and recommendation to the Church Communion,
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Buck, James Prime, Ann Prime, ye wife of James Prime, Recommended from Milford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oct. 19, 1718, William Gaylor, Johannah Gaylor, ye wife of William Gaylor, recommended from Woodbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Elizabeth Harris, ye wife of William Harris, recommended from Wethersfield "Mercy Bostwick, ye wife of John Bostwick, recommended from the church of Danbury "Rebecca Weller, ye wife of John Weller, admitted Oct. 19, 1718.
2 CONT
