1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ebenezer Barnard BIRTH	13 Mar 1696, Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	20 Jul 1764 (aged 68), Hadley, Hampshire County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Old Deerfield Burying Ground, Deerfield, Franklin Cou
2 CONC nty, Massachusetts, USA, MEMORIAL ID 43335989
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by the moo &  Ellen Johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT Born c.1695 to Joseph and Sarah (nee Strong) Barnard of Northampton, Ebenezer Barnard, a native of colonial Connecticut, died "in ye 68th Year of his Age". On February 29, 1715-16, when he was approximately 20 years old, he marrie
2 CONC d his first wife, Elizabeth Foster, the daughter of James and Ann (nee Lane) Foster of Dorchester. Nine children were born to the couple: Joseph, Ebenezer Jr., Samuel, Abner, Selah, Rebecca Barnard Saxton, Elizabeth Barnard Frary,
2 CONC  Anna Foster Barnard, and Lemuel. Two died before reaching adulthood: Ebenezer Jr. at age 17, and Anna at age 11. Mr. Bernard's wife Elizabeth, who was 59 at the time of her death, predeceased him by almost 11 years. He later died
2 CONC  in Hadley, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents	 Joseph Barnard, 1652–1695	 Sarah Strong Wells, 1656–1733
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses	 Elizabeth Foster Barnard, 1695–1753 (m. 1715)	 Mary Hitchcock Barnard, 1695–1781 (m. 1754)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings	 John Barnard, 1676–1726 Sarah Barnard Wells, 1677–1754 Joseph Barnard, 1681–1736	 Samuel Barnard, 1684–1762	 Hannah Barnard Childs, 1685–1727 Abigail Barnard Wells, 1691–1772	 Thankful Barnard Sheldon, 1694–1746
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	 Joseph Barnard, 1716–1785	 Ebenezer Barnard, 1719–1736	 Samuel Barnard, 1721–1788	 Abner Barnard, 1724–1797	 Salah Barnard, 1725–1795	 Rebecca Barnard Sexton, 1726–1803	 Anna Foster Barnard, 1733–1744	 Lemuel Barnard, 17
2 CONC 35–1817
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT Momento Mori In memory of Mr. EBENEZER BARNARD who Dec'd July ye 20th AD 1764 in ye 68th  Year of his Age
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43335989/ebenezer-barnard
2 CONT ----------------
