2 CONT Her elegant form, her noble and benignant countenance, her kind manners and gentle tones, and even her white dimity dress and black mantle, were well and long remembered (p. 86).     She had the rare merit of daring to be singular
2 CONC , more mild  and  more  uniformly  genial,  with  more  blandness  of  manner  and  much more  tact  than  her  husband,  she  was  equally  brave  and  determined. ("The New England Minister of Sixty Years Ago," by Rev. Sereno D.
2 CONC  Clark, Boston, 1877, pp. 80-90.) 
2 CONT
