1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "History of Enfield, CT" by Francis O. Allen. Kathren Munro: Father was Jonathan Bush. He was a Wheelwright. His children quitclaimed their rights in the estate of their Grandfather, Jonathan Bush. He married Rache
2 CONC l Kibbe, of Enfield, February 17, 1708. Children born at Enfield: Jonathan-May 2, 1710; Joshua-August 17, 1712; Moses-1714; Miriam-1715; Aaron-August 18, 1717; Rachel-May 30, 1722; Caleb-August 7, 1725; Elizabeth-January 12, 1727;
2 CONC  Mary-June 13, 1730.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bush-2855
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Bush
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 10 Apr 1681 in Springfield, Hampshire, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Jonathan Bush and Sarah (Lamb) Bush
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Bush and Sarah (Bush) Kibbe
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Rachel (Kibbe) Meacham — married 17 Feb 1708 in Enfield, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Jonathan Bush, Moses Bush, Aaron Bush, Miriam (Bush) Hale, Caleb Bush and Elizabeth (Bush) Hale
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 28 Feb 1746 in Enfield, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 28 Sep 2019 | Created 27 Mar 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Bush was born at Springfield, Massachusetts (just north of Enfield) on April 10, 1681 to Jonathan Bush and Sarah Lamb.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan and Rachel 'Keebee' were married at Enfield on February 17, 1708/9.[2] They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan, b. May 2, 1710 at Enfield[3] Joshua, b. August 17, 1712 at Enfield[4] Moses, b. December 8, 1714 at Enfield[5] Aaron, b. August 18, 1717 (recorded at Enfield about 1740)[6] Miram, b. about 1720 (see below)[7] Rachel, b. 
2 CONC May 30, 1722 at Enfield[8] Caleb, b. August 28, 1725 at Enfield[9] Elizabeth, b. January 12, 1727/8 at Enfield[10][11] Mary, b. June 13, 1730 at Enfield[12] He died at Enfield, February 28 1745/6,[13] or March 1, 1745/6.[14] The i
2 CONC nscription on his gravestone reads:[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT Here lies interred the Body of Mr Jona than Buſh he Fineſh ed his Peſſabe and Examplery life Febr. ye 28, 1746 in the 65 year of his age. That is, “He feneshed his Pessabel (peaceable) and exemplary life Febry. ye 28th 1746 in the
2 CONC  65th year of his life.”.
2 CONT
2 CONT A deed dated 1749 (recorded in Volume 3 of Enfield land records) records a sale of land where the sellers are: Jonathan Bush, Joshua Bush, Moses Bush, Aaron Bush, Caleb Bush, Richard French jur and his wife Miriam, John French and
2 CONC  his wife Rachel, Job Larkham and his wife Mary, and Elizabeth Bush, spinster, land at Enfield on the common right of "our grandfather Jonathan Bush decd".[15] This shows that Miriam, listed in order of eldest children, was Jonath
2 CONC an's oldest daughter, and born in the gap between Aaron (whose birth record itself was recorded 23 years after the fact) and Rachel.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel married 2 Lieutenant John Meacham.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a wheelwright by trade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
