2 CONT Profile last modified 26 Sep 2019 | Created 28 Mar 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Kibbe was born at Enfield on April 17, 1688 to Elisha 'Kebbe'.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel 'Keebee' and Jonathan Bush were married at Enfield on February 17, 1708/9.[2] They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan, b. May 2, 1710 at Enfield[3] Joshua, b. August 17, 1712 at Enfield[4] Moses, b. December 8, 1714 at Enfield[5] Aaron , b. August 18, 1717 (recorded at Enfield about 1740)[6] Miram, b. about 1720 (see below)[7] Rachel, b.
2 CONC  May 30, 1722 at Enfield[8] Caleb, b. August 28, 1725 at Enfield[9] Elizabeth, b. January 12, 1727/8 at Enfield[10] Mary, b. June 13, 1730 at Enfield[11] A deed dated 1749 (recorded in Volume 3 of Enfield land records) records a s
2 CONC ale of land where the sellers are: Jonathan Bush, Joshua Bush, Moses Bush, Aaron Bush, Caleb Bush, Richard French jur and his wife Miriam, John French and his wife Rachel, Job Larkham and his wife Mary, and Elizabeth Bush, spinste
2 CONC r, land at Enfield on the common right of "our grandfather Jonathan Bush decd".[12] This shows that Miriam, listed in order of eldest children, was Jonathan's oldest daughter, and born in the gap between Aaron (whose birth record 
2 CONC itself was recorded 23 years after the fact) and Rachel.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan died 1746. Rachel remarried Lieutenant John Meacham on April 19, 1758 at Enfield. [13]
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on January 13, 1786 at Enfield, and was buried there. The inscription on her tombstone reads:[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT In Memory of Mrs Rachel Meachem formerly wife of Mr Jonathan Buſh who died Jany 13th 1786 in the 100th year of her Age Sources
