1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Peck-799
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Peck was born Jan 4 1670 to Benjamin Peck and Mary Sperry, daughter of Richard Sperry and Denise Goodyear, in New Haven, CT[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin married Mary Sperry on May 2 1700 in in Derby, Connecticut. Mary Sperry was born Jan 16 1679 to John Sperry and Elizabeth Post, his first cousin, in New Haven, CT. She died 6 March 1728 [2][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Since his parents were same names as Benjamin and his wife, this has created a lovely genealogical confusion for future generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin and Mary had ten children [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Dinah
2 CONT # Elizabeth
2 CONT # Joseph
2 CONT # Mary
2 CONT # Benjamin
2 CONT # John
2 CONT # Ebenezer
2 CONT # Jonathan
2 CONT # Daniel
2 CONT # Submit
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Norwich, CT, which is now Franklin, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin died Mar 3 1722[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He is buried with his wife Mary, in Plains Cemetery, Franklin, New London, CT. [6]. Benjamin donated the 1st piece of land for Plains Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
