1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 6 Oct 2000  From:   "Lorraine Eachus" <LorraineE@worldnet.att.net> To: <olsalte@aol.com> My mother-in-law's grandmother is Irene Sterns Noble (not Boyd), daughter of Sexton Noble and Lavina Fish which you have in your lineage.  Ho
2 CONC wever, our family has her birthday as December 1, 1873 and death 12/2/1946. Further, she did not marry Arthur H. Noble, she married William B. Yerkes (8/12/1870-4/13/19??) and from that marriage she only had two children, a daught
2 CONC er Elizabeth Helene Yerkes (8/31/1895-4/1986), my mother-in-law's mother and a son Warren Yerkes.   Irene did have a sister, Nancy that married a brother of Thomas Boyd. Whoever married Arthur H. Noble right now is the question. T
2 CONC he children you list for Arthur Noble and Irene Stearns Boyd are cousins in the Noble family somewhere.  My mother-in-law says the family is very difficult to follow because the Damascus area had two Noble families and she says sh
2 CONC e has Noble's on both sides of her lineage.  I now see that Warren Yerkes is also in your family lineage. This is my husband's lineage thru his mother: .......Spencer C Noble ...Barbara J. Noble Eachus ..........................Jo
2 CONC seph W. Yerkes ...................Warren D Yerkes ..........................Elizabeth Burcher ..............William B Yerkes ....................Margaret Mitchell .......Elizabeth Helene Yerkes ..........................Sexton Nob
2 CONC le ................Irene Sterns Noble ..........................Lavina Fish Spencer W. Eachus
2 CONT
2 CONT My mother-in-law has given me an old medical book published in 1655 that was owned by Elizabeth Burcher way back 1792-1874.  Although tattered, it is still in decent condition considering its age.
2 CONT
2 CONT The below dates are fact.  Barbara Jean Noble (my mother-in-law), is daughter to Elizabeth Helene Yerkes and Spencer C. Noble and had just sent me a copy of her tree and I was trying to find some missing dates that she didn't have
2 CONC , specifically Lavina's death. Her mother was steeped in family geneology and had passed all kinds of memorabilia down to her including clothing articles and letters, etc. making her promise never to get rid of them.  Now she is i
2 CONC n a quandary of what to do with it since she is 80 and will need to downsize from her house in Virginia - hopefully nearer to us in Savannah, GA.   William B. Yerkes (her grandfather, son of Warren D. Yerkes & Margaret Mitchell) a
2 CONC nd his dates are 8/12/1870 - 4/13/19?? - Mom wasn't sure of death year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irene Sterns Noble 12/1/1873-12/2/1946 (her grandmother, daughter of Sexton Noble 1825-1898 & Lavina Fish (1831-??) married to William B. Yerkes in 1894 had two children.  That being Elizabeth Helene Yerkes b. 8/31/1895, d. 4/1986
2 CONC ,  (m. 4/19/1918 to Spencer C. Noble b.3/22/1894, d.10/10/1971 Honesdale, PA) and Warren Yerkes.  This last Warren Yerkes is dead now but the family farm in Damascus is still in his family owned by his son and grandson who my moth
2 CONC er refers to as Bill and young Bill. The only dates Mom said she might question were Lavina Fish.  The below dates are in Beers 1900 Reference.  Sexton Noble pp 38,39,680
2 CONT
2 CONT All the information given to me was passed down to my mother-in-law. She has additional records that are contained in a soft bound book about the families from Damascus and Calkins.    he was a lumberman & a farmer
2 CONT
