1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Descendants of Elder William Brewster, Part 1, Generations 1 through 4, Barbara Lambert Merrick, General Society of Mayflower Descendants, Plymouth MA, 2014, p. 124
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The tree for Susannah Turner (Keeney) continues [http://www.geni.com/family-tree/index/6000000003938484344#6000000000543553695 here].
2 CONT
2 CONT May have been married multiple times am seeing another husband   Joseph Miner
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT : Birth 06 SEP 1662 New London, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT : Marriage 26 DEC 1678 Stonington, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT : Husband:  [[Turner-4152|Ezekiel Turner]]
2 CONT : Wife:  [[Keeney-210|Susanna Keeney]]
2 CONT : Child:  [[Turner-4153|Grace Turner]]
2 CONT Susannah Keeney, the daughter of [[Keeney-209|John Keeney]] and [[Douglas-1540|Sarah Douglas]], was born in New London, Connecticut on September 6, 1662.≤ref>''Connecticut: Vital Records. New London Births-Marriages-Deaths 1646-18
2 CONC 54. Barbour Collection.'' Connecticut State Library, 1919. p. 175, citing New London Records Vol. 1, p. 3. [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB414/i/12577/175/0 Link to page at americanancestors.org].≤/ref>≤ref name="Caulkins">Ca
2 CONC ulkins, Frances Manwaring. "History of New London, Connecticut". H.D. Utley, 1895. p. 291. [https://archive.org/stream/historyofnewlond00caul#page/290/mode/2up Link to page at archive.org].≤/ref> She was baptized in New London on 
2 CONC February 26, 1670.≤ref>''Connecticut Church Records. Index. New London First Congregational Church 1670-1888.'' Connecticut State Library, 1949. p. 242. [https://www.ancestry.com/sharing/28765058?h=ec2aa0 Link to image of page].≤/
2 CONC ref>
2 CONT Susannah married, first, Ezekiel Turner, of Scituate, born 7 January 1651, baptized 19 January 1650/1, died 16 January 1704 in New London, Connecticut.  They married in New London, Connecticut, on 26 December 1678.≤ref>''Connectic
2 CONC ut: Vital Records. New London Births-Marriages-Deaths 1646-1854. Barbour Collection.'' Connecticut State Library, 1919. p. 175, citing New London Records Vol. 1, p. 14. [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB414/i/12577/175/0 Link t
2 CONC o page at americanancestors.org].≤/ref>
2 CONT Susanna married, second, in New London, as his second wife, 20 August 1706, Joseph Minor.≤ref>''Connecticut: Vital Records. New London Births-Marriages-Deaths 1646-1854. Barbour Collection.'' Connecticut State Library, 1919. p. 21
2 CONC 3, citing New London Records Vol. 1, p. 52. [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB414/i/12577/213/0 Link to page at americanancestors.org].≤/ref> Joseph was born in New London 6 August 1666, died there Monday 6 April 1752, aged 86 
2 CONC years, son of Clement and Francis (Burcham)(Willey) Miner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna died in New London 13 December 1748.  
2 CONT In 1679, Ezekiel was a sailor with Master Thomas Simond when the bark Providence  was wrecked on a rock near Fisher’s Island, according to his deposition dated November 29th.  Ezekiel Turner died intestate.  The inventory of his e
2 CONC state was taken 11 May 1704 and amountedto 217 pounds, 10 shillings, 6 pence.  Administration of the estate was granted to widow Susanna and on 9 November 1705 she posted bond with Richard Christophers as Surety.  On 1 October 170
2 CONC 6, Susanna Minor, Relict of Ezekiel Turner,” presented her accounting of the estate.
2 CONT On 12 March 1706/7, the Court ordered a division of the “Real and personal estate of Ezekiel Turner, late of New London, deceased.”  The said real estate contained a “Lott formerly belonging to William Nichols, [and] was, by a dee
2 CONC d of Gift, given by John Keney of New London to his son and Daughter, Ezekiel Turner, and their heirs for ever . . .”  On 17 June 1707, Susanna (now Susanna Minor, wife of Joseph Minor), claimed the lot and the Court ordered the “
2 CONC use, benefitand profit of said Lott be to said Susanna during her life . . .” and it was taken out of the inventory. 
2 CONT An addition was made to the inventory on 20 June 1707, recording “several things delivered by the deceased to Jonathan Calkins andto Adam Pickett, as part of his wives portions.”  Division of the remaining estate of Ezekiel Turner
2 CONC  was made 25 November 1707, and recorded 29 November 1707, to widow Susanna (1/3), son Ezekiel (double portion), and the other eleven children, with each child named in the order of their recorded birth.
2 CONT Ezekiel Turner and Susanna Kenney had the following children:≤ref>Barbara Lambert Merrick, Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol 24 Part 1, The Descendants of Elder William Brewster, General Society of Mayflower Descend
2 CONC ants, 2014. "The Silver Book" Page 207-208≤/ref>≤ref>Some additional  unsourced data* from [https://web.archive.org/web/20111006175224/http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~legends/turner.html Rootsweb page: Turner of Plymouth, 
2 CONC last updated 23 May 2000] (Link via Wayback Machine, capture date 06 Oct 2011)≤/ref>
2 CONT *Sarah Turner, baptized 3 Dec. 1682; died young
2 CONT *[[Turner-1844|Sarah Turner]], b. 28 Oct 1683; m. Jonathan Caulkins*[[Turner-301|Susanna Turner]], b. 2 Jan. 1685; died after 1710; married first, Adam Pickett; married second, Samuel Fosdick* (Adam and Samuel were both grandsons 
2 CONC of John Pickett and Ruth Brewster, sister of John Turner’s wife Mary Brewster, thus she married two of her cousins in succession).
2 CONT *[[Turner-48349|Mary Turner]], b. 30 May 1686; living 25 Nov. 1707
2 CONT *[[Turner-26715|Ruth Turner]], b. 2 Mar. 1688; m. Isaac Turner*[[Turner-37010|Lydia Turner]], b. 5 Sept. 1690; living in November 1707*; m. George Buttolph*[[Turner-302|Grace Turner]], b. 29 Aug. 1692, baptized 25 Sept. 1692;m. Jo
2 CONC seph Miner*Hannah Turner, b. 8 Sept. 1694, baptized 30 Sept 1694; m. Thomas Pember*[[Turner-6878|Elizabeth Turner]], b. 5 Dec. 1696; m. (1) Thomas Darte; m. (2) John Hazen*Ezekiel Turner, b. 14 Mar. 1698; baptized 19 Mar. 1698/9; 
2 CONC m. (1) Theoda Williams; m. (2) Borodel Denison*[[Turner-9189|Lucretia Turner]], b. 20 Jan. 1701; baptized 27 Apr. 1701; m. Joseph Caulkins*[[Turner-13455|Abigail Turner]], baptized 14 Mar. 1702/3; m. Clement Miner
2 CONT
2 CONT
