1 NOTE    From Situate, settled in New London about 1675 (p 278). The barque
2 CONT Providence, coming in from the sea, was lost with her cargo on the
2 CONT rocks at Fisher's Island Point in the night of 28 Nov 1679. The master
2 CONT Thomas Dymond, and his two assistants John Mayher and Ezekiel Turner,
2 CONT were barely saved (p 236) (New London Hx).
