1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Mayflower Family Member}}Mary Turner was a descendant of ''Mayflower'' passenger [[Brewster-4|'''William Brewster''']].
2 CONT == Biography ==Mary Turner, the daughter of [[Turner-2746|Ezekiel]] and [[Keeney-155|Susannah (Keeney) Miner]], was born 30 May 1686 in New London, Connecticut.≤ref>Merrick, Barbara Lambert, ''Mayflower Families through Five Gener
2 CONC ations, Vol 24 Part 1, The Descendants of Elder William Brewster,'' General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2014. "The Silver Book" Page 207-208≤/ref>≤ref>New London, New London, Connecticut, Record o Births, Marriages and Death
2 CONC s, Town Clerk, New London, Connecticut, Vol 1, p. 18; digital images, Family Search, image group 007730349, (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BT-C69B : accessed March 30, 2024)≤/ref> She was named in the division
2 CONC  of her father Ezekiel's estate, which was recorded 29 Nov 1707.≤ref>New London District, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-892R-ZK3T?i=1198&cat=141959 Probate packet #5400, Ezekiel Turner, 1705].≤/ref>≤ref>"Connec
2 CONC ticut, Wills and Probate Records, 1609-1999," database and images, Ancestry(https://www.ancestry.com : accessed 11 Jul 2020), Ezekiel Turner estate division recorded 29 Nov 1707; citing Probate Records.  Hartford, Connecticut:  Ha
2 CONC rtford County Probate Court.  Probate Packets, Tinker,Jonathan-Turner, Joseph, 1675-1850, images 1199-1210. Rec. Date: 9 Jun 2020.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === First Marriage : John Daniels ===Mary Turner and [[Daniels-947|John Daniels]] were married sometime before the birth of their first child in November 1708.≤ref name="NLVR1_35">[https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BT
2 CONC -CD11?cc=2448940 "Connecticut Marriages, 1640-1939,"] database with images, FamilySearch (11 April 2017), > image 1 of 1; Connecticut State Library, Hartford. New London Vital Records, 1:35, 1890 James N. Arnold copy.≤/ref> John w
2 CONC as born on 22 October 1686 at New London, the son of [[Daniels-946|John]] and [[Beebe-480|Agnes (Beebe) Daniels]].≤ref>[https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7HM-RQL "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906"] FamilySearc
2 CONC h (7 January 2020), John Daniells, 1686.≤/ref> 
2 CONT In a land record dated 18 October 1714, John Daniels Jr. of New Londonand Mary his wife sold to Samuel Fosdick of New London their rights and interest in the real estate of Ezekiel Turner late of New London deceased, which was set
2 CONC  out to Mary the daughter of Ezekiel Turner in the 1707 estate division (above).≤ref name="MD71">Wilson, Keith Edward, "Three Husbands for Mary Turner and One More for Susannah Turner of New London and Lyme, Connecticut," ''Mayflo
2 CONC wer Descendant'', Volume 71(2023):101-118, citing New London Deeds, 7:141, John Daniels and Mary, his wife, to Samuel Fosdick.≤/ref>
2 CONT John died at New London on 10 July 1731 and was buried the next day, on Sunday after meeting.≤ref>Hempstead, Joshua. ''Diary of Joshua Hempstead of New London, Connecticut,'' (New London, Conn. : The New LondonCounty Historical So
2 CONC ciety, 1901), p. 237 [https://archive.org/details/diaryofjoshuahem1901hemp/page/237/mode/1up Archive.org].≤/ref> John Daniels, of New London, carpenter, made his will on 10 July 1731 in which he named his dearly beloved wife Mary 
2 CONC as sole executrix (use of hishouse and lott adjoyning for her widowhood and 1/3 of household goods); son Ezekiel Daniells a double portion of John's inheritance and theremainder of his estate to be equally divided among the rest o
2 CONC f his (unnamed) children. He signed with his mark.Witnesses: Joseph Minor Jr., Samuel Daniells, Nathanael Daniells. The will was proved on 08 September 1731.≤ref name="NLPR1571">New London District, [https://www.familysearch.org/a
2 CONC rk:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G925-GVFT?i=918&cat=141959 Probate packet #1571, John Daniels jr., 1732].≤/ref>
2 CONT The settlement of his estate was made on 19 December 1734, triggered by his widow's remarriage. His children were named in it: Ezekiel Daniels (eldest son), Lucy Leach, Esther Daniels, John Daniels, Noah Daniels, Daniel Daniels an
2 CONC d Lucretia Daniels.≤ref name="NLPR1571" />
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage : Henry Rowland ===Mary married [[Rowland-16928|Henry Rowland]] or Roulen of Lyme on 03 Jun 1734 at the First Church of Christ, New London, New London, Connecticut, British Colonial America. ≤ref>"Connecticut, C
2 CONC hurch Records, 1660-1955", , FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QGRS-CL8Z : Sat Mar 09 17:53:19 UTC 2024), Entry for Henry Roland and Mary Daniels, 3 Jun 1734.≤/ref> ≤ref>"Connecticut Marriages, 1630-1997", 
2 CONC , FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7PB-2JN : 11 January 2020), Henry Roland, 1734.≤/ref> Henry made his will on 02 September 1734, and died probably not long before 14 April 1747 when itwas proved and his est
2 CONC ate was inventoried. One of the witnesses to his will was Richard Leech, probably the husband of Lucy Daniels, his step-daughter. In his will, he mentioned his "now wife" Mary and named her as sole executrix. He made small bequest
2 CONC s to the children of his first wife Temperance: John, Henry, Temperance, Patience and Elizabeth as he had previously given them their portions. He signed his name as Henry Roulen and set his seal.≤ref name="NLPR4629">New London Pr
2 CONC obate District, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G92R-ZS1Q?i=373&cat=141959 Probate packet #4529, Lyme, Henry Rowland, 1747.]≤/ref>
2 CONT There were no children of this marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Third Marriage : John Banning ===Mary (Turner) (Daniels) Rowland married [[Banning-8|John Banning]] of Lyme before 17 March 1751 when he gave each of his sons [[Banning-321|John]] and [[Banning-225|Samuel]]  70 acres of land i
2 CONC n Lyme, reservingthe use of it to his wife during her natural life.≤ref>Wilson, ''Mayflower Descendant'', Volume 71(2023):112, citing Friedlander, Mary Banning, "Block Island Settlers of Joshua's Town, Lyme, Connecticut, 1701-1800
2 CONC , Banning, Niles and Tiffany Families," ''NEHGR'' Vol. 153(1999):323-343, citing [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G925-JGWS?cat=141959 New London District Probate, File 294. ] [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB
2 CONC 202/t/11657/328/143511821 AmericanAncestors.org $ubscribers can request a copy.]≤/ref>
2 CONT [[Banning-8|John Banning]] of Lyme made his will on 08 September 1757 in which he named his "true and well beloved" wife Mary; unnamed children of his daughter [[Banning-7|Elizabeth]] (dec'd), former wife of Lt. John Brockway; gra
2 CONC ndson Thomas Dibble; unnamed heirs of his son JohnBanning dec'd; son Samuel Banning; daughter Mary, wife of John Wood; daughter [[Banning-329|Hannah]], wife of Joseph Wilder. His widow was to have all the estate she brought to the
2 CONC ir marriage, and more. JosephWilder to be executor. His will was proved 12 August 1759. He signed his will.≤ref name="NLPR294">New London District, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G925-JGWS?i=1156&cat=141959 Prob
2 CONC ate packet #294, John Banning, 1759].≤/ref>
2 CONT The last known record of Mary Banning was when she gave land to her son "for and in consideration of that love and good will and parental affection" that she had for her "dutiful son Daniel Daniels of sd Lyme."It was a parcel of a
2 CONC bout 5 3/4 acres of land at Walnut Hill.≤ref>Wilson, ''Mayflower Descendant'', Volume 71(2023):112, citing  Lyme Deeds 12:35.≤/ref>
2 CONT === Children ===The children of [[Daniels-947|John]] and Mary (Turner) Daniels were born at New London:≤ref name="MD71" />≤ref>[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BT-C6HP?i=4&cc=2448940&cat=301859 "Connecticut Marr
2 CONC iages, 1640-1939,"] database with images, FamilySearch (11 April 2017); Connecticut State Library, Hartford. New London Vital Records, Vol. 1, 1890, James N. Arnold copy, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BT-CD11
2 CONC ?i=47&cc=2448940&cat=301859 pp. 35, Ezekiel]; [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-C9BT-C698?i=49&cc=2448940&cat=301859 38, Peter, Lucy]; [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/619033:1:3Q9M-C9BT-C6SW?i=53&cc=2448940&cat=
2 CONC 301859 46, Hester].≤/ref>#[[Daniels-4692|Ezekiel Daniels]], b. 27 Nov 1708; d. aft. 16 Dec 1771; m. Elizabeth Crocker 27 Oct 1731 New London. 6 children b. New London. French & Indian war service.#[[Daniels-12242|Peter Daniels]], 
2 CONC b. 27 Dec 1710; d. 15 Jan 1728/9 NewLondon.#[[Daniels-4910|Lucy Daniels]], b. 29 Jun 1713; d. aft. 25 Feb 1757; m. Richard Leach 15 Nov 1732  New London. He was son of Thomas and Mary(Tubbs) (Crocker) Leach, b. 02 Feb 1710/1. 4 ch
2 CONC ildren bp. New London.#[[Daniels-12243|Esther/Hester Daniels]], b. 04 Aug 1715; m. Caleb Moore, son of Joseph, 02 Mar 1734/5. 4 children b. New London.#[[Daniels-10900|John Daniels]], b. ca 1718; m. Huldah Smith 03 Mar 1743 at New
2 CONC  London. French & Indian war service. 6 children b. New London & Lyme.#[[Daniels-12244|Noah Daniels]], b. ca. 1725, bp. 21 Apr 1734;≤ref name=NLbap /> d. aft. 20 Aug 1808; m. Elizabeth ____. 3 children b. New London.#[[Daniels-122
2 CONC 45|Daniel Daniels]], b. ca. 1726, bp. 07 Nov 1734≤ref>[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:4VPT-R8T2 "Connecticut, Births and Baptisms, 1639-1941"], FamilySearch (Sat Mar 09 16:39:56 UTC 2024), Entry for Daniel Daniels or 
2 CONC Rolands and Mary Daniels or Rolands,7 November 1734.≤/ref> d. Sep 1800 Lyme; m. Elizabeth ____. One childb. Lyme.#[[Daniels-2198|Lucretia Daniels]], b. ca. 1727, bp. 21 Apr 1734;≤ref name=NLbap>[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/6
2 CONC 1903/1:1:4VP6-2Q6Z "Connecticut, Births and Baptisms, 1639-1941",] FamilySearch (Sat Mar 09 06:58:36 UTC 2024), Entry for Lucretia Daniels and Mary Daniels, 21 April 1734.≤/ref> d. aft. Mar 1753; m1. Abner Tubbs 25 Apr 1725, m2. R
2 CONC obert Chapman bef. 03 Mar 1753, divorce petition filed for Abner's desertion. 2 children by Tubbs.
