2 CONT == Biography ==Grace Turner was the daughter of Ezekiel Turner and Susanna Keeney Turner Miner.≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref> Grace's father Ezekiel was the son of Mary Brewster, granddaughter of Elder William Brewster o
2 CONC f the Mayflower.≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===: Birth:  29 AUG 1692, New London, New London, Connecticut≤ref>Source:[[#S463]] ≤/ref>≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===: Grace's husband, Joseph Miner, died at Lyme on "30 May 1781, in his 93rd year".≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref>
2 CONT : Grace (Turner) Miner died at Lyme, New London, Connecticut on Sunday6 June 1784, widow of Mr. Joseph Miner.≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===
2 CONT : Husband:  [[Miner-776|Joseph(2) Miner]]
2 CONT : Wife:  [[Turner-4153|Grace Turner]]: Marriage:  26 FEB 1712/13,≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 24≤/ref> New Haven 2nd Church, New London, New London, Connecticut≤ref>Source: [[#S325]] [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=coo1
2 CONC .ark:/13960/t03x8v86w;view=1up;seq=13 ''Early Connecticut Marriages as found on ancientchurch records prior to 1800''], Rev. F. W. Bailey, Editor, at HathiTrust.org.  Original:  (1896). "New London: Joseph Minor & Grace Turner- 17
2 CONC 13". Vol 2, page 9≤/ref>≤ref>Source: [[#S331]]  New London Vital Statistics from the collated copy from the original records, Vol. 1, pg 44≤/ref>≤ref>Source: [[#S473]] ≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===: Grace (Turner) Miner and Joseph Miner her husband had eight children:≤ref>[[#Merrick|Merrick]], page 25≤/ref>
2 CONT ::  Joseph, b. 10 Sept 1714
2 CONT ::  Jesse, b. 13 Aug 1716, bapt. 18 Nov 1716
2 CONT ::  Elizabeth, b. 23 July 1719, bapt. May 1720
2 CONT ::  Hannah, b. 29 Aug 1721, bapt. 1 April 1722
2 CONT ::  Ezekiel, b. 20 Aug 1723, bapt. 1 Sept 1723
2 CONT ::  Theody/Theodore, b. 27 April 1726, bapt.7 Aug 1726
