1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Elizabeth (Turner) [Dart] Hazen profile at Source tab uploaded 1/11/2022 from the Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Vol 27, Brewster, William (MFIP Jonathan) p. 27, published 2015.
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems that a number of online trees have John Hazen's 2nd wife (Elizabeth Dart) as the daughter of Daniel Dart and Elizabeth (Douglas) Dart, but that seems to be an error contained in the Hazen Family in America genealogy by Tr
2 CONC acy Elliot Hazen, 1947.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ezekiel Turner & Susanna Keeney:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Turner. Born on 5 Dec 1696 in New London, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr10/rr10_198.html#P9590
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 May 1717 when Elizabeth was 20, she first married Thomas Dart (44451) , son of Daniel Dart (3 May 1666-2 Jan 1738) & Elizabeth Douglas (24904) (25 Feb 1668-8 Apr 1753), in New London, CT. Born on 8 Jul 1687 in New London, CT.
2 CONC  Thomas died in New London, CT, on 12 May 1720; he was 32.
2 CONT ===Second Marriage 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 May 1726 when Elizabeth was 29, she second married John Hazen,  son of Thomas Hazen (29 Feb 1657/8-12 Apr 1735) & Mary Howlett  (ca 1664-24 Oct 1727), in New London, CT Born on 23 Mar 1687 in Boxford, MA.419 John died in Nor
2 CONC wich, CT, on 24 Feb 1772; he was 84
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Elizabeth (Turner) (Dart) Hazen:
2 CONT
2 CONT *     i. Elizabeth Hazen, b. 15 Sep 1727 in Norwalk CT;
2 CONT *     ii.. Marcy Hazen, b. 18 May 1729 in Norwalk,CT;
2 CONT *     iii. Hannah Hazen, b. 28 June 1731 in Norwalk CT (Lyme VR has 18 May 1731); and then
2 CONT *     iv. Thomas Hazen, b. 12 Feb 1733 (Bpt 18 Feb 1733) both in Lyme CT m. Mary Giles (b. 21 May 1740)
2 CONT *     v.  Mary Hazen, b. 5 Jan 1735 in Lyme CT;
2 CONT *     v.  Ezekiel, bpt 21, Sept 1736 in Lyme, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * The Hazen Family in America: A Genealogy by Tracy Elliot Hazen, PH. D.  Front Cover. Tracy Elliot Hazen.  Page 36.  < [https://books.google.com/books/content?id=BlQZAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA36&img=1&pgis=1&dq=Dart&sig=ACfU3U2eWYtIKmSWP1T6m
2 CONC ASj317PeslE9A&edge=0 GoogleBooks] >Misidentified https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hazen/6000000105790743869’s second wife as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Hazen/6000000011725106501?through=6000000105790743869, daughter of 
2 CONC  Daniel Dart & Elizabeth Douglas.  John’s 2nd wife was  Elizabeth Dart’s sister in law, also called Elizabeth Dart (nee Turner), widow of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Dart/6000000011725218427?through=6000000003939394173.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Re: Did John Hazen marry Elizabeth Dart or Elizabeth Turner Dart? < [https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/hazen/1011/ link] > I have an excerpt from a letter written by the distinguished genealogist Donald Lines Jacob
2 CONC us, Dec 3, 1959, re Thomas Hazen in connection with an application of a family member for the DAR.He wrote: "The aforesaid Thomas Hazen was son of John Hazen of Norwich and Lyne, Conn. by his second wife Elizabeth Dart. The compil
2 CONC er of this book [Dr. Robert Hazen] misidentified her as daughter of Daniel Dart. She was not. She was a widow, Elizabeth (Turner) Dart. I think Elizabeth Turner descended from William Brewster of the Mayflower and if so, this woul
2 CONC d make you eligible to the Mayflower Society."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT {{Mayflower Family Member}}Elizabeth Turner was a descendant of ''Mayflower'' passenger [[Brewster-4|'''William Brewster''']].
2 CONT == Biography ==Elizabeth was born in New London, Connecticut on 5 December 1696 to  [[Turner-2746|Ezekiel]] and [[Keeney-155|Susannah (Keeney) Turner]].≤ref>Barbara Lambert Merrick, Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol
2 CONC  24 Part 1, The Descendants of Elder William Brewster, General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2014. "The Silver Book" Page 207-208≤/ref>≤ref name="MFIPBrewster">Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880. (Onlin
2 CONC e database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2017). From ''Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620.'' Plymouth, MA: Gen
2 CONC eral Society of MayflowerDescendants, 1975-2015. [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/27/71746043 William Brewster, (MFIP Jonathan), p. 27] (Link on ''AmericanAncestors.org'' by $ubscription.)≤/ref> She was named in t
2 CONC he division of her father Ezekiel's estate, which was recorded 29 Nov 1707.≤ref>"Connecticut, Wills and Probate Records, 1609-1999," database and images, Ancestry (https://www.ancestry.com : accessed 11 Jul 2020), Ezekiel Turner e
2 CONC state division recorded 29 Nov 1707; citing Probate Records.  Hartford, Connecticut:  Hartford County Probate Court.  Probate Packets, Tinker, Jonathan-Turner, Joseph, 1675-1850, images 1199-1210. Rec. Date: 9 Jun 2020.≤/ref>
2 CONT Elizabeth married Thomas Dart in New London on May 8, 1717. Their child Elizabeth was born on 17 March 1718. Thomas Dart died at sea between1718 and 1724 at which time the widowed Elizabeth (Turner) Dart sold his estate. 
2 CONT On 31 May 1726, Elizabeth (Turner) Dart remarried in Norwich, Connecticut to [[Hazen-4|John Hazen]] (1688-1772) and had five more children.≤ref name="MFIPBrewster" />≤ref>Hempstead, Joshua. ''Diary of Joshua Hempstead of New Londo
2 CONC n, Connecticut, covering a period of forty-seven years, from September 1711, to November, 1758,'' New London, Conn., TheNew London County Historical Society, 1970. Page 170. [https://archive.org/details/diaryofjoshuahem00hemp/page
2 CONC /170/mode/1up?q=hazen (Archive.org link)] Note:  "Jno Hazen & '''Wid''' Eliz Darte publisht"≤/ref>
2 CONT Child of [[Dart-503|Thomas]] and Elizabeth (Turner) Dart born New London:≤ref name="MFIPBrewster" />
2 CONT #[[Dart-180|Elizabeth Dart]], b. 17 Mar 1718, bp. 17 Aug 1718.
2 CONT Children of [[Hazen-4|John]] and Elizabeth (Turner) (Dart) Hazen:≤ref name="MFIPBrewster" />
2 CONT #[[Hazen-358|Elizabeth Hazen]], b. 15 Sep 1727, Norwich
2 CONT #[[Hazen-454|Marcy Hazen]], b. 18 May 1729, Norwich#[[Hazen-356|Hannah Hazen]], b. 28 Jun 1731, Norwich (18 May 1731 in Lyme VRs)
2 CONT #[[Hazen-351|Thomas Hazen]], b. 12 Feb 1732/3 Lyme, bp. 18 Feb 1732/3
2 CONT #[[Hazen-353|Mary Hazen]], b. 05 Jan 1734/5 Lyme
2 CONT #Ezekiel, bp. 21 Sep 1736 Lyme
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes ==
2 CONT '''Disputed Spouse:'''According to some sources, [[Hazen-4|John Hazen]] married [[Dart-127|Elizabeth Dart (1689-)]] on 31 May 1726 in Norwich (New London), Essex,Connecticut.≤ref>Hazen, Tracy Elliot, compiler, and Donald Lines Jac
2 CONC obus, editor. The Hazen Family in America, A Genealogy. New Haven, Connecticut: The Tuttle, Morehouse and Taylor Company, 1947. Page 36. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89064445307&seq=50&q1=dart&start=2 (HathiTrust lin
2 CONC k)]≤/ref>
2 CONT However, John Hazen married instead as his second wife, [[Turner-39969|Elizabeth (Turner) Dart]], daughter of  [[Turner-2746|Ezekiel]] and [[Keeney-155|Susannah (Keeney) Turner]], and the widow of [[Dart-503|Thomas Dart (1687-abt.
2 CONC 1720)]] as shown here. 
