1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail was born in 1703. She passed away in 1756. 
2 CONT : Abigail Turner was the ninth of ten daughters of Ezekiel Turner and Susanna Keeney, born in New London, Connecticut, and baptized there March 14, 1702/3. ≤ref>Connecticut. Church Records Index. Connecticut State Library, Hartfor
2 CONC d, Connecticut. Volume 079 New London, Baptism of Abigail Turner, daughter of Ezekiel Turner.≤/ref> ≤ref name="MFIPBrewster">''Mayflower Families in Progress:  William BREWSTER of the Mayflower, and the fifth generation descendant
2 CONC s of his son JONATHAN'', Page 31≤/ref> Two years after she was born, her father died. Her mother re-married in New London, August 20 1706. Abigail's step-father was Joseph Miner, a great uncle of the Clement Miner that Abigail lat
2 CONC er married.
2 CONT : Abigail Turner married Clement Miner in New London in the First Congregational Church on January 9, 1721/22. ≤ref>White, Lorraine Cook, ed. The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records. Vol. 1-55.Baltimore, MD, USA: 
2 CONC Genealogical Publishing Co., 1994-2002. Marriage of Abigail Turner and Clement Miner, Jr. ≤/ref> ≤ref name="MFIPBrewster"/> Abigail and Clement had ten children. Lucy, Lydia, Abigail, Jonathan, twins Ebenezer and Edward, Martha, a
2 CONC nd Clement were all born in New London. The last two children, Daniel and William were born in Norwich. ≤ref>Roser, Susan E. Mayflower Births and Deaths: From the Files of George Ernest Bowman at the Massachusetts Society of Mayfl
2 CONC ower Descendants. Volumes 1 & 2. Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992; family of Abigail Turner and Clement Miner, Jr.≤/ref>
2 CONT : Abigail died in Norwich September 23, 1756,≤ref name="MFIPBrewster"/> and is probably buried there, but no burial record has been located.(Find A Grave Memorial# 53506044)
2 CONT : Abigail is the granddaughter of Mary Brewster, herself granddaughterof Elder William Brewster, of the ship ''Mayflower''.≤ref name="MFIPBrewster"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
2 CONT * Merrick, Barbara Lambert, compiler, [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/31/71746047 ''Mayflower Families in Progress:  William BREWSTER of the Mayflower, and the fifth generation descendants of his son JONATHAN''],
2 CONC  Page 31.  Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2017). From Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the
2 CONC  Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-≤2015>.
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=53506044 ''Find a Grave Memorial ID 53506044, Abigail (Turner) Miner]
2 CONT * family tree
