1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Mayflower Project Brewster Family Work List]]
2 CONT {{Mayflower Family Member}} 
2 CONT == Biography ==Susanna Turner was born on 02 January 1685 at New London, Connecticut Colony, daughter of [[Turner-2746|Ezekiel]] and [[Keeney-155|Susannah (Keeney) Turner]].≤ref name="NLVR306"/>≤ref name="MFIP">Mayflower Families 
2 CONC Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2017). From Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymou
2 CONC th, Mass., December 1620. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-2015. [https://www.americanancestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/22/1422157394 MFIP - Jonathan Brewster, p.22] (AmericanAncestors.org, by $ubscription.)
2 CONC ≤/ref>≤ref name=mayflower>''Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880''. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic GenealogicalSociety, 2017). From Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: 
2 CONC Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620.Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-2015. [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/mayflower-families-fifth-generation-descendan
2 CONC ts-1700-1880/image?volumeId=51963&pageName=124&rId=71746140 Reference William Brewster, pages 124-5, 127, entry for Adam Pickett]. $Subscription≤/ref> 
2 CONT She married first [[Pickett-3101|Adam Pickett]], 26 November 1702 at New London.≤ref name="NLVR306"/> Adam Pickett was the son of Adam and Hannah (Wetherill) Pickett, born at New London on 07 September 1681 andbaptized on 11 Septe
2 CONC mber 1681. He died after 19 January 1703/4 and before 20 June 1707, when a notation on his father-in-law's inventory mentions items delivered to the widow of Adam Pickett as part of her portion.≤ref name=mayflower /> 
2 CONT She was known to be living November 26, 1707 when she was named in thedistribution of her father's estate.≤ref name=mayflower/>
2 CONT Because Susanna's name in her next marriage to Samuel Fosdick was recorded as Susanna ''Turner'', not ''Pickett'', there remained some question if Susanna was the daughter of Ezekiel Turner. Additionally, the citation notice on th
2 CONC e estate of Adam Pickett, was issued to Susanna, widow of Adam Pickett, on August 8, 1706. This date was three weeks after her supposed marriage to Fosdick; the citation should have been issued to Susanna Fosdick, late widow of Ad
2 CONC am Pickett if she was the sameperson. That question is resolved by the following quitclaim deed.≤ref name="MD71" /> 
2 CONT On 09 May 1717, Samuel Fosdick of New London and Susannah his wife quitclaimed to Joseph Miner Jr. of New London the rights in the real estate of Ezekiel Turner late of New London deceased, which was settled onSusannah as part of 
2 CONC her portion, along with what had been purchase from the other heirs to the estate by Samuel Fosdick.≤ref name="MD71">Wilson, Keith Edward, "Three Husbands for Mary Turner and One More for Susannah Turner of New London and Lyme, Co
2 CONC nnecticut," ''Mayflower Descendant'', Volume 71(2023): 101-118, citing New London Deeds, 7:144, Samuel Fosdick and Susanna his wife, to Joseph Miner Jr.≤/ref>≤ref>New London District, [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3
2 CONC QS7-892R-ZK3T?i=1198&cat=141959 Probate Packet #5400, Ezekiel Turner, 1705].≤/ref>
2 CONT Susanna Turner married Samuel Fosdick, as her second husband, on July 13, 1706 recorded at New London.≤ref name="NLVR306">Connecticut: VitalRecords (The Barbour Collection), 1630-1870 (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New E
2 CONC ngland Historic Genealogical Society, 2011.) Fromoriginal typescripts, Lucius Barnes Barbour Collection, 1928.[https://www.americanancestors.org/DB414/i/12577/306/139524842 New London, p. 306] (AmericanAncestors.org by $ubscriptio
2 CONC n); also [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSZC-K9MP-R?i=328&cat=2473 ''Vital records of New London from 1646-1854''  p. 306] (FamilySearch.org)≤/ref>≤ref name="MFIP" />
2 CONT Susanna (Turner) (Pickett) Fosdick died February 22, 1753 at Charlestown, Massachusetts.≤ref name="MFIP127" />
2 CONT Samuel Fosdick's death date was between April 23, 1767 and November 4,1784.≤ref name="MFIP127">Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical 
2 CONC Society, 2017). From Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-2015. [https://www.americanan
2 CONC cestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/127/71746143 MFIP - Jonathan Brewster, pp. 126-8].≤/ref>
2 CONT Adam and Susannah (Turner) Pickett had no children.≤ref name=mayflower/>
2 CONT The children of Samuel and Susannah (Turner) Fosdick were:≤ref name="MFIP127" />
2 CONT #[[Fosdick-24|Mercy Fosdick]] (1708–~1775)
2 CONT #[[Fosdick-28|Samuel Fosdick]] (1710–1792)
2 CONT # [[Fosdick-29|William Fosdick]] (1712– )#Ruth Fosdick, b. 25 Jan 1713/4, bpt. 07 Feb 1713/4; not in father's will.
2 CONT # [[Fosdick-4|James Fosdick]] (1716–1784)
2 CONT # [[Fosdick-31|Ezekiel Fosdick]] (1719–1786)
2 CONT # [[Fosdick-32|Jesse Fosdick]] (1722–1786)
2 CONT # [[Fosdick-33|Susannah Fosdick]] (1724–1801)
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT ≤references />
