2 CONT == Biography == Ruth Turner, d/o Ezekiel and Susanna (Keeney) Turner, was born in New London, Connecticut, 2 March 1688, and was probably bpt 13 March 1691/2.≤ref name=MF5>Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880
2 CONC . (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2017). From Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620. William Brews
2 CONC ter:Jonathan p. 3, 4. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-2015. https://www.americanancestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/4/71746020 ≤/ref>
2 CONT Her death is unknown, however she was still living 29 Nov 1724, when son Waitstill was baptized, but probably deceased by Dec 1769, when a guardian was appointed for her husband, because he was declared non-compos mentis.≤ref name
2 CONC =MF5 />
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: born and bpt. in Scituate.≤ref name=MF5 />
2 CONT #Susanna b. 12 Aug 1712; bpt 7 Dec 1712
2 CONT #Jonathan b. 27 may 1714; bpt 19 Dep 1714#Isaac bpt 5 Apr 1719. Isaac and his brother Waitstill were declared non-compos in 1772 by the town of Hanover.
2 CONT #Lemuel bpt 14 Aug 1720
2 CONT #Ezekiel bp 23 Sep 1722
2 CONT #Waitstill bp 29 Nov 1724. 
2 CONT Ruth Turner married her cousin Isaac Turner in Scituate Wednesday, 31 October 1711.
2 CONT Ruth is the daughter of Ezekiel Turner4 (Mary3 Brewster, Johnathan 2, William 1)and hs wife, Susanna (Keeney). Ruth was also a descendant ofElder William Brewster of the Mayflower {Families #24 and #108}
2 CONT == Sources ==
