2 CONT {{Mayflower Family Member}}Lydia Turner was a descendant of ''Mayflower'' passenger [[Brewster-4|'''William Brewster''']].
2 CONT == Biography ==Lydia Turner was the daughter of [[Turner-2746|Ezekiel]] and [[Keeney-155|Susannah (Keeney) Miner]].≤ref>Barbara Lambert Merrick, ''Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol 24 Part 1, The Descendants ofElder
2 CONC  William Brewster, General Society of Mayflower Descendants,'' 2014. "The Silver Book" Pages 207-208.≤/ref> She was named in the division of her father Ezekiel's estate, which was recorded 29 Nov 1707.≤ref>"Connecticut, Wills and 
2 CONC Probate Records, 1609-1999," database and images, Ancestry (https://www.ancestry.com : accessed 11 Jul 2020), Ezekiel Turner estate division recorded 29 Nov 1707; citing Probate Records.  Hartford, Connecticut:  Hartford County Pr
2 CONC obate Court.  Probate Packets, Tinker, Jonathan-Turner, Joseph, 1675-1850, images 1199-1210. Rec. Date: 9 Jun 2020.≤/ref>
2 CONT She married [[Buttolph-8|George Buttolph]] after 25 November 1707 and before 1712.≤ref>Dates of division deed and deed of sale, Land Recordsof New London, Conn. 6:338.≤/ref>
2 CONT Lydia Buttolph died of consumption on 02 June 1742 in New London aged about 50 [''sic''].≤ref>Hempstead, Joshua, ''Diary of Joshua Hempsteadof New London, Connecticut, covering a period of forty-seven years, from September 1711, t
2 CONC o November, 1758'' (New London, Conn. : New London County Historical Society, 1970) p. 394. [https://archive.org/details/diaryofjoshuahem00hemp/page/394/mode/1up?q=buttolph Archive.org]≤/ref>
2 CONT The children of [[Buttolph-8|George]] and Lydia (Turner) Buttolph bornor baptized in New London, Connecticut:≤ref>Mayflower Families Fifth Generation Descendants, 1700-1880. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England His
2 CONC toric Genealogical Society, 2017). From MayflowerFamilies Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass., December 1620. Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1975-2015. [http
2 CONC s://www.americanancestors.org/DB2728/i/51963/23/71746039 William Brewster, MFIP Jonathan, pp. 22-3.] (Link by $ubscription.)≤/ref>
2 CONT #[[Buttolph-171|Lydia Buttolph]], bp. 06 May 1716.#[[Buttolph-101|Elizabeth Buttolph]], bp. 02 Sep 1716 [recorded as Hannah in Hempstead Diary - (''sic'')]; d. 18 Oct 1746 at New London; unmarried.#Ann Buttolph, bp. 20 Dec 1719, p
2 CONC robably "the child of George Buttolph, who died yesterd." on 13 Jun 1721.#[[Buttolph-200|Jonathan Buttolph]], b. ca. 1721 (age at death); d. 1750 in New London, age 27. His will named sister Ann Buttolph.#[[Buttolph-84|George Butt
2 CONC olph]], bp. 25 Mar or 01 Apr 1722; d. 07 Mar1724/5 in New London.
2 CONT #Mary Buttolph, bp. 30 Jun 1728.
2 CONT #Ann Buttolph, b. 02 Apr 1732, bp. 30 Jun 1732.
