2 CONT {{Connecticut}}
2 CONT == Biography ==David Caulkins, son of Hugh and Ann (Eaton) Calkins was probably born about 1642 in Gloucester, Massachusetts. In the baptismal records in Waverton, Cheshire, his older sisters Sarah, Mary and Rebecca are shown, the
2 CONC  last one in November 1631. There is a Deborah shown baptized, then buried in 1639, although it is not clear if she is Hugh and Ann's child. No baptisms are shown for David and John, which could be sloppy record keeping, non-recor
2 CONC ding for dissenters, or the fact that they were already in America. There is a sister Deborah who was baptized 18 March 1643/4 in America. David and John were born between those dates of 1631 and 1644, so could have been born Wave
2 CONC rton or Gloucester.≤ref>See attached parish register abstracts.≤/ref>
2 CONT David's father and brother left New London about 1659/1660 to found Norwich. David remained on the family farm at Nahantick,≤ref name=NewLondon /> which remained in the family for 6 generations. ≤ref>Caulkins: History of New Londo
2 CONC n. p. 158≤/ref>
2 CONT He married (1) Mary Bliss, daughter of [[Bliss-2|Thomas Bliss Jr (bef.1618-1688≤ref name=NewLondon />
2 CONT He married (2) Hannah (_____) widow of Benjamin Abell, who died at Norwich, Conn., in 1699.≤ref>Abell, Horace A. and Lewis P. Abell. ''The Abell family in America : Robert Abell of Rehoboth, Mass., his English ancestry and his des
2 CONC cendants, other Abell families and immigrantTs, Abell families in England''  (Rutland, Vt. : Tuttle Publishing Co., [1940] )≤/ref>≤ref name=probate />
2 CONT David Caulkins died 25 Nov 1717.≤ref name=NewLondon />≤ref>White, Lorraine Cook, ed. New London. The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records. Vol. 1-55. Baltimore, MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1994-2002. p 62
2 CONC  [http://dunhamwilcox.net/barbour/newlond_barbour_c1.htm link at dunhamwilcox.net]≤/ref>
2 CONT Will: Dated 20 June 1717, proved 10 Jan 1717/8. "I David Caukin being in good helth of body ...soul to god ... body to the ground ... just debts and funeral Charges be paid ... Loving wife Hannah Caukin twenty five pound ... of mo
2 CONC vables as mony. w≤sup>th≤/sup> what more is Comingto me of the Estat of her dec≤sup>d≤/sup> husband benj Abel ... bed and furniture with the other houshold stuff ... and at her death to be delivered to my son Joseph Caukin. ... my
2 CONC  Son John Caukin ... to my grandson david Caukin. Son to my Sd Son John Caukin ... my daugher Ann Burchard ... my daughter Mary Bushnel ... my daughter Lydya Kille ... my son David Caukin dec≤sup>d≤/sup> and my son Jonathan Caukin
2 CONC s ... SonJoseph Caukin my Sole excuto≤sup>r≤/sup> ..."≤ref name=probate>New London Co Probate records, 1675-1916 [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L92Y-LZX9?i=29&cat=421297 will p. 234 (image 30 of 616)]; [https://
2 CONC www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L92Y-LZ6Q?i=31&cat=421297 Inventory pp. 239-241 (image 32 of 616)]≤/ref>
2 CONT Children by his wife Mary Bliss.≤ref name=NewLondon>Caulkins, Frances Manwaring,  History of New London, Connecticut : from the first surveyof the coast in 1612 to 1860 (New London: HD Utley, 1895) [https://play.google.com/books/r
2 CONC eader?id=ij8OAAAAIAAJ&pg=GBS.PA360&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_atb_hover p. 361] ≤/ref>
2 CONT #David b. 5 July 1674
2 CONT #Ann b. 8 Nov 1676
2 CONT #Jonathan b. 9 Jan 1678/9
2 CONT #Peter b. 9 Oct 1681
2 CONT #John
2 CONT #Mary
2 CONT #Joseph bpt 3 Nov 1694
2 CONT #Lydia bpt 9 Aug 1696#Ann, is listed twice in History of New London, but I suspect there isonly one Ann.
