1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VERMONT with the rank of CAPTAIN. [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A018336  DAR Ancestor # A018336]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Capt. Stephen Calkin's Company, Vermont Republic Militia, American Revolution]][[Category: Col. Ebenezer Allen's Regiment, Vermont Republic Militia, American Revolution]][[Category: Col. Ira Allen's Regiment, Vermont R
2 CONC epublic Militia, American Revolution]]
2 CONT [[Category:Read Cemetery, Danby, Vermont]]
2 CONT == Biography =={{1776 Sticker|unit=Col. Ira Allen's Regiment, Vermont Republic Militia, American Revolution|rank=Captain}}
2 CONT {{Society Ancestor|society=DAR|ancestor= A018336}}
2 CONT {{NSSAR Patriot Ancestor|sar-number=127444|rank=Captain}}
2 CONT We have no date of the marriage of Stephen and Rebecca.  They were notmarried in Connecticut.  Stephen was a sea captain and tradition comes down to us that he married in England on one his voyages.  He names his wife, "Rebecca" i
2 CONC n his will made March 26, 1801; and among her friends she was known as "Lady Rowland".  Stephen with his wife and son Richard, came to Danby, Vermont in 1767, being among the first settlersof that place.  He was prominent in the h
2 CONC istory of the town, taking part in the stirring events of the revolution, being a member of the committee of safety, etc.  He was also a Captain in Col. Ira Allen's regiment of " Green Mountain Boys".  he built the first grist mil
2 CONC l in hissection of the country, receiving a bonus of sixty acres of land fromthe township.  He quarried his first set of mill stones from the granite ledge, near which the mill was built.
2 CONT This information is courtesy of a family tree researched and compiled by the wife of Neil Richardson Allen, a descendent of Captain Stephen Calkins, when he applied for membership in the Nation Society Sons of the American Revolut
2 CONC ion, Oregon Chapter.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Name ===: Name:  Capt. Stephen /Calkins/≤ref>Source: [[#S165]]  Page:  Ancestry Family Trees Data:   Text:  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=17838154&pid=595290906≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT : Birth Date:  13 MAR 1731/32
2 CONT : Place:  Lyme, , Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT === Revolutionary War Service ===
