1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage, c 1668, Thomas Geer/Greer b: ABT 1623 in Heavitree, near Exeter, Devon; d 14 jan 1721/2 Enfield Ct
2 CONT
2 CONT "In our historical sketch of George and Thomas Geer, we traced the history of the latter until his arrival in Enfield, Conn., about 1682. From the records of that town, it appears that he was one of the early settlers; for in July
2 CONC  24th, 1682, he had a grant of a house lot and thirty acres of meadow land; also, in 1684 and '87, other grants of land are recorded. Enfield was then in Massachusetts, but later was included in Connecticut. According to the town 
2 CONC records, Thomas was a tanner by trade, and was also an extensive land owner. He deeded various pieces of lands to his son Shubael, and owned at various times, besides his home lot, some 15 acres in the South Field on the "grate ri
2 CONC ver"; 13 acres more or less in the North Field; also at Schantuck river, 2 acres meadow and 3 acres of field land; in 1687 an additional 5 acres of field, to make up the 35 acres "as was engaged him." In 1691, "the Commoners voat 
2 CONC to chose a man of an other towne to be a Moderator to act for them as to Settling their common rights in this town"; "those that Desent agst ye Last act" are given and Thomas Geer is one of them. ... Of the extent or value of Thom
2 CONC as Geer's property nothing certain is known, only what may be gathered from a deed of gift which he and his wife made to their son Shubael, and signed by their X mark. this deed is dated Feb. 22, 1694-5, and is recorded in the Reg
2 CONC ister's office, Jan. 16, 1698-9. Also Thomas, and Deborah his wife, gave a deed to their son Shubael, of all their right and title to all lands in the town of Enfield. this deed is dated August 23d, 1717, and signed by their x mar
2 CONC k, (the name written Geer,) and is recorded on the 342d page, book No. C., in the Registers office in Springfield, Mass. He died Jan. 14th, 1721-2, aged 99. His wife survived him 14 years, and died Jan. 1735-6, aged about 95 years
2 CONC . The property of Thomas remained in the same name until 1796, when, as appears from record, Elihu Geer disposed of his house and lands and removed, since which time there is no record of any descendants residing in Enfield"
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Geer and His Descendants First Generation: from: "The Geer Genealogy: A Historical Record of George and Thomas Geer and Their Descendants in the United States from 1623 to 1923", by Walter Geer, (Norwood, MA: The Plimpton P
2 CONC ress, 1923), pp. 297-298: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Found this entry at this website: https://archive.org/stream/cu31924028819212/cu31924028819212_djvu.txt:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Deborah Davis married Thomas Geere of Enfield, Conn.,had Shubael who has descendants, and Elizabeth born May 4,1685, who died under three years of age, Thomas, the father died 14th Jan.1722, aged 99 years, and his wife Deborah 
2 CONC in 1736, aged 91. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Found this entry at the following website: http://bigelowsociety.com/rod2005/davis05.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Deborah Davis, born January 1645 at Yarmouth, married Thomas Greer, and died in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
