1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Pvt. Consider White''' was born on August 12, 1763 in Sharon, Litchfield, Connecticut. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-88048877 John White] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745558431 Prudence White]. He was a 
2 CONC Revolutionary War Veteran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Consider married [https://www.geni.com/profile-37688294 Sarah White] on October 4, 1788 in Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702766 Caroline B
2 CONC athsheba White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702778 Laura Canfield White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-87869565 Sarah Sallie Robbins]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37688170 Julianne Mariah Payne]; [https://www.geni.com/prof
2 CONC ile-34767993339 Julian Maurice White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702805 Clementine White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702847 Albert Augustus White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702834 William Augustus White]; [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/profile-37702821 Albert Consider White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37702857 Fisher Ames White]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Consider married [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703611 Sarah T White] on July 18, 1819 in Greenwich, Washington, New York, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703799 George Hen
2 CONC ry White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703823 Mary Augusta White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703848 Noah Washburn White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703880 Darwin Washburn White]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-37703
2 CONC 867 James Teft White]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on January 6, 1837 in Greenwich, Washington, New York, United States and was buried after January 6, 1837 in Bottskill Baptist Church Cemetery. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/155199807/person/172247257237 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 9 2020, 6:53:44 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1) Anne Kaufman, Ph.D., Augsburg College, Minneapolis, MN (Sep 2008). Cites: (a) "Families of Early Hartford," p.635. (b) Pension application file, frame 0135, Revolutionary war pension and bounty-land-warrant application files
2 CONC  of the National Archives. Microfilm M-804. (c) Bottskill Baptist Church, Greenwich, Washington Co., N.Y. Copy of all tombstone inscriptions existing in 1901 made by Stuart C. Wade, Genealogist. (d) 1810 census, Troy, Rensselaer C
2 CONC o., NY, p.33. (e) 1820 census, Greenwich, Washington Co., NY. (f) Death notice of Asa Bigelow, Troy, NH "Daily Whig," 24 Jul 1849. (g) "Troy's 100 Years:1789-1889," by James Arthur Weise (William H. Young, Troy, NY, 1891) p.324.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: (1) 12 Aug 1763. Sharon, Litchfield Co., CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage to Sarah WASHBURN: (1a) 4 Oct 1788. Harford, Harford Co., CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marriage to Sarah TEFFT: (1b,f,g)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Death: (1b,c) 6 Jan 1837. Greenwich, Washington Co., NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Burial: (1c) Bottskill Baptist Church, Greenwich, Washington Co., NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1b) 1782, 1 Apr: Consider WHITE enlisted to serve in the Revolutionary War. Served 12 months as a private in Captain STRONG's Company, Colonel SWIFT's CT Regiment.
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1g) 1809-1812: A Troy, NY firewarden.
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1d) 1810: C. WHITE was living in Troy, Rensselaer Co., NY. In household were 3 males 0-9 (Albert, William, Fisher); one male 10-15 (unknown); one male 16-25 (unknown); one male over age 45 (Consider WHITE); three females 10-15 
2 CONC (Sarah, Julianna, Clementina); two females 16-25 (Bathsheba, Laura); one female 26-44 (wife Sarah).
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1f) A merchant operating in company with his brother-in-law, Asa BIGELOW.
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1e) 1820: Consider WHITE was living in Greenwich, Washington Co., NY. In household were two males 10-15 (Fisher, Albert); one male 16-18 (William); two males 19-25 (unknown); one male over 45 (Consider); one female 10-15 (unkno
2 CONC wn); three females 16-25 (daughters Sarah, one unknown; wife Sarah).
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1b) 1832: Applied for pension. Resident of Greenwich, Washington Co., NY.
2 CONT
