2 CONC ia Ann, 1, born Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 U.S. Census, Ohio, Licking county, Hartford township, dwelling 975; Amos Vansickle, 26, tailor, born Ohio; Julia A. Vansickle, 23, born New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 U.S. Census, Missouri, Clark county, Jackson township, dwelling 1738; Hiram Payne, 67, farmer, born New York; Julia M., 63, born New York; Hiram, 23, born Ohio. Included in the dwelling; Julia A. Vansickle, 32, born Ohio; Jul
2 CONC ia C. Vansickle, 11, born Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 U.S. Census, Missouri, Sullivan county, Buchanan township, dwelling 101; George Keller, 60, farmer, born Virginia; Julia C., 44, born Ohio; Josephine, 8, born Missouri; Emory E., 6, born Missouri; Maud, 4, born Missouri. Incl
2 CONC uded in the household is Julia Vansickle, 21, domestic, born Ohio; Hiram Paine, 77, born New York; Hiram Paine Jr., 36, farm laborer, born Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiler's note 1: From the above, it is assumed the Julia A. Vansickle, 32 in 1860 is a daughter of Hiram Payne. She apparently lost her husband Amos Vansickle shown above in the 1850 Ohio census. It is assumed the Julia Vansickl
2 CONC e, 11, in 1860 and 21 in 1870 is a daughter of Amos and Julia Vansickle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiler's note 2: It is assumed the Julia Vansickle, 32 in 1860 is Julia, wife of George Keller in 1870. This assumption is based on the fact that her father Hiram and brother Hiram are in the same 1870 household; as well as her 
2 CONC daughter Julia Vansickle, 21.
