2 CONT Originally spelled Morrison in England.  He and his children adopted the Morris spelling. ! QUESTION:In 1st ref. below, Bowen lists his parents as Thomas Morris and Grissie Hewsone.  NEHGR research believes this is not right but a
2 CONC nother line. ! DEATH: Descrepancy in death date 4/14 Sept 1689 or 1690. ! BIOGRAPHY: Immigrated to N.E. by 23 Feb 1652/3. Was granted land in Roxbury, MA, 25 Feb 1652, and then was one of the Original settlers of Woodstock, Windha
2 CONC m, Connecticut. ! MARRIAGE: 20:9:55, by Mr. Richard Bellingham, Deputy Governor, Boston. ! REFERENCES: "Genealogies of Woodstock Families," Bowen, VII:453-4. Family Researcher: Laura E.M. Rappleye, S.L.C. NEHGR 146:3:275-278, Jul 
2 CONC 1992. NEHGR 11:201, 1857, "Early Records of Boston" (Marriage). NEHGR 18:227, "Origin of Woodstock, CT & Names of 1st Settlers."
2 CONT
2 CONT !Roxbury constable,selectman and Deputy to General Ct;among the 1st settlers of Woodstock CT;parents could have been Thomas Morris and Grissie Hewsone of Waltham Abbey,Essex ENG;
2 CONT
2 CONT !Chr in Holy Cross Abby, Dea.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adopted Morris vs. Morrison
2 CONT He was christened at Great Amwell, Co.Hertfordshire on Jan 22, 1631/2, the son of Edward Morris/Morrison and Prudence (Heath) Morris/Morrison. See NEHGR 146:277 for most recent research.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistaken Identity of Parents The history of this Morris line was published in 1887 after being excellently compiled by Jonathan Flynt Morris.  It is titled "A Genealogical and Historical Register of the Descendants of Edward Morr
2 CONT
