1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Grace Bett Morris=
2 CONT * BIRTH August 30, 1634 Roxbury, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 6 Jun 1705 (aged 70–71) Roxbury, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Woodstock Hill Cemetery, Woodstock, Windham County, Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 11446920  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT The origin of Grace Bett(?) is unknown and Torrey's marriage index suggests four versions of the surname.  On November 20, 1655 at Boston, Massachusetts, Grace married Edward Morris 1632 - 1689 son of Edward Morrison & Prudence He
2 CONC ath [2] They had at least nine children together before he died in 1690.[3] Grace died at Roxbury on June 6, 1705.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Through, Grace Betts and Lieutenant Edward Morris. Their daughter, Margaret Morris is related to Margaret, Both Grace and Edward Morris were early settlers of Woodstock, Connecticut. “The breaking out of King William’s war in 1689
2 CONC  aroused fresh apprehension of Indian assault.” “In the sense of our great hazard and danger, and our incapacity to defend ourselves,” the inhabitants of New Roxbury met together and organized as a military company, making choice 
2 CONC of Edward Morris for lieutenant.” [20]
2 CONT
2 CONT "How long our good but distant grandmother, Grace, the widow of Edward Morris, remained in Woodstock we do not know. We find her death, June 6, 1705, recorded in Roxbury, where, perhaps, she may have returned either to visit or ma
2 CONC ke her home with her married daughters, the Childs, or with her son Samuel. The place of her burial is not known. The compiler supposes it to have been in the ancient burying-ground at the corner of Washington and Eustis streets i
2 CONC n Roxbury, or possibly in the buring-ground at West Roxbury Village,; but no stone marks it in either place." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Lieut. Edward Morris 1632–1690 m. 11/20/1655 in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Isaac Morris 9/16/1656- m Hannah Mayo
2 CONT Susannah Morris Clayton 1654–1710
2 CONT Dea. Edward Morris Jr. 3/10/1658–1727 m Elizabeth Bowen
2 CONT Grace Morris Child 2/7/1661–1723 m Benjamin Child
2 CONT Lieut Ebenezer Morris 4/14/1664–1718 m Sarah Davis
2 CONT Elizabeth Morris Child 3/25/1666–1752 m Joshua Child
2 CONT Margaret Morris Johnson 9/25/1668–1750 m Dea John Johnson
2 CONT Samuel Morris 3/19/1671–1745  m Mehitable Mayo
2 CONT Martha Philbrick Morris Lyon 1/30/1675–1756 m Dea William Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT A previous version of this profile had her as daughter of Thomas Betts (of Connecticut) and Mary Bridge. There is no evidence that Thomas of Connecticut had a daughter Grace, nor is there evidence that he was ever in Roxbury, Mass
2 CONC achusetts. Not a known daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Betts-of-Norwalk/6000000006802928410?through=5678779172790103812.  Her surname is from the Boston marriage record, but her parentage or origins are not known to
2 CONC  me at this time.  Grace Morris formerly Bett aka Bell, Burr [uncertain].  While her husband is buried in Woodstock,CT, the reference to her on the monument is likely a cenotaph. [9]   
2 CONT
2 CONT Since https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Bell-of-Roxbury/6000000083650032261 was in Roxbury at the same time as Edward Morris, it's possible Grace was a Bell and lived in his household, though she is not listed as one of his child
2 CONC ren. Thomas mentions many relatives and friends in his will, even his maid, but no Grace.  There are a number of people in this time frame that have the last name "Bett or Bell", which shows that the two names can be confused. Sin
2 CONC ce extensive research has not found a Grace Bett or a Bett(s) family matching the dates and places of this Grace, her name might have been Grace Bell [4,9]  Possibly she was a servant in another Roxbury household.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is likely not the daughter of Thomas Betts and Mary (Unknown) Betts or sister of Thomas Betts Jr., Mary (Betts) Raymond, John Betts, Hannah (Betts) Camp, Stephen Betts, Daniel Betts I, Samuel Isaac Betts, James Betts and Sarah
2 CONC  (Betts) St. John.  v, Edward [Morris], bp. at Great Amwell 22 Jan 1631/2; d. at Woodstock,Conn. shortly before 27 Oct. 1690; m. at Boston, Mass., 20 Nov 1655,''' GRACE BETT''', who d at Roxbury 6 June 1705.
2 CONT
