1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[Curator note]
2 CONT >This profile represents '''Sarah Chamberlain''' (1649–1717) of Roxbury. It must remain distinct from contemporary "Sarah Chamberlains" in Chelmsford or Hull. Her identity is anchored by her 1649 Woburn birth and her 1717 Roxbury 
2 CONC death record. The 1673 "triple birth" entries of children (Joseph, Sarah, Elizabeth) are consistent with post-war record clustering in the Roxbury VR and should be maintained as a single sibling group to prevent identity conflatio
2 CONC n with later generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah (Chamberlain) Davis (1649–1717) was a colonial resident of the Massachusetts Bay Colony. Born on December 18, 1649, in Woburn, Middlesex County, she was the daughter of Edmund Chamberlain and Mary Turner. While some secondar
2 CONC y sources erroneously cite a 1648 christening in "Norfolk County," primary records and jurisdictional history confirm her birth in the Middlesex cluster followed by her removal to Roxbury, Suffolk County, where she spent her adult
2 CONC  life.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Estate
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 28, 1670, Sarah married Joseph Davis, Sr. (1647–1717). Joseph was a husbandman and landholder in the Roxbury/Brookline area. Their household remained a stable agrarian unit through the disruptions of King Philip’s War (
2 CONC 1675–1678), eventually serving as the generational anchor for the family's 18th-century expansion into Worcester County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The 1717 Mortality Event
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah’s life concluded during a localized epidemic in December 1717—likely smallpox or malignant pleurisy.  The Roxbury Vital Records document a "triple death" within the immediate family that serves as a rare forensic "weld" for 
2 CONC genealogical auditing:
2 CONT
2 CONT * December 23, 1717: Death of her eldest son, Joseph Davis, Jr. (the Cordwainer) (Case #3918).
2 CONT * December 25, 1717: Simultaneous death of Sarah and her husband, Joseph, Sr. (Case #3917).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment is established at the '''Eliot Burying Ground''' (First Burial Ground) in Roxbury. While individual headstones for Sarah and Joseph Sr. are no longer extant, the residency of the Davis family in this specific yard is sub
2 CONC stantiated by the nearby surviving headstone of Joseph’s brother, John Davis (1643–1705).
2 CONT * Cemetery Link: [https://www.findagrave.com/cemetery/712231/eliot-burying-ground Eliot Burying Ground] (Find A Grave)
2 CONT * Family Anchor: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/65040762/john-davis John Davis Memorial] (Find A Grave #65040762) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family Register
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Joseph Davis, Sr. (1647–1717), son of William Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph Sr. and Sarah (Chamberlain) Davis, births recorded at Roxbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph Davis, Jr. (1673–1717); m. (1) Sarah [Unknown], (2) Elizabeth Lane.
2 CONT # Sarah Davis (b. 1673); m. [First Name] Morris.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Davis (1673–1753); m. Benjamin Sabin.
2 CONT # Mary Davis (b. 1675); m. George Warner.
2 CONT # Unnamed Daughter (d. 21 Jan 1680); Died Young.
2 CONT # Unnamed Child (d. 10 Mar 1680); Died Young.
2 CONT # Hannah Davis (b. 1680); m. John Allen.
2 CONT # Benjamin Davis (b. 1682); m. Anne Robinson.
2 CONT # Mehitable Davis (b. 1684); m. Jonathan Mayo.
2 CONT # Rachel Davis (b. 1687); m. Samuel Truesdell.
2 CONT # Abigail Davis (b. 1688); m. John Sabin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Research Notes: Conflict Resolution 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources citing a 1713 burial in Boston or a 1648 christening refer to separate individuals and are chronologically incompatible with this verified lineage.
2 CONT
2 CONT * The 1648 Christening: Rejected as chronologically inconsistent with the 1649 birth record (Woburn VR). It is likely a conflation with a child of Thomas or William Chamberlain.
2 CONT * The 1713 Burial: Rejected based on the Suffolk County Probate Case #3917 and the 1717 Roxbury Vital Records. Sarah (Chamberlain) Davis was alive in 1717 to witness the death of her son Joseph Jr.; her recorded death is 25 Dec 17
2 CONC 17.
2 CONT * Jurisdictional Error: The FamilySearch entry cites "Roxbury, Norfolk" for 1649. As noted, Norfolk did not exist until 1793; the 1649 birth occurred in Middlesex (Woburn) and the marriage in Suffolk (Roxbury).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Digital Audit Notes
2 CONT >Profile audited April 2026 to resolve "Identity Smash-ups" involving unverified sources citing a 1713 burial or anachronistic "Norfolk County" origins. Jurisdictional accuracy for Suffolk County (Roxbury) and Middlesex County (Wo
2 CONC burn) has been restored. Sibling spouses for Morris, Allen, Robinson, Mayo, and Truesdell have been cross-referenced with both Brayton and Verhulst datasets.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == References and Sources ==
2 CONT Primary Archival Records
2 CONT * Massachusetts Vital Records (to 1850): Woburn: Birth of Sarah Chamberlain, 18 Dec 1649 (Vol. 1, p. 48).
2 CONT * Roxbury: Marriage of Joseph Davis and Sarah Chamberlain, 28 Oct 1670 (Vol. 2, p. 106).
2 CONT * Roxbury: Deaths of Joseph Jr. (23 Dec 1717), Joseph Sr. (25 Dec 1717), and Sarah (25 Dec 1717) (Vol. 2, p. 501).
2 CONT * Suffolk County Probate Records: Estate of Joseph Davis, Sr. (Jan 1717/18), Case #3917. Estate of Joseph Davis, Jr. (Dec 1717), Case #3918.
2 CONT Secondary Genealogical Authorities
2 CONT * Brayton, John Anderson. The Complete Ancestry of Tennessee Williams. Winston-Salem, NC: J.A. Brayton, 1993. p. 52. (Confirms the 1649/1717 dates and parental link to Edmund Chamberlain).
2 CONT * Davis, G. L. Samuel Davis of Oxford, Mass. and Joseph Davis of Dudley, Mass. Worcester, MA: Charles Hamilton, 1884.
2 CONT * Mayo, C. G. John Mayo of Roxbury, Massachusetts 1630-1688. Rutland, VT: Charles E. Tuttle Company, 1965.
2 CONT * Daniels, G. F. History of the Town of Oxford, Massachusetts. Oxford, MA: 1892.
2 CONT * Morse, A. A Register of the Descendants of Several Ancient Puritans, Vol. III. Boston: H.W. Dutton & Son, 1861.
2 CONT * Descendants of: Joseph Davis & Sarah Chamberlain (Register report) < [http://www.verhulsts.com/hollyshome/main/deF321.html link] > (has errors) 
