1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Davis of Roxbury By first wife, Elizabeth___, who was buried May 4, 1658. They had: John, b. Oct 1, 1643; Samuel, b. Feb. 21, 1645; Joseph, b. Oct. 12, 1647;
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Primary Death Evidence ==
2 CONT * '''Joseph Davis, Sr.''': ''Vital Records of Roxbury, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849'', Vol. 2, p. 501. "Davis, Joseph [Sr.], Dec. 25, 1717."
2 CONT * '''Sarah Chamberlain''': ''Vital Records of Roxbury, Massachusetts, to the End of the Year 1849'', Vol. 2, p. 501. "Davis, Sarah, w. Joseph, Dec. 25, 1717."
2 CONT
2 CONT === Identity Audit Note ===
2 CONT The simultaneous death of the parents on 25 Dec 1717, occurring two days after the death of their son Joseph Jr. (23 Dec 1717), provides the clinical evidence of a household contagion. This record serves as the definitive separato
2 CONC r between the parent generation and the children's subsequent  probate proceedings.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Archival Verification: The 1717 Mortality Event ==
2 CONT * '''Joseph Davis, Jr.''' (d. 23 Dec 1717) — Case #3918.
2 CONT * '''Joseph Davis, Sr.''' (d. 25 Dec 1717) — Case #3917.
2 CONT * '''Sarah (Chamberlain) Davis''' (d. 25 Dec 1717) — Wife of Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT If you look at the Suffolk County Probate for Joseph Sr. (which occurred at the same time as his son’s), you will see the family was forced to settle two generations of land and debt at once. This massive legal "reset" is likely w
2 CONC hy the brothers (Joseph III, Samuel, and Ebenezer) eventually decided to leave the "cursed" homestead in Roxbury and start fresh in Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Burial
2 CONT The Burial Site: While no individual headstones remain, they were almost certainly interred in the Eliot Burying Ground (First Burial Ground) in Roxbury, where the Davis family held traditional plots.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Curator Note on Identification ===
2 CONT The proximity of these deaths (within 48 hours) requires strict adherence to probate case numbers to prevent identity conflation. Sarah Chamberlain is identified as the wife of Joseph Sr. via their 1670 marriage record; she is dis
2 CONC tinct from the 'Sarah' who was the first wife of Joseph Jr.
