2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married Sarah Brown on 23 October 1755 in Pomfret, Windham, Connecticut, United States.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He served in the Revolutionary War as a Lieutenant in the New York Militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away in 1788.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was mentioned on a memorial in Cherry Valley Cemetery, Cherry Valley, Otsego County, New York, United States with a death date of 1788.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died Y. 31 DEC 1788. Cherry Valley, Otsego Co. NY. Note: Buriel: Cherry Valley, Otsego, New York, USA. Age: 61.
