1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Seth William Paine=
2 CONT * BIRTH 20 Aug 1690 Rehoboth, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 18 Jan 1772 (aged 81) Pomfret, Windham County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL South Cemetery, Pomfret, Windham County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 81020984
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Samuel & Anne Paine's son Seth was born 20 Aug 1690 in Rehoboth, Bristol, Massachusetts Bay.[2][3]  Seth Paine entered his intentions to marry Mary Morris of Woodstock on 16 April 1718 in Woodstock, Connecticut. [4] and married he
2 CONC r in Pomfret, Connecticut, on 03 June 1719. [5] [6]  Mary & Seth Paine had 10 children together all born in Pomfret, Connecticut.  Seth is buried in south Cemetery, Pomfret, Windham, Connecticut [3] living to age 81.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seth was a petitioner to the General Court in 1713 for a town organization in Pomfret. In 1739 he subscribed £10 to the United Library for the Propagation of Christian and Useful Knowledge in Pomfret. Seth took a leading part in t
2 CONC he affairs of Pomfret and was a patron of education. Many of his descendants lived in Vermont. [1]
2 CONT
