1 NAME Isaac /Cummings/ Sr.
2 GIVN Isaac
2 SURN Cummings
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Cummings
2 NICK Isaack Commen
2 NICK Isahk Commin
2 NICK Deacon Isaac Cummings
2 NICK Isaack Cummings
1 NAME Isaac Cumings /Sr./
1 NAME Deacon Isaac Cummings, of Easthorpe & Topsfield
1 SEX M
1 OCCU unknown
2 PLAC Grandjuryman, deacon, freeman May 18, 1642 farmer, constable
2 ADDR
1 BAPM
2 DATE 5 APR 1601
2 PLAC Easthorpe, Essex Co., ENG
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 APR 1601
2 PLAC Easthorpe, Essex Co., England
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 1677
2 PLAC Topsfield, Essex, Mass
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 22 MAY 1677
2 PLAC Topsfield, Essex Co., MA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU to No.Am. ~1636; to Ipswich 1638
1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr01/rr01_457.html#P62148
2 CONT
2 CONT Family of John Cummin (618) & Amy Greene:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Cummings married Anne. Anne died in Topsfield, MA ca 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Isaac Cummings (Died soon) (ca 1629-May 1629)
2 CONT #John Cummings (ca 1630-1 Dec 1700)
2 CONT #Dea. Isaac Cummings (ca 1632/3-Jan 1721)
2 CONT #Anne Cummings (ca 1634/5-29 Jun 1689)
2 CONT #Elizabeth Cummings (ca 1637-9 Jul 1679)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT © Isaac Cummings Family Association 2016 Isaac CUMMINGS aka Isaack COMMEN 1601-1677
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Cummings came from England to this country in October, 1635. The first mention of his name in Middlesex County records is an entry made by the town clerk of Watertown as receiving a grant of 35 acres in the earliest general 
2 CONC land grants in 1636 called the "Great Dividends". Also, a record exists made by the Town Clerk of Ipswich, showing that he owned a planting lot near Reedy marsh, in that town, previous to July 25, 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 9th of the second month (April) of 1639, he also owned a house lot in Ipswich village on the street called the East End, next to the lot owned by Rev. Nathaniel Rogers. He was a commoner in 1639, and the same year sold 7 ac
2 CONC res of land near the highway leading to Jeffrey's Neck to Andrew Hodges. He also possessed, in 1639, land adjoining John Winthrop and William Goodhue, the farm being partly in Ipswich and partly in Topsfield. He was a proprietor i
2 CONC n Watertown in 1642, and at Topsfield afterward, where he was one of 30 commoners.
2 CONT
2 CONT As an Ipswich commoner he was one of those "that have the right of commonage there the last of the last month (Feb), 1641", and was made a freemanin Watertown May 18, 1642. On the first day of the second month (April), 1652,Isaac 
2 CONC Cummings, for 30 pounds, bought of Samuel Symonds, 150 acres of land, "being the North-east corner of his farm called Ollivers". This lot of land was in Topsfield and bounded on the west and north-west by land lately of John Winth
2 CONC rop, on the south and west by land of Francis Peabody, and on the south by land of Daniel Clark.
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm began at what is known as the Hobbs-Bell place, and continued down both sides of the brook, then called "Winthropps", to what is now called Howlett's Brook, one hundred acres lying on the westerly side and fifty acres on 
2 CONC the easterly side, probably joining other land belonging to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several court records of him:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1."Goodman Isaac Cummings of Topsfield, having claimed ownership of a heifer in the possession of John Fuller and driven same to his home" had suit brought against him, March 28, 1654.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Isaac Comings, senior was witness against Wm. Duglas, March1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Isaac Commins, senior was sued for debt by Zerobabell Phillips of Ipswich March 1657.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Isaac Cummings, senior brought suit against John Fuller for damage done in his corn by swine belonging to said Fuller, Dec. 31, 1656. In 1666 he was constable, and his son Isaac was his deputy, and in a deposition he made in Mar
2 CONC ch, 1666, he states his age to be 65. The same year he was assed 4 s. 7d. to pay the town's indebtedness. He was deacon of the church for many years and was chosen grand juryman in 1675.  He was a moderator of the Town meeting in 
2 CONC 1676. His estate was valued at about 166 pounds. No trace of his wife's family name is found. She was not living at the time of his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Albert Oren Cummins book, augmented with additional information from the Mooar book.
2 CONT
2 CONT © Isaac Cummings Family Association 2016 Children of Isaac and Anne Cummings
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac CUMMINGS - immigrant b: 1601 of Mistley, Essex, England baptized Easthorpe, Essex, England on 5 April 1601 d: Abt. May 22, 1677 in Topsfield, Essex Co, MA +Anne (unknown)d: Bef. 1677
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac and Anne had five children, as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaack CUMMINGS (dired as an infant) b: Bef. May 20, 1629 in Mistley, Essex, England d: Bef. May 23, 1629 in Mistley, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT John CUMMINGS b: Bef. May 09, 1630 in Mistley, Essex, England d: December 01, 1700 in Dunstable, Middlesex Co, MA +Sarah HOWLETT b: March 03, 1633/34 in Ipswich, Essex Co, MA m: December 01, 1655 in Boxford, Essex Co, MA d: Decemb
2 CONC er 07, 1700 in Dunstable, Middlesex Co, MA Father: Thomas HOWLETT Mother: Alice FRENCH
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac CUMMINGS b: Bef. March 17, 1632/33 in Mistley, Essex, England d: June 1721 +Mary ANDREWS b: 1638 in Topsfield, Essex, Massachusetts m: November 27, 1659 d: Bef. 1712 Father: Robert ANDREWS Mother: Grace MELBURN
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann CUMMINGS b: Bef. February 22,1634/35 in Mistley, Essex, England d: June 29, 1689 in Enfield, Essex Co, CT +John PEASE, Jr b: Bef. February 11,1630/31 in Great Baddow, Essex, England m: October 08, 1669in Salem, Essex Co, MA d:
2 CONC  July 08, 1689 in Enfield, Essex Co, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth CUMMINGS b: Abt. 1637 in probably Watertown, Middlesex Co, MA d: July 09, 1679 in Ipswich, Essex Co, MA +John JEWETT b: Abt. 1637 m: February 02, 1660/61 in Rowley, Essex Co, MA d: Aft. November 29,1708
