1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nathaniel Pease (1643 - 1714)''', son of Robert Pease and Mary Rodans, was baptized 15 October 1643 at Salem, Essex County, Massachusetts, but was probably born in England. He died about the age of 71, around 17
2 CONC 14. Nathaniel’s wife Mary Hobbs Pease was born 1646 in Salem. It is believed that the Mary Pease of the Salem Witch Trials was his wife, though there are no records of her trial. If they had children is unknown, there being no rec
2 CONC ord of issue. He was a participant of King Philip’s War in 1675, and was still living in 1714.
