2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 65262161
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (Unknown) Pease* (abt. 1580 - bef. 1645)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was married to Frances Weston; presumably a second marriage for both. Prior to her marriage to Frances, she is thought by some to have been married to a gentleman by the surname of Reeves*, who would have been the father 
2 CONC of Margaret's daughter, Lucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1630, she, Frances, and her daughter, Lucy emigrated to the America with the Winthrop fleet. Frances Weston was an early leader of the colony, a deputy of the court, and a land owner, but soon the Weston's, who were followers o
2 CONC f Samuel Gorton, found themselves in conflict with religious authorities.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1637, Margaret, along with her husband, was sued by William Pester for defamation. She accused the pastors of the church of hypocrisy, and was in turn accused of disorderly carriage by the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 5, 1638, she was sentenced by the General Court to be set in the bilboes, two hours in Boston, and two hours in Salem upon a lecture day, and was also banished to Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to her death, she became "of hopelessly unsound mind". 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igmpostem.cgi?op=show&app=merrygo&notify=Zu0X0rH-DIBfswYSQ3_C0iYQFQhuUeOo&key=I1724&return=%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fcgi%2Dbin%2Figm%2Ecgi%3Fop%3DGET%26amp%3Bdb%3Dmerrygo%26amp%3Bid%3DI1724%22
2 CONC %3EReturn+to+WorldConnect%3C%2Fa%3E Postem]
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the book, "Genealogical Register of Plymouth Families" is the following entry under Weston: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "FRANCIS, came to Plymouth with Roger Williams and went with him to Rhode Island. He m. Margaret Reeves, 1640, and died 1645, childless." 
2 CONT
2 CONT There was another Francis Weston b. abt 1610 who married a Margery Reeves in 1639 or so- but these were different people than Sir Francis Weston b.1586 and Margaret ? b.abt 1585, and married before 1630 in England. They do have th
2 CONC e two Mr. Westons mixed up here because Sir Francis Weston (stepfather to Lucy Weston) did die in 1645 childless, but the Francis Weston (sometimes called Francis West) and Margery Reeves married in 1640 went on to have children.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Great Migration Project as posted by Linda Mac on [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=65262161 FindAGrave:]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''(comment: this bio seems to be a mixup with John Pease's "mother in law" '''Margaret''', widow of Francis Weston & mother of his wife)''
2 CONT
2 CONT There are two competing versions of [http://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Pease/6000000007680189221?through=6000000021138033640 Margaret's] later history, each of which has its problems. We prefer the first of these two stories. On
2 CONC  3 November 1635 it was ordered "that John Pease shall be whipped, & bound to his good behavior, for striking his mother, Mrs. Weston, & deriding of her, & for diverse other misdemeanors, & other evil carriages." On 1 September 16
2 CONC 44 "Margit Pease" of Salem made a will in which the principal beneficiaries were the children of her son Robert Pease; this will was proved on 1 January 1644/5. For this to be the widow of Francis Weston, we would have to assume t
2 CONC hat he had died before 1 September 1644 (and there is nothing to contradict this), and that after his death she had returned to Salem and reassumed the name of an earlier husband. Richard Harcourt, who later held some of the land 
2 CONC of Francis Weston, noted that Margaret had held a life interest in these lands, so there should not have been a competing claim from her Pease heirs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The second story is that she married (2) by early 1651 Adam Goodwin, was supported by the town because of her distracted condition, and died on 2 May 1651. This later history for Margaret is dependent on a letter of Roger Williams
2 CONC  in which in early 1651 he mistakenly called her "Mrs. Weston" when she was already married to Adam Goodwin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links 
2 CONT * http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=103121254
2 CONT
