2 CONT John Pease (bef. 1608 - aft. 1677)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born before 20 Nov 1608 in Great Baddow, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT ANCESTORS
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Robert Pease Sr and Margaret (Unknown) Pease
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Robert Pease II
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Lucy (Unknown) Pease — married before 1637 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Unknown) Pease — married before 1653 in Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT DESCENDANTS
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of James Pease Sr., Samuel Pease, Thomas Pease and Sarah (Pease) Capron
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 25 Sep 1677 in Enfield, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile managers: Jillaine Smith, Puritan Great Migration Project WikiTree, Michael Sanderson, and Gordon Ralls 
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 17 Nov 2018 | Created 14 Sep 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT The Puritan Great Migration. John Pease migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640). Join: Puritan Great Migration Project Discuss: PGM Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pease was baptized Great Baddow, Essex, England, 20 November 1608, son of Robert Pease.[1]and Margaret (____) Pease who arrived in Salem at an unknown date. His brother was Robert Pease who arrived at Salem in 1635.
2 CONT
2 CONT John migrated to New England in 1634 on the Francis of Ipswich. Children under the care were listed as Fayth Clearke, aged 15; Robert Pease, aged 3; and Darcas Greene, aged 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first resided at Salem, then moved to Edgartown on Martha's Vineyard by 1646.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a land-owner, both at Salem and at Edgartown with the occupation as that of a husbandman/farmer. At Edgartown he held the office of constable on November 7, 1653.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1637 he had married Lucy _____.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Lucy James Pease was born March 15, 1637/8 He married (1) Elizabeth Norton, daughter of Nicholas Norton. He married (2nd) Abigail (Travis) Covell on April 22, 1706. John Pease was born about 1640. From his fat
2 CONC her's will he received land at New London and lived there in 1672. By about 1657 John had married Mary _____. She married (2nd) by 1688 a man with the surname Creber, and possibly his first name was Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Mary (birth order estimated) Thomas Pease was born about 1657. He married by 1685 Bathsheba Merry, daughter of Joseph Merry. Abigail Pease was born about 1659. Mary Pease was born about 1661. Rebecca Pease was
2 CONC  born about 1663. Sarah Pease was born about 1665 and may have married John Doggett by 1686. Jonathan Pease was born about 1667. Samuel Pease was born about 1669 David was born about 1671. His will, dated March 4, 1674/5 bequeaths
2 CONC  inheritance to his two sons James and John by his first wife, his 2nd wife Mary and children Thomas, Jonathan, Samuell, David, Abigail, Mary, Rebecca and Sarah
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pease died after September 1677.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Pease[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT March the 4th, 1674. The last will and testament of me, John Peas, husbandman and inhabitant uppon Martins Vineyard in the Town called Edgartown, I John Peas having upon good consideration and being now in some measure in good hea
2 CONC lth and perfect understanding and memory though I am striken in years and Crasy in respect of what formerly, I having had two wives one formerly deceased and by her have yet two sons surv- iving, James Peas, & John Peas and these 
2 CONC two sonnes James the Elder, God hath been pleased to bless him in his labours & indeavours and I have been helpfull to him so that he is verry well to pass in his Estate farre beyond myself: I do therefore in this my last will and
2 CONC  testament give to my eldest Son James Peas twelve pence; My second son John Peas I have alreddy given unto and do hereby give unto him all that was given unto me at Mohegin, with that frame of a house I set up uppon some part of 
2 CONC that land; I say I give it unto my son John Peas & his heirs forever: I having by my now living wife Mary Peas, four sonnes & four Daughters, my Sonnes Thomas Peas Jonathan, Samuell, and David and my Daughters Abygaill Peas, Mary,
2 CONC  Rebecca, and Sarah Peas unto these my four Sonnes and four Daughters I doe give all my landes and houseing that I have upon this Iland Martins Vineyard to be either equally devided or valued or sold or exchanged and the price the
2 CONC reof Equally devided to everyone of them alike and this to be performed at convenient age of them: or as my now living wife Mary shall see meet whome I make my full and whole Executrix to performe all this my last will and testame
2 CONC nt; and I give unto whatsoever I have more or less for her use and comfort and helpfulness in bringing up my children at her disposing for Ever. In witness hereunto my hand and seal. JOHN PEAS. Further I give and bequeath unto my 
2 CONC second son John Peas twelve pence. Wee whose names are underwritten are witnesses to this will and testament. Thomas Birchard, Kathrin Birchard, Thomas Trappe, 
2 CONT
