2 CONT * Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Deliverance-Longley/6000000009161345529
2 CONT * Seen as wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Jonathan-Crispe/6000000000859863119?through=6000000030507925315 - disproved
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliverance Pease  b. 6 Dec 1673 at Salem MA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From * Pease, Elaine K., "Goody Pease of Salem Town,"  (The Essex Genealogist, August, 1984 (vol. 4, no. 3), pp. 126-135.) [http://www.spicerweb.org/genealogy/pease/PeaseElaineGoodyPease.pdf PDF]
2 CONT
2 CONT >The second daughters named Deliverance and Bethiah would have been 18 and 16, respectively, and it is likely  they were '''unmarried''' at the time of their mother's arrest (1692).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Could not have been the wife of Jonathan Crispe:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Jonathan Crispe, b. Jan 29, 1640 and died unmarried before Oct 25, 1680
2 CONT
2 CONT Miner Descent has:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan’s wife '''Deliverance Pease''' was born 16 Oct 1664 in Salem, Essex, Mass. Her parents were Robert PEASE – The Former and Sarah [SEDGWICK?]. Deliverance died 27 Jul 1694 in Groton, Middlesex, Mass (this is the death date 
2 CONC for Jonathan’s sister  https://www.geni.com/people/Deliverance-Longley/6000000009161345529)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name seen as “Lydia Pease Mansell”  in online trees.  
2 CONT
