1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Ancestry of Lydia Harmon": Page 42 - 44 [https://books.google.com/books?id=Y61RAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA121&ots=iY5m1Pe5mD&dq=Esther%20(Goodale)%20Sturdivant&pg=PA42#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. ZACHARIAH3 GOODALE (Isaac2, Robert1) was born in Salem May 15, 1675. In January, 1698/9, his mother and brother conveyed to him ten acres of his late father's farm as his share of the estate, and two weeks later he sold this pr
2 CONC operty to Zachariah White of Lynn for thirteen pounds. In this same year, 1699, he settled in Wells, in the Province of Maine, then and for many years to come a frontier post against French and Indian attack, and on May 22, 1700, 
2 CONC he married there Elizabeth Cousins, a daughter of Thomas Cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT Goodale's first purchase of land in Wells was from William Webb -- a lot on the main highway of the village, near the Ogunquit river, eleven or twelve rods in breadth and stretching back into the country two miles. This was in 169
2 CONC 9. In 1716 he added to this the next lot to the westward, twenty rods in breadth, purchased from the Drisco heirs. The highway to Berwick was the western boundary of the large farm which resulted from the joining of these two lots
2 CONC . He also owned a one-hundred acre tract west of the Ogunquit river, which had been a town grant to Francis Littlefield, Jr., and which was sold to him by David Littlefield, a son of the grantee. He sold this land to Gershom Maxey
2 CONC  in 1717. He also purchased smaller lots on the river from Richard Stimson and Eliab Littlefield. On Dec. 30, 1734, the proprietors of the town, of whom he was one, confirmed his title to the Webb and Drisco lots by grant. He deed
2 CONC ed a portion of his land to his son Zachariah in 1735, and conveyed the homestead and farm to his son John, in return for maintenance, in 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Cousins) Goodale conveyed her share in her father's estate to her brother Ichabod in 1717. She died before 1747, when, on July 27, Zachariah Goodale's intention to marry Abigail Tarrott was published. She was the widow 
2 CONC of James Tarrott of Peaks Island, Falmouth, and was about sixty-seven years of age at the time of her second marriage. She was living in 1757.
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of Zachariah Goodale's death is not known, and the settlement of his estate is not recorded. Of his children two of the sons are identified by deeds and the birth of one of his daughters is entered in the town book. There
2 CONC  can be no doubt, however, that the five others listed below were his children as no other family of the name had settled in Wells or in Maine at that time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT
2 CONT i. ELIZABETH, b. July 28, 1703; m. Samuel Littlefield, son of Dependance and Elizabeth (Batson) Littlefield of Wells, March, 172
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT * 1. Phoebe Littlefield, bapt. Feb. 20, 1725/
2 CONT * 2. Samuel Littlefield, bapt. May 28, 1726/
2 CONT * 3. Elizabeth Littlefield, bapt. Nov. 16, 1728/
2 CONT * 4. Dependance Littlefield, bapt. April 9, 173
2 CONT * 5. Dorothy Littlefield, bapt. June 30, 173
2 CONT * 6. Daniel Littlefield, bapt. Aug. 1, 1735/
2 CONT * 7. Stephen Littlefield, bapt. Feb. 4, 1737/8.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. ABIGAIL, bapt. (adult) Jan. 30, 1725/6; m. William Low, int. Nov. 12, 1726.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT * 1. Esther Low, bapt. June 15, 1728/
2 CONT * 2. William Low, bapt. Sept. 24, 173
2 CONT * 3. John Low, bapt. March 14, 1735/
2 CONT * 4. Sarah Low, bapt. Dec. 31, 173
2 CONT * 5. Phebe Low, bapt. April 4, 1741/2.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. ESTHER, bapt. (adult) Jan. 30, 1725/6; m. Jonathan Sturdivant, Oct. 19, 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. HANNAH, m. Nathaniel Harmon Nov. 30, 1727. (See Harmon
2 CONT
2 CONT v. ZACHARIAH. He m. Elizabeth Littlefield, a daughter of Josiah and Elizabeth (Hilton) Littlefield of Wells, Nov. 26, 1730. He was made a proprietor of the town in 1734 and was constable in 1737. It was apparently very soon after 
2 CONC his death that his widow published her intention to marry Samuel Stewart, a housewright of Wells, on May 2, 1752. They were appointed administrators of his estate on Oct. 17, 1752, and returned an inventory showing property valued
2 CONC  at 268: 1: 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT * 1. Bathsheba, bapt. Sept. Sept. 8, 1734; m. John Hatc son of Samuel and Mary (Littlefield) Hatch of Wells, int. Dec. 2, 1749.
2 CONT * 2. Zachariah, bapt. Sept. 8, 173
2 CONT * 3. Tabitha, bapt. March 9, 1734/
2 CONT * 4. Tabitha, bapt. June 26, 1737; unm. in 1760.(
2 CONT * 5. Zachariah, bapt. April 5, 1739; m. Mehitable Stewa April 9, 1760.
2 CONT * 6. Esther, bapt. July 19, 1741; m. William Deland, in Dec. 12, 1761.
2 CONT * 7. Samuel, bapt. April 23, 174
2 CONT * 8. Elizabeth, bapt. Aug. 11, 174
2 CONT * 9. Meribah, bapt. May 3, 1747; pub. with John Holm June 15, 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. CATHERINE. She m. Samuel Harmon Aug. 20, 1733. (See Harmon
2 CONT
2 CONT vii. JOSEPH. He m. Mary Matthews Oct. 12, 1738. A Mary Goodale, possibly his widow, m. William Deland, int. Sept. 24, 1753.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Joseph, bapt. July 29, 1739; m. Dorcas Stevens Fe 26, 1760.
2 CONT * 2. A daughter, bapt. Jan. 3, 174
2 CONT * 3. Thomas, bapt. March 25, 174
2 CONT * 4. Daniel, bapt. April 26, 1746/7.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. JOHN. He m. Elizabeth Littlefield Dec. 4, 1740. His will, dated Jan. 7, and probated April 8, 1771, leaves to his wife his homestead and negro servants, and mentions the children listed below.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:--
2 CONT * 1. Jedediah, executor of his father's estat
2 CONT * 2. John, bapt. May 23, 1742; m. Grace Came of York Nov. 20, 1769.
2 CONT * 3. Sarah, bapt. Aug. 5, 1744.
2 CONT * 4. Betty, bapt. June 29, 1746; m. John Tibbets Feb. 8, 1770.
2 CONT * 5. Abraham, bapt. July 17, 1748; m. Irene Cousins, pub. May 2, 1772.
2 CONT * 6. Molly, bapt. Sept. 9, 1750; m. Aaron Burnham of Scarborough June 21, 1770.
2 CONT * 7. Hepsibah, bapt. May 27, 1753; m. John Tibbets March 11, 1773.
2 CONT * 8. Susanna; m. Jonathan Buzzell May 20, 177
2 CONT * 9. Lucy; m. Zachariah Goodale, Jr., Dec. 24, 1782 .
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT <p>Bought in Wells 1699 a lot on the main highway near Ogunquit River. In 1716 he added to it the Drisco lot adjacent. he deposed in July 1749, at about age 74, that he worked for the Cloyes about 1701. Grand jury 1703, jury 1708,
2 CONC  fence viewer 1721, 1723-24, constable 1712. In 1747 he conveyed his homestead to his son John for maintenance. [Noyes et al., p. 271] Town proprietor of Wells.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Zachariah goodale was born in Salem May 15, 1675. 
2 CONC In January, 1698/9, his mother and brother conveyed to him 10 acres of his late father's farm as his share of the estate, and two weeks later he sold this property to Zachariah White of Lynn for thirteen pounds. In this same year,
2 CONC  1699, he settled in Wells, in the province of Maine, then and formany years to come a frontier post against French and Indian attack, and on May 22, 1700 he married there Elizabeth Cousins, a daughter of Thomas Cousins.</p><p>&nb
2 CONC sp;</p><p>Goodale's first purchase of land in Wells was from William Webb--a loton the main highway of the village, near the Ogunquit river, eleven or twelve rods in breadth and streaching back into the country two miles. This was
2 CONC  in 1699. In 1716 he added to this the next lot to the westward, twenty rods in breadth, purchased from the Drisco heirs. The highway to Berwick was the western boundary of the large farm which resulted from the joining of these t
2 CONC wo lots. He also owned a one-hundred acre tract west of Ogunquit river, which had been a town grant to Francis Littlefield, Jr., and which was sold by David Littlefield, a son of the grantee. He sold this land to gershom Maxey in 
2 CONC 1717. He also purchased smaller lots on the river from Richard Stimson and Eliab Littlefield. On December, 30, 1734, the proprietors of the town, of whom he was one, confirmed his title to the Webb and Drisco lotsby grant. He deed
2 CONC ed a portion of his land to his son Zachariah in 1735, and conveyed the homestead and farm to his son John, in return for maintenance, in 1747.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Elizabeth [Cousins] Goodale conveyed her share in her father's esta
2 CONC te to her brother Ichabod in 1717. She died before 1747, when, on july 27, Zachariah Goodale's intention to marry Abigail Tarrottwas published. She was the widow of James Tarrott of Peaks Island, Falmouth, and was about sixty-seve
2 CONC n years of age at the time of her second marriage. She was living in 1757.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The date of Zachariah Goodale's death is not known, and the settlement of his estate is not recorded. Of his children two of the sons ar
2 CONC e identified by deeds and the birth of one of his daughters is entered in the town book. There can be no doubt, however, that the five others listed below were his children as no other family of the name had settled in Wells or in
2 CONC  Maine at that time. [The Ancestry of Lydia Harmon, pp. 42-43]</p><p>&nbsp;</p>Removes: 1699, Wells, York Co., Maine.
