2 CONC d numerous town offices. For some years he was town clerk, from 1744 to 1748. With him began the change in the orthography of the surname. It had been Batcheller, but afterwards it became Batchellor, the e in the last syllable bec
2 CONC oming o, by the peculiar way in which David wrote his name.
