1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Elizabeth Beauchamp
2 CONT * aka Beacham, Beachum, Bircham
2 CONT * Born 23 Jul 1648 in England or Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony  
2 CONT * Died 30 Jun 1715 at age 66 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony  
2 CONT * Daughter of Edward Beauchamp and Elizabeth 
2 CONT * Spouse: Zachariah Goodale - married 31 December  1666 in Salem.  ( "last of 10 m" in 1666 (modern style date 31 December 1666).  He was the son of Robert Goodale & Catherine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their 11 children were born at Salem: 
2 CONT * 1. Zechariah b. 9 Feb 1667 (Salem MA) m. 1691 Sarah WHIPPLE d. 1727 - 
2 CONT * 2. Samuel b. 3 Oct 1669 (Salem MA) m. 25 Dec 1697 Mary BUXTON (Salem MA) d. 1717 (Maine) - 
2 CONT * 3. Joseph b. 23 Sep 1672 (Salem MA) m. 6 Apr 1694 Mary HUTCHINSON (Salem MA) d. 1718 - 
2 CONT * 4. Mary b. 29 Sep 1674 (Salem MA) m. 24 Oct 1713 John WILKINS - 
2 CONT * 5. Thomas b. 30 Oct 1676 (Salem MA) m. 2 Dec 1698 Sarah HORRELL (Beverly MA) d. 22 Oct 1766 (Pomfret CT) - 
2 CONT * 6. Abraham b. 7 Sep 1678 (Salem MA) m. (1) Apr 1703 Hannah RHODES (Lynn MA) (2)23 Jun 1725 Mary TARBELL d. 1753/4 (Danvers MA) - 
2 CONT * 7. John b. 10 Aug 1681 (Salem MA) m. (1) 8 Sep 1703 Elizabeth WITT (b. 1676 in Marlboro MA dau of John WITT and Elizabeth BAKER) (2) Elizabeth d. 11 May 1752 (Marlboro MA) - 
2 CONT * 8. Elizabeth b. 23 Mar 1683 (Salem MA) m. 16 Oct 1714 William FULLER - 
2 CONT * 9. Sarah bap. 23 Mar 1689 (Salem MA) m. 10 May 1709 Samuel FELTON - 
2 CONT * 10. Benjamin b. 4 Jul 1687 (Salem MA) m. 21 May 1711 Hannah GARY (Pomfret CT) d. 1754 (Marlboro MA)
2 CONT * 11.  David b. 31 Mar 1689 (Salem MA) m. 7 Jan 1712 Abigail ELIOT d. 1717 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Beauchamp-72
2 CONT
2 CONT Roberts gives her name as Elizabeth Beacham, born 1648, married Zachariah Goodale in Salem, 1666. Ancestors of President William Howard Taft.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Beauchamp, born in 1648, was the daughter of Edward and Elizabeth Beauchamp..
2 CONT On 31 December 1666 in Salem, Massachusetts, Elizabeth married Zachariah Goodale.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other dates for their marriage have been found in Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints microfiche cards, including 30 Apr 1666 and October 1666. The multiple dates may include dates when banns or posted, or they may be due 
2 CONC to confusion regarding the interpretation of "last of 10 m."
2 CONT
2 CONT The court records of the year 1672 give, somewhat in detail, the tragi-comic history of an incident in the life of Elizabeth Beauchamp Goodale. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that John Smith, the husband of her sister-in-law, had for several years made somewhat crude and amorous advances toward her. In a too successful attempt to scandalize the gossips of the Village neighborhood, she told s
2 CONC everal women, who came purposely to ferret out the details of the affair, a highly colored version of Smith's conduct, and as a result she found herself the defendant in a suit for slander brought by Smith, and both of them were h
2 CONC aled before the magistrate for "uncivil carriages." Smith lost his suit and was sentenced to be whipped and to remain in gaol until the sentence should be carried out or pay a fine of forty shillings. The whipping was remitted, ho
2 CONC wever, and the incident closed with a confession by Elizabeth Goodale that she was "heartily sorry for her foolish words." . (See the account under John Smith for more details.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:LZGL-T1H
2 CONT
2 CONT …. Anderson makes the interesting point that the baptismal record we commonly use for Zachariah does not include a given name.  However, he points out that "with one exception, ages given in depositions coincide with this date (de
2 CONC posed on 18 July 1676 'aged about thirty years'...deposed 25 November 1679 'aged about forth years'...deposed on 26 March 1685 'aged about forth-five years.")  
2 CONT
2 CONT There is attached to this file under the Memories tab the original, handwritten ancient record of Zachariah's marriage to Elizabeth Beachum and listings for eight children - Zachariah, Samuel, Joseph, Mary, Thomas, Abraham, John, 
2 CONC and Benjamin, born 1687.  However, it is clear that he had at least one more son, David born in 1689, who inherited his father's estate in return for maintenance until his death.  Most secondary sources also include Sarah and Eliz
2 CONC abeth, who were baptized in 1690 but their father's first name was not listed - only "Brother."  Their christening records look like this: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, d. "Brother", bp. Mar. 23, 1690. CR2
2 CONT Elizabeth, d. "Brother", bp. Mar. 23, 1690. CR2
2 CONT
2 CONT However, a limited number of men with the last name of Goodale were living in the area at the time, and none of Zachariah's brothers appear to have been married and alive in 1690 in order to have had children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT So putting together these various sources together, we think Zachariah and his wife Elizabeth probably had 11 children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zachariah
2 CONT Samuel
2 CONT Joseph
2 CONT Mary
2 CONT Thomas
2 CONT Abraham
2 CONT John
2 CONT Benjamin 
2 CONT David 
2 CONT Sarah*
2 CONT Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Thomas moved to Connecticut early, before 1698 when he married.  It appears that the remainder of the family stayed closer to home.  It appears that all of his children (with perhaps the exception of Mary) lived to adulthood, 
2 CONC which was quite a feat for those days.  And eight of those 11 children were boys, who carried on the Goodale name.  David, Zachariah Junior, Joseph and Abraham all received land from their parents, and I have attached those deeds 
2 CONC under Sources.  I am assuming that Samuel, Thomas, John and Benjamin did as well, but that we don't have record of it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Written by Rachelle Child. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
