2 CONT WikiTree contributors, "Elizabeth (Smith) Sturtevant (bef.1662-1746)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Smith-2527 : accessed 21 August 2025).
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, daughter of John and Elizabeth (Goodell) Smith, was born at Salem, MA and baptized August 8, 1672. She married Humphrey Horrell, as his second wife, at Beverly, MA on January 10, 1687/88. They resided at Beverly where t
2 CONC hey had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey died at Beverly on February February 9, 1710 at the age of 60. She remained a widow until she married Samuel Sturtevant on August 12, 1715 removing to his home in Plympton, MA with her four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon Samuel Sturtevant died at Halifax, MA on April 21, 1736 at the age of 82. Although arrangements had been made for her to be able to continue to live in his house, she chose to move her church affiliations from Halifax back 
2 CONC to Plympton and reside with her unmarried son, Humphrey. She died there on August 6, 1746.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, daughter of John and Elizabeth (Goodell) Smith, was born at Salem, MA and baptized August 8, 1672. She married Humphrey Horrell, as his second wife, at Beverly, MA on January 10, 1687/88. They resided at Beverly where t
2 CONC hey had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey died at Beverly on February February 9, 1710 at the age of 60. She remained a widow until she married Samuel Sturtevant on August 12, 1715 removing to his home in Plympton, MA with her four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon Samuel Sturtevant died at Halifax, MA on April 21, 1736 at the age of 82. Although arrangements had been made for her to be able to continue to live in his house, she chose to move her church affiliations from Halifax back 
2 CONC to Plympton and reside with her unmarried son, Humphrey. She died there on August 6, 1746.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Plympton VR's have the death of Elizabeth notated as widow to "Moses, sister of Humphrey Horrel" in parenthesis. This is in error. All the parenthesized notations in Plympton VR's were made almost 100 years after the fact by Lewis
2 CONC  Bradford. If they are correct they can be a major help to family researchers. but, unfortunately, many are incorrect and can cause many hours to correct, or even worse, the continual dissemination of inaccurate information.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
