1 NAME James /Adams/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Adams
2 _MARNM Adams
1 NAME James Adams, of Scituate
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC At Sea
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 27 MAY 1627
2 PLAC Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 8 APR 1657
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==James Adams==
2 CONT *Birth:  before May 22 1627 / 17 DEC 1630 in Plymouth, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts 
2 CONT * Death: in Of, Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts 
2 CONT * Father: John Adams 
2 CONT * Mother: Eleanor Newton
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT # Frances Vassall b: 1623 in Stepheny, Middlesex, England Married: 15 JUL 1646 in Scituate, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # William Adams b: 16 MAY 1647 in Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT #  Anna Adams b: 18 APR 1649 in Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT #  Richard Adams b: 19 APR 1651 in Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT #  Mary Adams b: 27 JAN 1651/52 in Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT #  Margaret Adams b: 8 MAY 1654 in Marshfield, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT #  Martha Adams b: 1 APR 1658 in Of, Scituate, Plymouth Co. Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * no further record in Plymouth Colony after 1657; may have moved to the Mass Bay Colony
2 CONT * Ref; AFN: FZQ6-47
2 CONT * Ref: Signers of the Mayflower Compact, Adams, John & Bassett, William, Page 103
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://www.plimoth.org/media/pdf/adams_john.pdf A genealogical profile of John Adams]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FROM THE BOOK THE PLYMOUTH COLONY LET FREEDOM RING JAMES² ADAMS (John¹), "resided on a farm on the Marshfield side of North River, nearly opposite Mr. Vassall's, the father of Mrs Adams. They worshipped with the second church in S
2 CONC cituate, and their children were carried there for baptism." [1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Plymough Colony Records, under date of June 10, 1651, record that James Adams came before the goveror and acknowledged that he had received from Kenelm Winslow the £5 which was to be paid to him when he became of age, and "on 
2 CONC the 26th of December 1651, it was ordered to bee entered upon the publicke record as payed and received."[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Adam's widow, Frances, had 150 acres of land laid out to her by the Massachusetts General Court, May 7, 1673, "About eight miles northward from Lancaster."[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Kenelme Winslow and his stepson, James Adams [age 16 or older] appear in a list of those able to bear arms in the colony of New Plymouth in 1643. They are listed consecutively under the town of Marshfield See NEHG Register Vo
2 CONC l 4, July 1850, p. 259. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Adams and Frances Vassall: i. William, born May 16, 1647; bapt. by Mr. Witherell, May 23, 1647. ii. Anna, born April 18, 1649; bapt. May 20, 1649 iii. Richard, born April 19, 1651; bapt. April 27, 1651. iv. Mary,
2 CONC  born Jan 27, 1653; bapt. Feb 5, 1653. v. Margaret, (no record of birth), bapt. March 18, 1654.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT James was born in 1626. James was the child of John Adams and Eleanor Newton. James passed away in 1673. [5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Robert Charles Anderson, Great Migration Begins: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "i James, b before 22 May 1627; m. Scituate 15 or 16 June or 16 July 1646 Frances Vassall, daughter of WILLIAM VASSALL [ScVR 2:11; PCR 2:108; 8:19] 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Adams: "Who died at sea in the good ship called the James of London on the 19th of January, 1651, to which Captain John Allin was master, and chief commander of said vessel." His inventory amounted to £34.15. His step-father
2 CONC  Kenelm Winslow was administrator of his estate. [Ref] 
2 CONT --------------------
