1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Abbe Bement BIRTH	25 Jan 1715, Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	3 Aug 1788 (aged 73), Enfield, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA in the 73 year of her age BURIAL	Enfield Street Cemetery, Enfiel
2 CONC d, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA, MEMORIAL ID 26169353
2 CONT
2 CONT Photos added by Jack Jr
2 CONT
2 CONT wife of Capt. Dennis Bement [from "History of Enfield, CT," vol. III, by Francis Olcott Allen, c. 1900, page 2322]
2 CONT
2 CONT [From the book published in 1916 "Abbe -Abbey Genealogy In Memory of John Abbe and his Descendants"  by Cleveland Abbe and Joseph Genung Nichols
2 CONT
2 CONT MARY ABBE, daughter of Thomas and Mary (Pease) Abbe, born in Enfield, Conn., January 25, 1715-6; died there August 3, 1788.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married in Enfield, January 13, 1736-7, CAPTAIN DENNIS BEMENT, born in Enfield, 1711; died November 16, 1789, son of Edmond and Priscilla (Warner) Bement. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was 7th Captain of the Enfield militia; kept a public house there and held various town offices.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, born in Enfield
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - Mary Bement, b. July 19, 1739 ; married Richard Abbe, son of John and Hannah (Boardman) Abbe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 - Tryphena Bement, b. May 21, 1741; m. Jonathan Parsons. Children: i. Sarah, b. May 1, 1766 ; ii.  Walter, b. Jan. 4, 1771 ; iii. Dennis, b. Nov. 20, 1773, probably the Dennis Parsons who m. in  Enfield, April 20, 1796, Dorcas B
2 CONC ush. She d. Feb. 12, 1798, and had son, Bush, b. Jan. 25, 1798.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 - Dennis Bement, jr., b. Feb. 11, 174.3-4 ; m. Lydia .
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 - Prudence Bement, b. May 11. 1746; d. Aug. 30, 1831. Her will, made July 7, 1829, probated Sept. 6,  1831, mentions the following : Lydia, wife of Elisha Holton ; Elizabeth, wife Dr. Horatio A. Hamilton ;  widow Mary Olmstead ;
2 CONC  Piney, wife of Seth Alden ; Delight, wife of Roderick White ; Charlotte, wife of Richard Abbe, jr. ; widow Huldah Lord ; widow Tryphena Parsons.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 - Edmond Bement, b. Jan. 16, 1748-9. Settled in Enfield and d. there. His will, made July 21, 1798,  probated April 19, 1799, left property to the following : to his sisters. Prudence Bement ; Mary, wife  of Captain Richard Abbe
2 CONC  ; Tryphena, wife of Jonathan Parsons ; and to his brother, Dennis Bement.  He d. March 9, 1799, at Enfield.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents Thomas Abbe, 1686–1759 Mary Pease Abbe, 1688–1745
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	 Dennis Bement, 1711–1789
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings	 Sarah Abbe Parsons, 1718–1785	 Tabitha Abbe Pease, 1720–1787	 Hannah Abbe Phelps, 1723–1818 Abigail Abbey, 1725 – unknown Obadiah Abbe, 1728–1745 Thomas Abbey, 1731–1811
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	 Mary Bement Abbe, 1738–1821	 Dennis Bement, 1743–1820
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/26169353/mary-bement
