1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genforum.genealogy.com/pease/messages/2703.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.2.6.3.2 Cornelius A., son of David (Jonathan, John, Robert) and Elizabeth Pease; b. Apr 01, 1735 in Freehold, NJ; d. Jan 02, 1811 in Freehold; bur. in the Old Scot’s Burying Ground in Monmouth County with his wife; m. Jul 10, 17
2 CONC 58 in Freehold, Elizabeth Clark; b. about 1727 in Freehold; bpt. at Old Tennant Church; d. Feb 26, 1803 age 65 in Freehold. She was the daughter of Alexander Clark; b. 1693 in Monmouth County; d. Aug 07, 1730 in Freehold; bur. Top
2 CONC enamus Burial Ground, Freehold, and Sarah Everts Van Gelder Hendrickson; b. Mar 1690 in Brooklyn, NY; d. after 1730 in Freehold. Cornelius was a farmer who owned much land in Monmouth and Gloucester Counties, in NJ. He served with
2 CONC  two of his sons in the Monmouth County Militia during the Revolutionary War. In Jul 1784, Cornelius Pease was taxed in Deptford Township, Gloucester County for 400 acres of "unimproved land", which he paid the tax of 18 shillings
2 CONC  and 5 d. His will (No. 8916H) was filed Jan 03, 1811 in lower Freehold Township, Monmouth County, NJ. To his son, William, Cornelius bequeathed one dollar, to his daughter Margaret (Peggy), he gave a heifer, to daughter Sarah, a 
2 CONC tract of land in Middlesex County, and to daughter Elizabeth, a tract of land in Monmouth County. Pheobe received two tracts of land in Freehold on the road leading from Englishtown to Mt. Pleasant. Children of Cornelius A. and El
2 CONC izabeth (Clark) Pease born in Freehold, NJ:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.2.6.3.2.1 William        b. ca. 1758        d. ca.       1830 1.2.6.3.2.2 Sarah b. ca. 1765              d. 1.2.6.3.2.3 Elizabeth b. Nov       24, 1766       d. Jun       08,       1840       Freehold, NJ 1.2.6.3.2.4 Margaret   
2 CONC     b. ca. 1768              d. 1.2.6.3.2.5 Adam C.       b. Nov       15, 1768       d. Jul       19,1817       Cross Keys, NJ 1.2.6.3.2.6 Phoebe       b.        ca.       1769       d. 1.2.6.3.2.7 Jonathan C.       b. Nov       
2 CONC 28, 1773 d. Mar       12,       1840       Monmouth Co., NJ 1.2.6.3.2.8 David              b.               d. 1.2.6.3.2.9 John C.              b.               d. 1.2.6.3.2.10 Josiah        b.        d. Jun 20, 1842       Middles
2 CONC ex Co., NJ 1.2.6.3.2.11 Mary              b.               d.
2 CONT --------------------
