2 CONT In Find  a Grave George Phelps is of the Tewkesbury Phelps family, born 1605. He is married to the same women and have the same children?? http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=37604287
2 CONT
2 CONT Info:  https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-40001/familysearch-family-tree?itemId=348098502&action=showRecord
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS PARENTS ARE NOT KNOWN.  George Phelps was from county Dorset, England.  It has been proven that the Phelps' who immigrated were not of the Tewkesbury Phelps family. William Phelps of Crewkerne was not the son of William Phelps
2 CONC  of Tewkesbury.  DNA testing has also proven that William and George Phelps who arrived in America in 1630 were not brothers. This family in Tewkesbury (over to the east near London) was not even in the same area of Dorset and Som
2 CONC erset counties where the recruitment of the Colonists was actively happening.  There just happened to be a family named William Phelps in Tewkesbury at the correct time, with a son named William.  However, that William remained in
2 CONC  Tewkesbury and carried on business.  That family did not even have a son George in any records. (The author of "The Phelps Family of America" had not completed his investigations and correspondence with Tewkesbury when the book w
2 CONC as printed.)
2 CONT
2 CONT It was thought that George emigrated on the same ship, the Mary and John, as William, but it has become apparent that he may be the G___ Phelps on the Recovery in 1634.  He settled with William in Windsor, came from the same area,
2 CONC  so most likely they were related, but not brothers as DNA testing has shown.
2 CONT
2 CONT George and Phillury had six children:  Isaac, Abraham, and Joseph lived.  Abigail lived four years.  There was also a child who died in infancy, and a child who died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Phillury's death, George married her sister, Frances, who had been widowed of Mr. Clark, then Thomas Dewey.  George and Frances had three sons, Jacob, John, and Nathaniel.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
