3 NOTE Hi Lillian,
4 CONT Nice to meet you. 
4 CONT It doesn't bother me that the birth name is shown in brackets. It helps me to distinguish between birth and married names. It also help Geni in the search for matches on the name. They it different in other countries depending on 
4 CONC what name is used after marriage. Men can also have a different birth name, as are those that have been adopted. However it is a shame that women are not as easy to trace because of their name change. I use my maiden name as my mi
4 CONC ddle name. I remember my grandmother telling me years ago that you are suppose to use your maiden name as your middle name after marriage. (She told me this after I had already chosen to do this.) I'm not sure what percentage of p
4 CONC eople do this, but it does help in the search.
3 NOTE It`s a pitty (in my opinion) most users show women's surnames between brackets in family trees or they just avoid them as if they were just unidentified objects - or as if they had lost their actual names for the sake of getting m
4 CONC arried - that naming system leads us to unnecessary repetition of surnames, to prevent us from getting an easier reading of family trees and many times to lose tracks of women's names-
4 CONT Lilian
