1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Miller-102589
2 CONT
2 CONT Obadiah Miller Jr was born in Springfield, Massachusetts 26 Jan 1658, and died there 25 Aug 1731. On 15 Jun 1683 in Springfield he married Benedicta Lawton (1666-1719). Together they had at least 7 children, as follows. All but th
2 CONC e second Sarah were recorded in Springfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah b. 6 Oct 1684, d. 24 Nov 1684, an infant.
2 CONT # Steward b. 2 Jan 1686, d. 3 Jan 1704 age 18 in Springfield, unmarried.
2 CONT # Mary b. 2 Feb 1688, d. 22 Mar 1760 age 72 in Enfield, Connecticut, m. Thomas Hale.
2 CONT # John b. 29 Jan 1690, d. 27 Feb 1766 age 76 in Springfield, m. Mary Matoon and Priscilla Hale.
2 CONT # Hannah b. 8 Oct 1699, d. about 1790 age 91 in Suffield, Connecticut, m. Nathaniel Harmon.
2 CONT # Sarah b. about 1703, d. 23 Mar 1756 age 53 in Suffield, Connecticut, m. John Marshall.
2 CONT # Obadiah III b. 21 May 1706, d. after 1732, m. Mary Perkins
2 CONT .
2 CONT See the profile of Sarah (Miller) Marshall (abt.1703-1756) for the reasons she may have been born in Suffield at about the time indicated. It can't be ruled out that there were additional births in Suffield, where the vital record
2 CONC s are damaged.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following Benedicta's death, Obadiah married Dorothy Root, the widow of Japhet Chapin, in Springfield on 18 Mar 1720. There were no additional children from that marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obadiah purchased 20 acres from his brother Lazarus in Suffield in 1684, It is unclear whether he ever lived there, as he had children recorded in Springfield from 1684 to 1706. In 1726 he was granted additional Suffield land, sug
2 CONC gesting that he was using it. He and Benedicta may have divided their time between their Springfield and Suffield properties, which were about 10 miles apart. That would help explain their daughters' marriage to Suffield gentlemen
2 CONC . There is no evidence in the Suffield or Springfield histories that Obadiah Jr was ever involved in civic or church affairs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
