1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Agreeable to order from the Hon. Court of Probate for the district of Windham, appointing the subscribers to divide and set out such real estate of Mr Moses Phelps late of Mansfield dec'd, to the children and heirs
2 CONC  of his son Joel Phelps dec'd being seven in number, viz. Apama, Ezra, Ira, Sally, Lillie, Chester, and Esther, in equal parts, consisting of one farm ....[3] This implies that Joel pre-deceased his father, Moses, and that Moses h
2 CONC ad died before 23 Feb 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Phelps-6229
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Phelps was born on 6 March 1722 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut to Joseph Phelps and Sarah Curtis. He is the  brother of Joseph Phelps, Eunice Phelps, Eunice Phelps and	Nathaniel Phelps. Moses married Sarah (Meacham) Phe
2 CONC lps —on 29 May 1745 in Windham, Connecticut. He is the father of Joel Phelps. Moses died before 23 Oct 1802 in Connecticut, United States [uncertain].
2 CONT
2 CONT The probate records for Moses Phelps, dated 23 Feb 1802, start as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agreeable to order from the Hon. Court of Probate for the district of Windham, appointing the subscribers to divide and set out such real estate of Mr Moses Phelps late of Mansfield dec'd, to the children and heirs of his son Joel
2 CONC  Phelps dec'd being seven in number, viz. Apama, Ezra, Ira, Sally, Lillie, Chester, and Esther, in equal parts, consisting of one farm ....[3] This implies that Joel pre-deceased his father, Moses, and that Moses had died before 2
2 CONC 3 Feb 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
