1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A090216  DAR Ancestor # A090216]
2 CONT
2 CONT Silas Phelps married Hannah Dewey on 23 Dec 1742 in Lebanon, New London, CT with issues: Joseph Phelps b. 27 May 1758, and Elphalet I Phelps b. 5 Nov 1743 in Lebanon, New London, CT.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 	Nov 17 1720 - Lebanon, New London, Connecticut, United States Death:	Dec 23 1816 - Rome, Oneida, New York, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Phelps, Elizabeth Phelps, Abigail Phelps, Abiel Phelps, Jacob Phelps, Dorothy Phelps, Abigail Phelps, Paul Phelps, Benjamin Phelps, Anna Phelps, Jeremiah Phelps, Lucy Phelps, Jedediah Phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Lilian,
2 CONT    Thanks for getting in touch.  My wife, Susan is the great-great granddaughter of the union of Sarah Sophia Phelps (1823-1861) and Isaac Hall (1815-1867).  I'm attaching photos of Sarah and Isaac.
2 CONT    Sarah was the daughter of Asa Hosmer Phelps (1795-1835).
2 CONT    Asa was the son of Eliphalet Phelps (1765-1842).
2 CONT    Eliphalet was the son of Eliphalet Phelps (1743-1773)
2 CONT    Eliphalet was the son of Silas Phelps (1720-1816) and he was George Phelps great grandson.
2 CONT    The patriarch of all US Phelps is William Phelps.  He had three sons, William, George and Richard.  Richard, after spending a very short period in the Massachusetts Bay Colony, took off for the Caribbean and disappeared.  There
2 CONC  is a published book on the Phelps family, and Sue has a connection through both George and his older brother William Phelps (1599-1672).
2 CONT    We have been able to trace Sue's maternal and paternal lines pretty much back to Massachusetts and then England.  We have traced her mother's paternal line (Seaver) to Roxbury, Massachusetts, and have photos of headstones in th
2 CONC e 4th oldest cemetery in Boston.  What was fun was to trace the Seaver line from Roxbury to Phillipston, Massachusetts, then up to Cavendish, Vermont, and finally to Woodstock, Vermont, where her mom grew up.  Her father's family 
2 CONC settled Fairfield, Vermont, after leaving Fairfield, Connecticut, so she is pretty much a native Vermonter.
2 CONT    My family, on the other hand is more difficult.  Three of my four grandparents are Swedish.  I've found some links, and hope to travel  to Sweden in October for sightseeing and checking out home towns.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Sue and I live in Vermont, have 3 children, and 3 grandchildren.  Both retired.  Sue spent her career in banking, and I spent my career as a fighter pilot with the Air National Guard in Burlington, Vermont.  I have more picture
2 CONC s if you want of Sophia's son and his wife, and Sue's grandparents.  Could send pictures of us if that is something you're interested in. Best, John Richard "Dick" Strifert
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/150355713/silas-phelps
2 CONT
