1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SAMUEL BEMENT was one of sixteen charter members of St. John's Lodge, Free and Accepted Masons when it was formed in Middletown, Connecticut on 26 Feb 1763 in the tavern of Captain Michael Burnham. The tavern was s
2 CONC till standing on Washington Street, below Main and was occupied as a residence about 1915. (Source: Bement Chronicles in America; 1928, pp. 77-79) 
