0 @N6000000006165964301@ NOTE Benjamin PARSONS, married Sarah, daughter of Richard VORE of Windsor. He was a brother of Cornet Joseph PARSONS, who married Mary BLISS. In Pynchon's account book, page 250, in an account with Joseph is this: "The wheat your broth
1 CONC er Benjamin delivered to me." Some of the dependents of Joseph have stated that he is not a brother of Benjamin. Benjamin was prominent in church and town affairs, was for many years a Deacon and a Selectman, and evidently was hig
1 CONC hly esteemed for character and ability. His wife died January 1, 1676, and he married, second, Sarah LEONARD, widow of John, who was killed by the Indians, February 24, 1676. He died August 24, 1689, and his widow married Peter TI
1 CONC LTON of Hadley, November 3, 1690. The children by his first wife were:--
1 CONT
1 CONT        Sarah, b. August 13, 1656, m. James DORCHESTER.
1 CONT        Benjamin, b. September 15, 1658, m. Sarah KEEP.
1 CONT        Mary, b. December 10, 1660, d. January 27, 1652.
1 CONT        Abigail, b. January 6, 1662, m. John MUNN, and second, John RICHARDS.
1 CONT        Samuel, b. October 10, 1660, m. Hannah HITCHCOCK.
1 CONT        Ebenezer, b. November 17, 1668, m. Margaret MARSHFIELD.
1 CONT        Mary, b. December 17, 1670, m. Thomas RICHARDS.
1 CONT        Hezekiah, b. November 24, 1673, m. Hannah COOLEY.
1 CONT        Joseph, b. December ___, 1675, m. Abigail PHELPS.
