1 CONT
1 CONT Daniel was the first in his family to settle in Spartanburg Co., S.C. in 1786.  
1 CONT He was born in Baltimore County, Maryland (now Harford County).  He moved from Baltimore Co., Maryland to Bedfor County, Virginia in the early 1750's along with a group of his brothers and cousins.  He served as a Sergeant in the 
1 CONC Bedford County Militia in 1758 in the French and Indian War and on Nov. 22, 1779 was appointed a Second Lieutenant in the Bedford County Military in the Revolutionary War.
1 CONT After the Revolution Daniel Gilbert moved to Spartanburg Co., SC in 1786 where he lived until his death about 1810.  He along with three of his sons were listed as Charter members in the reconstitution of the Boiling Springs Bapti
1 CONC st Church in Spartanburg Co., S.C.
