0 @N6000000001958957865@ NOTE David came to America as a part of the Reverend Davenport and business man Theophilus Eaton party.  They had both religious and business motives.  They wanted freedom to follow their Puritan values and take advantage of the new wo
1 CONC rld's riches.  The were not able to obtain royal approval.  The got a group together, concealed their identities and chartered the ship the Hector. Because they traveled under assumed identities, there is no known passenger list. 
1 CONC  Approx. 250 people set sail (fifty heads of family)  This group included the largest group of wealthy men ever to venture to New England.
1 CONT
1 CONT David Atwater and his brother were one of seven founders who set out from the Masschusetts Bay Colony after the arrival of the Hector on 6 June 1637.  There is a plaque in the town center pointing out this encampment. They camped 
1 CONC at the New Haven site for the first summer, saving the spot as it were.  There area was called "Quinnipiack" and was a verdant and fertile meadow area.
