0 @N6000000001959587934@ NOTE Deacon Jonathan , son of Moses and Mercy (Glover) Mansfield , was born February 16, 1686, baptized March 21, same year, and died January 10, 1775.  His name appears on the land records in fifty-six deeds, and in the court and town
1 CONC  records, thirty-nine times. He was an enterprising and active business man, and was appointed a member of important and responsible public trusts. In farming he was equally successful. His will, dated October 1, 1767, left an est
1 CONC ate of £1,493, which was considered large for that time. He joined the church under the Rev. James Pierpont, August 28, 1709.
