0 @N6000000006348486552@ NOTE From a correspondent:
1 CONT .
1 CONT
1 CONT Patrick Jr.
1 CONT In 1697 he was married to his "first wife" and had a son. The son seems to be
1 CONT dead by 1728 when Patrick made his will and mentions only grandson Gregor and
1 CONT Mary's family.
1 CONT In 1724 he gave land to David Southerland and his daughter Mary. This is
1 CONT probably around the time of their marriage. So I estimate Mary was born c
1 CONT 1704 and David perhaps a few years earlier.
1 CONT In 1728 in the will, David and Mary had sons Patrick and David. The
1 CONT birthdates for these two are usually given as much later. I don't know where
1 CONT these dates come from. If they are correct, the two boys must have died young
1 CONT and two others given the same names. This is certainly possible since David
1 CONT Jr. married Hannah McDonnell who was born in 1745.
