0 @N6000000002441667300@ NOTE [Scott090406.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT He was one of those “Yankees” who went to the Wyoming Valley and settled on its fertile lands, prior to the Revolutionary war. Being a mill-wright by trade, he built a mill, the site of which is now occupied by another. It too is 
1 CONC over eighty years old and fast going into decay. He married and had four children, one of whom, 
1 CONT Thomas, was a lieutenant in the little band that went forth to meet Butler and his Indians, above
1 CONT Forty Fort, and were slain on July 3, 1778, less than a score escaping. Thomas Williams, Sr., although not in the battle, was slain in the horrible massacre that followed the fight and which has come down in history to be known as
1 CONC  the Wyoming Massacre. Mrs. Williams and her three small children became much alarmed some days before the fight and started over the mountains from Wilkes Barre 
1 CONT to go to her former home in Connecticut.
0 @N6000000001959310383@ NOTE HUDSON AND MOHAWK VALLEYS book, Came to New Haven in 1663. After his marriage he settled in Wallingford, April 1670, with the first planters. He was the first shoemaker and tanner in the town. He held many offices of trust in the 
1 CONC town and church. He died March 1702, leaving as estate of three hundred and forty pounds. There is information in GEN. DICT OF NEW ENGLAND SETTLERS VOL 1.
1 CONT "Samuel, New Haven, m. 2 May 1667, Hope, d. of Edward Parker, had Samuel, b 3 Mar 1668; John, 3 Dec 1669; and a d. without name. rem to Wallingford 1673, where the residue of his ch. nam. in his will twelve in all, were b. Mary Iv
1 CONC es, Judith, Isaac, Joseph, Hope, Isreal, Mabel, Benjamin, Ephraim, and Eliz. A sec. W. Mary, he had, but we kn. not, wh. of these ch. if any, were hers. He made his will Mar. 1703 and soon d." The Family Cook/Cooke says born 30 Ju
1 CONC ly 1641 Salem MA died 25 Dec 1703. Information in" COLONIAL FAMILES OF AMERICA" Vol 12, pag 104-107 and THE POINEER OF MASS by Charles Henry Pope, Gen Pub Co., 1981, page 115 May have died Dec 25, 1703 Wallingford New Haven, CT
