1 CONT Excerpt from the Genealogical Register of the First Settlers of New-England.
1 CONT ==============================================================================
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac Cummings, likely one of the first and surely the one with the most complete lineage, first appeared in Salem, Mass. in 1636.
1 CONT
1 CONT He arrived at Salem and went to Watertown, Mass. in 1636 where he recieved a grant of 35 acres of land that year.  He also was a land owner at Ipswich, Mass., July 1638 and owned a house lot in Ispwich in Feb. 1639.  In the same y
1 CONC ear, he possessed a farm, partly in Ispwich and partly in Topfield and was admitted freeman, May 18, 1642.  He purchased a farm of 150 acres, Feb. 1, 1652 in Topsfield from Samual Symonds and spent the remainder of his life there,
1 CONC  being a deacon of the church for many years.  He also held numerous town offices.  His surname was given as Comin in his last will and testament; it made no mention of his wife's given name.  He died shortly before May 22, 1677, 
1 CONC the date of the inventory of his estate.  
1 CONT
1 CONT Excerpt from Our Isaac Cummings (Cummins) Family, Paternal Ancestors of Paul O. Seekins.
1 CONT =============================================================================
1 CONT
