1 CONT Connections to England
1 CONT
1 CONT "Immigrants to New England in the 1630s, such as Isaac Cummings, nearly all came from England.  Moreover, Isaac's fellow settlers of Watertown& Ipswich, Massachusetts came predominantly from Suffolk and Essex. A search of the Fami
1 CONC ly History Library's International Genealogical Indexes for those two counties brings to light (FHL microfilm #560,909) an Isaack COMMEN who had children exactly matching those of the immigrant. He was of Mistley, Essex, with is r
1 CONC ight on the Suffolk border.  Also of Mistley was Henry Kimball who came on the Elizabeth in 1634 and lived in Watertown, MA.
1 CONT
1 CONT It seems clear that Isaack COMMEN of Mistley was the immigrant. He disappears from the records there just before appearing in Watertown, MA, where he settled among great numbers of his fellow countrymen, even townsmen.  His three 
1 CONC children baptized in Mistley exactly match American records.  The spelling COMMEN is in line with the American variations.. .
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac must fit in somehow with the CUMMINGS family of Essex and Suffolk. No others are found in Mistley, however.  There was Stephen COMYNG of Essex in 1273 (Charles Wareing Bardsley, 'A Dictionary of English and Welsh Surnames', 
1 CONC Baltimore, 1967, p 198) when Isaac Cummings' claimed ancestors were still in Scotland. . .
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac CUMMINGS was born in 1600/1601, according to a deposition dated27 March 1666 (Essex Court Files, 2:90) or in 1602/3 per a deposition of25 March 1675.  He died at Topsfield, Massachusetts, between 8 and22 May 1677 (from proba
1 CONC te records).  He married ANNE (last name unkown), probably in Essex or Suffolk, England by 1628, as his first known child was baptized at Mistley in early 1629".  The first four children are recorded in Mistley (FHL microfilm #560
1 CONC ,909, item 2); surname CUMMINGS ".
1 CONT
1 CONT WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWw
1 CONT Isaac's Parents
1 CONT By David Butler Cummings
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac Cummings was baptized 5 April 1601 at Easthorpe, Essex, England, the son of John and Amy (Green) Cummings.  This is a major conclusion of the research detailed below.
1 CONT
1 CONT In June I posted a retraction of false information on the Cummings family in Copford, Essex, England that had been supplied by an English genealogist.  At that time I stated that Mrs. Jane Bedford, of the Colchester Branch of the 
1 CONC Essex County Records Office, had found the correct baptismal records for Isaac and his siblings.  These were in the parish of Easthorpe, Essex,  which is contiguous to Copford on the southwest.  My wife and I agreed with her trans
1 CONC cription of the original record under ultra violet light.  Those records have also been transcribed by Peter C. Nutt, of Wickford, Essex, England, Genealogist and Record Researcher, who has worked with Abbott Lowell Cummings.  The
1 CONC  results fit well with other research done by Abbott Lowell Cummings and Peter C. Nutt, and John Plummer.  The material in this posting was presented at the Isaac Cummings Family Association reunion on August 14 in Gloucester, Mas
1 CONC sachusetts.
1 CONT
1 CONT Easthorpe Parish Register, Original in Essex Record Office, Colchester, D/P386/1/1
1 CONT Salt Lake Family History Library Microfilm 0853320
1 CONT
1 CONT Baptisms
1 CONT Ao 1595 Junii 17 John Commin soon of John Commin & his wife bapt
1 CONT Ao 1597 Maii 8 Ursely Commin daught[er] of Goodman Commin bapt
1 CONT 1599 November 11 Abraham Commin the sonne of Jhon Comin & his wyf baptised
1 CONT Anno 1601 Apr 5 Izahk Comin the sonne of Jhon Commin baptised anno ut sup___
1 CONT [remainder of word unclear; probably either supradicto or suprascripto meaning "the year as
1 CONT above said or above written"]
1 CONT
1 CONT Copford Parish Register, Original in Essex Record Office, Colchester, D/P186/1/1
1 CONT Salt Lake Family History Library Microfilm 1472221
1 CONT
1 CONT Baptisms
1 CONT 1605 Mary Comming the daughter of John Comming was babtized the x day of November
1 CONT 1608 John Commin sonn of John Commin babtized the xxv of March
1 CONT An Dm 1619  [Blank] the Daughter of John Comyns and of [Blank] his wife was baptised the 28th of Ffebruarie 1619[/1620]
1 CONT
1 CONT Burials
1 CONT 1608[/1609] A maid servant of John Commins 10 January
1 CONT 1610 John Commyn buryed 3 children 1 Novemb.1.2.3
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTE: Entries above and below this have the day after the month but prior entries have the day first.  A mark like a 1 before Novemb may be the day. The meaning of .1.2.3 is not clear. Suggestions are 1) triplets, 2) the first thr
1 CONC ee of their children, or 3) they are buried on top of each other.  We do not know which children were buried.  There are gaps in the birth sequence in which 3 or 4 children could have been born.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1612 The wife of John Comens Noveb 3
1 CONT
1 CONT This is presumably Amy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages
1 CONT
1 CONT There is no specific date, but the following entry appears between 1 Sep 1590 and 26 Feb 1593/1594. In the IGI it is given as 1591.
1 CONT
1 CONT Matrimony was solemnised the [Blank] Daie of [Blank] Between [Blank] Commins and Amy Greene Daughter of John Grene of much-birch. [also known as Great Birch]
1 CONT
1 CONT     *
1 CONT
1 CONT       Considering: 1) the proximity of Copford and Easthorpe, 2) no other marriage for John has been found, 3) the children of John began after this marriage, and 4) John owned land in Copford (see below), this is probably the mar
1 CONC riage of John Commin, the father of children in both parishe
1 CONT
1 CONT Land Survey
1 CONT
1 CONT The following document was also found by Jane Bedford showing John was a landowner in Copford in the third year of the reign of King James I [1606] which is consistent with his marriage and children born there.
1 CONT
1 CONT Uncatalogued survey of the manor of Copford 13 January 3 James I [1606], Essex Records Office accession C891 [will be catalogued as part of D/DV 161/ ]
1 CONT
1 CONT John Cumyne claims to hold by virtue of the surrender by Robert Noothe and Marger[y] his wifeand Thurston Noothe, one tenement and one virgate of heriotable [land] containing XXX ta [?30] acres called from ancient times Goreland a
1 CONC lias Hedghouse and now Fullers and one croft containing five [?] acres of land called Hedgland, parcel of Hedgeland tenement.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT The information above leads to the following family group:
1 CONT
1 CONT John Commin
1 CONT
1 CONT John Commin, born about 1565, of Copford and Easthorpe.
1 CONT
1 CONT His father might possibly be Johannes (John) Cowman, baptized 23 Jul 1561 at Bocking, Essex, found in the IGI and confirmed in the Bocking parish register, SLFHL Film 1471886, Extracted SLFHL Film 0472340.  Bocking is about eleven
1 CONC  miles from Copford whereas Mistley, where Isaac's first four children were born, is about thirteen miles from Copford.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married 1590/1594 at Copford.
1 CONT
1 CONT Amy Greene, born about 1569, daughter of John Greene of Much (Great) Birch.  Died 3 Nov 1612 at Copford.
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. John1 Commin, baptized 17 Jun 1595 at Easthorpe (Probably John of Tolleshunt D'Arcy, Essex)
1 CONT    2. Ursely Commin, baptized 8 May 1597 at Easthorpe
1 CONT    3. Abraham Commin, baptized 11 Nov 1599 at Easthorpe (Probably Abraham of Woolverstone, Suffolk)
1 CONT    4. Izahk Com[m]in, baptized 5 Apr 1601 at Easthorpe
1 CONT    5. Mary Comming, baptized 10 Nov 1605 at Copford
1 CONT    6. John2 Commin, baptized 25 Mar 1608 at Copford
1 CONT    7. (?) [Blank] Comyns, baptized 28 Feb 1619/1620 at Copford.  (This could be a child that might have caused Amy's death in 1612 and was not baptized until later, or it could be the daughter of a another wife, or the daughter of
1 CONC  a different John Comyns)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac Cummings served as constable in Topsfield, Massachusetts, and as such gave depositions in 1666 and 1673 in which his age would yield a birth in 1600/1601.  This fits precisely with the birth of Izahk above.
1 CONT
1 CONT The following data come from an article by Abbott Lowell Cummings in The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Vol 163, January 1999, especially pages 64 through 66.  A court record in 1631 in Mistley recorded the thef
1 CONC t of goats belonging to Isaac Cummyn and Abr. Cummyn, in a "cote" or pen.  Their having livestock in the same pen would suggest a relationship between Isaac and Abraham.  In addition, he quotes from the will of Abraham Comin, yeom
1 CONC an, then of Much Tey, Essex, dated 10 January 1656.  In it he named his son John Comyns executor, and a brother, John Comyn of "Tolson Darcey" in Essex, as one of the "supervisors."  From the dates of their first children below, t
1 CONC he ages of John, Abraham, and Isaac would be in the order of the baptisms above.  In addition, all three names were given to children of Abraham.  John had only one son, John.  Isaac named his sons Isaac and John.  All three appea
1 CONC r in the family of Isaac's son John.  Although the proof is not positive, these three appear to be sons of John and Amy.
1 CONT
1 CONT John Commin
1 CONT
1 CONT Using the data of Abbott Lowell Cummings the family of John of Tolleshunt D'Arcy can be assembled as follows using the Easthorpe baptism for the first John and estimated dates for Rebecca and their marriage.  The children were all
1 CONC  baptized at Tolleshunt D'Arcy.
1 CONT
1 CONT NOTE: Although it is not common, sometimes there were two or more living children of the same Christian name, especially when the name was John.  Peter C. Nutt cited an example of a family with three Johns that were called "Young 
1 CONC John," Middle John," and "Old John." Therefore, though more common, having two sons named John does not necessarily mean that the first John died and the name was used again. This is important because the second John would have be
1 CONC en too young to have been John of Tolleshunt D'Arcy.
1 CONT
1 CONT John1 Comyn, baptized 17 Jun 1595 at Easthorpe, about 7 miles from Tolleshunt D'Arcy.  Married about 1624.
1 CONT Rebecca, born about 1600
